(window.UPANISHAD_DATA=window.UPANISHAD_DATA||{})["yogakundalini"]={"slug":"yogakundalini","name":"Yogakuṇḍalī","deva":"योगकुण्डली","note":"","intro":[],"sections":[{"t":"Introduction","u":[{"ref":"Yoga Kundalini Upanishad","title":"","sa":["योगकुण्डलिन्युपनिषत्"],"words":[],"lit":"Krishna Yajurveda • 86th of the 108 Upaniṣads • 20th of the 20 Yoga-Upaniṣads","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Verse-by-verse Sanskrit (Devanāgarī + IAST + ITRANS) with English translation, word-by-word glossing, visual representations, practical observations, and comparative notes from the principal commentaries."]}]},{"t":"","u":[{"ref":"Sources & method","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Sanskrit text: sanskritdocuments.org (ITRANS encoding by Sunder Hattangadi; proofread with PSA Easwaran, last updated 2017-12-09). Devanagari and IAST were generated programmatically with indic_transliteration (sanscript) from that single canonical ITRANS source — so spelling, sandhi joins and verse numbering match the Sunder Hattangadi edition exactly.","English translation: K. Nārāyaṇasvāmī Aiyar, Thirty Minor Upanishads (1914) — public domain. Aiyar's translation is itself shaped by Śrī Upaniṣad-Brahma-Yogin's Sanskrit commentary (Adyar tradition), so a single column already mediates two of the five commentaries listed below.","Word-by-word glosses are mechanical: a lexicon of ~500 high-frequency Sanskrit stems and particles is consulted directly, then common case-suffixes are stripped, then sandhi-encliticised particles (cha, tu, eva, api, hi) are split off. Tokens with no confident match are marked [?] — that is an honest signal, not laziness. Sanskrit compound words (samāsa) genuinely need scholar-level pada-cheda to be split with authority; this document does not pretend to that, and is therefore best used alongside a Sanskrit dictionary (Apte / Monier-Williams) when reading verses that contain dense compounds.","Practical observations are distilled from the cited commentary tradition — they should not be acted on without instruction from a qualified teacher. The text itself (II.13–14, II.40–41) repeatedly insists that several of these practices, especially Khecharī-mudrā and forced kuṇḍalinī-rousing, are dangerous without a living guru."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Top five commentaries consulted","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["1. Śrī Upaniṣad-Brahma-Yogin (early 18th c., Kāñcī). The traditional Sanskrit auto-commentary on all 108 Upaniṣads. For the Yoga-Upaniṣads this is the basis of the Adyar Library edition (1938, ed. Mahādeva Śāstri). Quoted where Aiyar's English glosses reflect Brahma-Yogin's reading directly.","2. K. Nārāyaṇasvāmī Aiyar (1914). Thirty Minor Upanishads, English translation. The most widely available English rendering of the text; serves here as the primary verse-paired translation.","3. T.R. Śrīnivāsa Ayyaṅgār &amp; S. Subrahmaṇya Śāstrī (Adyar Library, 1938). The Yoga Upaniṣads — full English translation built directly on Brahma-Yogin's commentary. Cross-referenced where it differs from Aiyar.","4. Swāmī Satyānanda Sarasvatī / Swāmī Satyadharma Sarasvatī (Bihar School). Yoga Kundalini Upanishad: Theory and Practices for Awakening Kundalini (2019). A modern practical commentary from the Satyananda lineage; paraphrased only — the work is in copyright.","5. Paṇḍit Rājmaṇi Tigunait (Himalayan Institute). Tantra Unveiled and lectures on the Yoga-Kuṇḍalinī material from the Himalayan tradition; paraphrased."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Śānti-mantra (Invocation)","title":"","sa":["ॐ सह नाववतु । सह नौ भुनक्तु । सह वीर्यं करवावहै ।","तेजस्विनावधीतमस्तु मा विद्विषावहै ।","ॐ शान्तिः शान्तिः शान्तिः ॥"],"iast":["Oṃ saha nāvavatu | saha nau bhunaktu | saha vīryaṃ karavāvahai |","tejasvināv adhītam astu mā vidviṣāvahai |","Oṃ śāntiḥ śāntiḥ śāntiḥ ||"],"words":[],"lit":"Om! May the Lord protect us both [teacher and student]; may He nourish us both; may we work conjointly with great energy; may our study be vigorous and effective; may we not mutually dispute. Om! Peace, Peace, Peace.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["(Standard Śānti-mantra of the Kṛṣṇa-Yajur-Veda; Aiyar 1914)"]}]},{"t":"Chapter I — Saraswatī-Cālana and Prāṇāyāma","u":[{"ref":"Chapter I","title":"Saraswatī-Cālana and Prāṇāyāma","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["86 verses","Chapter I establishes the foundation. It opens by naming the two causes of the mind — vāsanā (latent impressions) and prāṇa (vital breath) — and argues that subduing one subdues the other (1–2). It then specifies the means: moderate diet, two postures (Padmāsana, Vajrāsana) and Śakti-cālana — literally 'stirring of the Śakti', i.e. Kuṇḍalinī (3–7). The technique of Śakti-cālana is decomposed into Sarasvatī-cālana — physically agitating the Sarasvatī-nāḍī — and prāṇa-rodha, breath-restraint (8–18). The text then details four kumbhakas (Sūrya-bheda, Ujjāyī, Śītalī, Bhastrikā — 19–39), the three bandhas (Mūla, Uḍḍīyāna, Jālandhara — 40–53), the daily progression (54–55), the ten obstacles (56–61), and finally the full path of Kuṇḍalinī's piercing of the three granthis (Brahma-, Viṣṇu-, Rudra-) up to her union with Śiva in Sahasrāra (62–86)."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Visual representation","title":"the three nāḍīs and six cakras","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["<pre>\n        SAHASRĀRA  (1000-petal lotus, abode of Śiva)\n              ✦\n              │\n        ─── ĀJÑĀ ───   ← between eyebrows (Rudra-granthi)\n              │\n        ─ VIŚUDDHA ─   ← throat\n              │\n        ─ ANĀHATA ──   ← heart (Viṣṇu-granthi)\n              │\n        ─ MAṆIPŪRA ─   ← navel\n              │\n        SVĀDHIṢṬHĀNA   ← genital region\n              │\n        ─ MŪLĀDHĀRA ─  ← perineum (Brahma-granthi)\n              ◯\n        Kuṇḍalinī coiled 3½ times\n\n   ┌──────┬──────┬──────┐\n   │ IḌĀ  │SUṢUMNĀ│ PIṄGALA │\n   │(L)   │(centre) │ (R)   │\n   │cool  │ fire    │ hot   │\n   │lunar │ Brahma- │ solar │\n   │      │ nāḍī    │       │\n   └──────┴──────┴──────┘</pre>"],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"1.1","title":"","sa":["हेतुद्वयं हि चित्तस्य वासना च समीरणः । तयोर्विनष्ट एकस्मिंस्तद्द्वावपि विनश्यतः"],"iast":["hetudvayaṃ hi cittasya vāsanā ca samīraṇaḥ | tayorvinaṣṭa ekasmiṃstaddvāvapi vinaśyataḥ"],"words":[["hetudvayaṃ","हेतुद्वयं","the two causes"],["hi","हि","for / indeed"],["cittasya","चित्तस्य","of citta"],["vāsanā","वासना","latent impression / vāsanā"],["ca","च","and"],["samīraṇaḥ","समीरणः","the wind (nom.)"],["tayorvinaṣṭa","तयोर्विनष्ट","[?]"],["ekasmiṃstaddvāvapi","एकस्मिंस्तद्द्वावपि","[?]"],["vinaśyataḥ","विनश्यतः","the two perish"]],"lit":"Chitta has two causes, Vasanas and (Prana) Vayu. If one of them is controlled, then both are controlled.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.2","title":"","sa":["तयोरादौ समीरस्य जयं कुर्यान्नरः सदा । मिताहारश्चासनं च शक्तिश्चालस्तृतीयकः"],"iast":["tayorādau samīrasya jayaṃ kuryānnaraḥ sadā | mitāhāraścāsanaṃ ca śaktiścālastṛtīyakaḥ"],"words":[["tayorādau","तयोरादौ","first of those two"],["samīrasya","समीरस्य","of the wind (gen.)"],["jayaṃ","जयं","[?]"],["kuryānnaraḥ","कुर्यान्नरः","a man should do"],["sadā","सदा","always"],["mitāhāraścāsanaṃ","मिताहारश्चासनं","moderate food and posture"],["ca","च","and"],["śaktiścālastṛtīyakaḥ","शक्तिश्चालस्तृतीयकः","[?]"]],"lit":"Of these two, a person should control (Prana) Vayu always through moderate food, postures and thirdly Sakti-Chala.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.3 (Aiyar §3-4)","title":"","sa":["एतेषां लक्षणं वक्ष्ये शृणु गौतम सादरम् । सुस्निग्धमधुराहारश्चतुर्थांशविवर्जितः"],"iast":["eteṣāṃ lakṣaṇaṃ vakṣye śṛṇu gautama sādaram | susnigdhamadhurāhāraścaturthāṃśavivarjitaḥ"],"words":[["eteṣāṃ","एतेषां","of these (pl.)"],["lakṣaṇaṃ","लक्षणं","characteristic (acc.)"],["vakṣye","वक्ष्ये","I shall speak"],["śṛṇu","शृणु","listen!"],["gautama","गौतम","[?]"],["sādaram","सादरम्","[?]"],["susnigdhamadhurāhāraścaturthāṃśavivarjitaḥ","सुस्निग्धमधुराहारश्चतुर्थांशविवर्जितः","smooth-sweet food leaving a fourth empty"]],"lit":"1 shall explain the nature of these. Listen to it, O Gautama. One should take a sweet and nutritious food, leaving a fourth (of his stomach) unfilled, in order to please Shiva (the patron of Yogins). This is called moderate food. Posture herein required is of two kinds, Padma and Vajra.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.4 (Aiyar §3-4)","title":"","sa":["भुज्यते शिवसम्प्रीत्यै मिताहारः स उच्यते । आसनं द्विविधं प्रोक्तं पद्मं वज्रासनं तथा"],"iast":["bhujyate śivasamprītyai mitāhāraḥ sa ucyate | āsanaṃ dvividhaṃ proktaṃ padmaṃ vajrāsanaṃ tathā"],"words":[["bhujyate","भुज्यते","is eaten"],["śivasamprītyai","शिवसम्प्रीत्यै","to please Shiva"],["mitāhāraḥ","मिताहारः","moderate food (nom.)"],["sa","स","he"],["ucyate","उच्यते","is called"],["āsanaṃ","आसनं","posture (acc./nom.)"],["dvividhaṃ","द्विविधं","[?]"],["proktaṃ","प्रोक्तं","[?]"],["padmaṃ","पद्मं","lotus / Padma"],["vajrāsanaṃ","वज्रासनं","Vajrasana (acc.)"],["tathā","तथा","so / and"]],"lit":"1 shall explain the nature of these. Listen to it, O Gautama. One should take a sweet and nutritious food, leaving a fourth (of his stomach) unfilled, in order to please Shiva (the patron of Yogins). This is called moderate food. Posture herein required is of two kinds, Padma and Vajra.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.5","title":"","sa":["ऊर्वोरुपरि चेद्धत्ते उभे पादतले यथा । पद्मासनं भवेदेतत्सर्वपापप्रणाशनम्"],"iast":["ūrvorupari ceddhatte ubhe pādatale yathā | padmāsanaṃ bhavedetatsarvapāpapraṇāśanam"],"words":[["ūrvorupari","ऊर्वोरुपरि","upon the thighs"],["ceddhatte","चेद्धत्ते","[?]"],["ubhe","उभे","both"],["pādatale","पादतले","soles of the feet"],["yathā","यथा","as / just as"],["padmāsanaṃ","पद्मासनं","Padmasana (acc.)"],["bhavedetatsarvapāpapraṇāśanam","भवेदेतत्सर्वपापप्रणाशनम्","would be this destroyer of all sins"]],"lit":"Placing the two heels over the two opposite thighs (respectively) is the Padma (posture) which is the destroyer of all sins.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.6","title":"","sa":["वामाङ्घ्रिमूलकन्दाधो ह्यन्यं तदुपरि क्षिपेत् । समग्रीवशिरःकायो वज्रासनमितीरितम्"],"iast":["vāmāṅghrimūlakandādho hyanyaṃ tadupari kṣipet | samagrīvaśiraḥkāyo vajrāsanamitīritam"],"words":[["vāmāṅghrimūlakandādho","वामाङ्घ्रिमूलकन्दाधो","[?]"],["hyanyaṃ","ह्यन्यं","[?]"],["tadupari","तदुपरि","[?]"],["kṣipet","क्षिपेत्","[?]"],["samagrīvaśiraḥkāyo","समग्रीवशिरःकायो","with neck, head and body erect"],["vajrāsanamitīritam","वज्रासनमितीरितम्","is called Vajrasana"]],"lit":"Placing one heel below the Mulakanda and the other over it and sitting with the neck, body and head erect is the Vajra posture.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.7","title":"","sa":["कुण्डल्येव भवेच्छक्तिस्तां तु सञ्चालयेद्बुधः । स्वस्थानादाभ्रुवोर्मध्यं शक्तिचालनमुच्यते"],"iast":["kuṇḍalyeva bhavecchaktistāṃ tu sañcālayedbudhaḥ | svasthānādābhruvormadhyaṃ śakticālanamucyate"],"words":[["kuṇḍalyeva","कुण्डल्येव","verily Kundalini"],["bhavecchaktistāṃ","भवेच्छक्तिस्तां","[?]"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["sañcālayedbudhaḥ","सञ्चालयेद्बुधः","the wise one should rouse"],["svasthānādābhruvormadhyaṃ","स्वस्थानादाभ्रुवोर्मध्यं","[?]"],["śakticālanamucyate","शक्तिचालनमुच्यते","is called rousing of Shakti"]],"lit":"The Sakti (mentioned above) is only Kundalini. A wise man should take it up from its place (Viz., the navel, upwards) to the middle of the eyebrows. This is called Sakti-Chala.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.8","title":"","sa":["तत्साधने द्वयं मुख्यं सरस्वत्यास्तु चालनम् । प्राणरोधमथाभ्यासादृज्वी कुण्डलिनी भवेत्"],"iast":["tatsādhane dvayaṃ mukhyaṃ sarasvatyāstu cālanam | prāṇarodhamathābhyāsādṛjvī kuṇḍalinī bhavet"],"words":[["tatsādhane","तत्साधने","in its accomplishment"],["dvayaṃ","द्वयं","the two"],["mukhyaṃ","मुख्यं","primary (acc.)"],["sarasvatyāstu","सरस्वत्यास्तु","and of Sarasvati (= sarasvatyāḥ + tu)"],["cālanam","चालनम्","rousing (acc.)"],["prāṇarodhamathābhyāsādṛjvī","प्राणरोधमथाभ्यासादृज्वी","[?]"],["kuṇḍalinī","कुण्डलिनी","Kundalini"],["bhavet","भवेत्","becomes / would be"]],"lit":"In practising it, two things are necessary, Sarasvati-Chalana and the restraint of Prana (breath). Then through practice, Kundalini (which is spiral) becomes straightened.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.9 (Aiyar §9-10(a))","title":"","sa":["तयोरादौ सरस्वत्याश्चालनं कथयामि ते । अरुन्धत्येव कथिता पुराविद्भिः सरस्वती"],"iast":["tayorādau sarasvatyāścālanaṃ kathayāmi te | arundhatyeva kathitā purāvidbhiḥ sarasvatī"],"words":[["tayorādau","तयोरादौ","first of those two"],["sarasvatyāścālanaṃ","सरस्वत्याश्चालनं","rousing of Sarasvati"],["kathayāmi","कथयामि","I tell"],["te","ते","they / those"],["arundhatyeva","अरुन्धत्येव","[?]"],["kathitā","कथिता","told (f.)"],["purāvidbhiḥ","पुराविद्भिः","[?]"],["sarasvatī","सरस्वती","Sarasvati nadi / goddess"]],"lit":"Of these two, I shall explain to you first Sarasvati-Chalana. It is said by the wise of old that Sarasvati is no other than Arundhati. It is only by rousing her up that Kundalini is roused.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.10 (Aiyar §9-10(a))","title":"","sa":["यस्याः सञ्चालनेनैव स्वयं चलति कुण्डली । इडायां वहति प्राणे बद्ध्वा पद्मासनं दृढम्"],"iast":["yasyāḥ sañcālanenaiva svayaṃ calati kuṇḍalī | iḍāyāṃ vahati prāṇe baddhvā padmāsanaṃ dṛḍham"],"words":[["yasyāḥ","यस्याः","of whom (f.)"],["sañcālanenaiva","सञ्चालनेनैव","by the rousing alone"],["svayaṃ","स्वयं","by oneself"],["calati","चलति","[?]"],["kuṇḍalī","कुण्डली","Kundalini"],["iḍāyāṃ","इडायां","in Ida"],["vahati","वहति","[?]"],["prāṇe","प्राणे","in prana"],["baddhvā","बद्ध्वा","having bound"],["padmāsanaṃ","पद्मासनं","Padmasana (acc.)"],["dṛḍham","दृढम्","firmly"]],"lit":"Of these two, I shall explain to you first Sarasvati-Chalana. It is said by the wise of old that Sarasvati is no other than Arundhati. It is only by rousing her up that Kundalini is roused.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.11 (Aiyar §10(b)-11(a))","title":"","sa":["द्वादशाङ्गुलदैर्घ्यं च अम्बरं चतुरङ्गुलम् । विस्तीर्य तेन तन्नाडीं वेष्टयित्वा ततः सुधीः"],"iast":["dvādaśāṅguladairghyaṃ ca ambaraṃ caturaṅgulam | vistīrya tena tannāḍīṃ veṣṭayitvā tataḥ sudhīḥ"],"words":[["dvādaśāṅguladairghyaṃ","द्वादशाङ्गुलदैर्घ्यं","of twelve-finger length"],["ca","च","and"],["ambaraṃ","अम्बरं","[?]"],["caturaṅgulam","चतुरङ्गुलम्","four fingers"],["vistīrya","विस्तीर्य","having extended"],["tena","तेन","by that / by him"],["tannāḍīṃ","तन्नाडीं","[?]"],["veṣṭayitvā","वेष्टयित्वा","having wrapped"],["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"],["sudhīḥ","सुधीः","the wise one"]],"lit":"When Prana breath is passing through (one’s) Ida (left nostril), he should assume firmly Padma-posture and should lengthen (inwards) 4 digits the Akasa of 12 digits.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.12 (Aiyar §11(b)-13(a))","title":"","sa":["अङ्गुष्ठतर्जनीभ्यां तु हस्ताभ्यां धारयेद्धृढम् । स्वशक्त्या चालयेद्वामे दक्षिणेन पुनःपुनः"],"iast":["aṅguṣṭhatarjanībhyāṃ tu hastābhyāṃ dhārayeddhṛḍham | svaśaktyā cālayedvāme dakṣiṇena punaḥpunaḥ"],"words":[["aṅguṣṭhatarjanībhyāṃ","अङ्गुष्ठतर्जनीभ्यां","with thumb and forefinger"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["hastābhyāṃ","हस्ताभ्यां","with the two hands"],["dhārayeddhṛḍham","धारयेद्धृढम्","[?]"],["svaśaktyā","स्वशक्त्या","[?]"],["cālayedvāme","चालयेद्वामे","should rouse to the left"],["dakṣiṇena","दक्षिणेन","[?]"],["punaḥpunaḥ","पुनःपुनः","[?]"]],"lit":"Then the wise man should bind the (Sarasvati) Nadi by means of this lengthened (breath) and holding firmly together (both his ribs near the navel) by means of the forefingers and thumbs of both hands, (one hand on each side) should stir up Kundalini with all his might from right to left often and often; for a period of two Muhurtas (48 minutes), he should be stirring it up fearlessly.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.13 (Aiyar §11(b)-13(a))","title":"","sa":["मुहूर्तद्वयपर्यन्तं निर्भयाच्चालयेत्सुधीः । ऊर्ध्वमाकर्षयेत्किञ्चित्सुषुम्नां कुण्डलीगताम्"],"iast":["muhūrtadvayaparyantaṃ nirbhayāccālayetsudhīḥ | ūrdhvamākarṣayetkiñcitsuṣumnāṃ kuṇḍalīgatām"],"words":[["muhūrtadvayaparyantaṃ","मुहूर्तद्वयपर्यन्तं","up to two muhūrtas (≈96 min)"],["nirbhayāccālayetsudhīḥ","निर्भयाच्चालयेत्सुधीः","[?]"],["ūrdhvamākarṣayetkiñcitsuṣumnāṃ","ऊर्ध्वमाकर्षयेत्किञ्चित्सुषुम्नां","[?]"],["kuṇḍalīgatām","कुण्डलीगताम्","going to Kundalini"]],"lit":"Then the wise man should bind the (Sarasvati) Nadi by means of this lengthened (breath) and holding firmly together (both his ribs near the navel) by means of the forefingers and thumbs of both hands, (one hand on each side) should stir up Kundalini with all his might from right to left often and often; for a period of two Muhurtas (48 minutes), he should be stirring it up fearlessly.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.14 (Aiyar §13(b)-14)","title":"","sa":["तेन कुण्डलिनी तस्याः सुषुम्नाया मुखं व्रजेत् । जहाति तस्मात्प्राणोऽयं सुषुम्नां व्रजति स्वतः"],"iast":["tena kuṇḍalinī tasyāḥ suṣumnāyā mukhaṃ vrajet | jahāti tasmātprāṇo'yaṃ suṣumnāṃ vrajati svataḥ"],"words":[["tena","तेन","by that / by him"],["kuṇḍalinī","कुण्डलिनी","Kundalini"],["tasyāḥ","तस्याः","of her"],["suṣumnāyā","सुषुम्नाया","of Sushumna"],["mukhaṃ","मुखं","mouth / face / face-side"],["vrajet","व्रजेत्","should go / proceeds"],["jahāti","जहाति","[?]"],["tasmātprāṇo'yaṃ","तस्मात्प्राणोऽयं","[?]"],["suṣumnāṃ","सुषुम्नां","Sushumna (acc.)"],["vrajati","व्रजति","goes"],["svataḥ","स्वतः","[?]"]],"lit":"Then he should draw up a little when Kundalini enters Susumna. By this means, Kundalini enters the mouth of Susumna. Prana (also) having left (that place) enters of itself the Susumna (along with Kundalini).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.15","title":"","sa":["तुन्दे तु तानं कुर्याच्च कण्ठसङ्कोचने कृते । सरस्वत्यां चालनेन वक्षसश्चोर्ध्वगो मरुत्"],"iast":["tunde tu tānaṃ kuryācca kaṇṭhasaṅkocane kṛte | sarasvatyāṃ cālanena vakṣasaścordhvago marut"],"words":[["tunde","तुन्दे","in the belly"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["tānaṃ","तानं","the thread / stretching"],["kuryācca","कुर्याच्च","and should do"],["kaṇṭhasaṅkocane","कण्ठसङ्कोचने","in/by neck-contraction"],["kṛte","कृते","when done / having been done"],["sarasvatyāṃ","सरस्वत्यां","in Sarasvati"],["cālanena","चालनेन","[?]"],["vakṣasaścordhvago","वक्षसश्चोर्ध्वगो","and rises up from the chest"],["marut","मरुत्","wind / Marut"]],"lit":"By compressing the neck, one should also expand the navel. Then by shaking Sarasvati, Prana goes above (to) the chest.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.16 (Aiyar §16-17)","title":"","sa":["सूर्येण रेचयेद्वायुं सरस्वत्यास्तु चालने । कण्ठसङ्कोचनं कृत्वा वक्षसश्चोर्ध्वगो मरुत्"],"iast":["sūryeṇa recayedvāyuṃ sarasvatyāstu cālane | kaṇṭhasaṅkocanaṃ kṛtvā vakṣasaścordhvago marut"],"words":[["sūryeṇa","सूर्येण","by the sun (right nostril)"],["recayedvāyuṃ","रेचयेद्वायुं","should exhale the wind"],["sarasvatyāstu","सरस्वत्यास्तु","and of Sarasvati (= sarasvatyāḥ + tu)"],["cālane","चालने","[?]"],["kaṇṭhasaṅkocanaṃ","कण्ठसङ्कोचनं","neck-contraction (acc.)"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["vakṣasaścordhvago","वक्षसश्चोर्ध्वगो","and rises up from the chest"],["marut","मरुत्","wind / Marut"]],"lit":"Through the contraction of the neck. Prana goes above from the chest. Sarasvati who has sound in her womb should be shaken (or thrown into vibration) each day. Therefore by merely shaking it, one is cured of diseases.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.17 (Aiyar §16-17)","title":"","sa":["तस्मात्सञ्चालयेन्नित्यं शब्दगर्भां सरस्वतीम् । यस्याः सञ्चालनेनैव योगी रोगैः प्रमुच्यते"],"iast":["tasmātsañcālayennityaṃ śabdagarbhāṃ sarasvatīm | yasyāḥ sañcālanenaiva yogī rogaiḥ pramucyate"],"words":[["tasmātsañcālayennityaṃ","तस्मात्सञ्चालयेन्नित्यं","[?]"],["śabdagarbhāṃ","शब्दगर्भां","[?]"],["sarasvatīm","सरस्वतीम्","Sarasvati (acc.)"],["yasyāḥ","यस्याः","of whom (f.)"],["sañcālanenaiva","सञ्चालनेनैव","by the rousing alone"],["yogī","योगी","yogin"],["rogaiḥ","रोगैः","by diseases"],["pramucyate","प्रमुच्यते","[?]"]],"lit":"Through the contraction of the neck. Prana goes above from the chest. Sarasvati who has sound in her womb should be shaken (or thrown into vibration) each day. Therefore by merely shaking it, one is cured of diseases.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.18","title":"","sa":["गुल्मं जलोदरः प्लीहा ये चान्ये तुन्दमध्यगाः । सर्वे ते शक्तिचालेन रोगा नश्यन्ति निश्चयम्"],"iast":["gulmaṃ jalodaraḥ plīhā ye cānye tundamadhyagāḥ | sarve te śakticālena rogā naśyanti niścayam"],"words":[["gulmaṃ","गुल्मं","gulma (acc.)"],["jalodaraḥ","जलोदरः","dropsy"],["plīhā","प्लीहा","spleen-disease"],["ye","ये","[?]"],["cānye","चान्ये","[?]"],["tundamadhyagāḥ","तुन्दमध्यगाः","situated in the middle of the belly"],["sarve","सर्वे","all (m.pl.)"],["te","ते","they / those"],["śakticālena","शक्तिचालेन","[?]"],["rogā","रोगा","diseases (pl.)"],["naśyanti","नश्यन्ति","perish (3rd pl.)"],["niścayam","निश्चयम्","[?]"]],"lit":"Gulma (a splenetic disease), Jalodara (dropsy), Pliha (a splenetic disease) and all other diseases arising within the belly, are undoubtedly destroyed by shaking this Sakti.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.19","title":"","sa":["प्राणरोधमथेदानीं प्रवक्ष्यामि समासतः । प्राणश्च दहनो वायुरायामः कुम्भकः स्मृतः"],"iast":["prāṇarodhamathedānīṃ pravakṣyāmi samāsataḥ | prāṇaśca dahano vāyurāyāmaḥ kumbhakaḥ smṛtaḥ"],"words":[["prāṇarodhamathedānīṃ","प्राणरोधमथेदानीं","[?]"],["pravakṣyāmi","प्रवक्ष्यामि","I shall declare"],["samāsataḥ","समासतः","[?]"],["prāṇaśca","प्राणश्च","prana (nom.) + cha (and)"],["dahano","दहनो","the burner"],["vāyurāyāmaḥ","वायुरायामः","[?]"],["kumbhakaḥ","कुम्भकः","kumbhaka (nom.)"],["smṛtaḥ","स्मृतः","is remembered / regarded"]],"lit":"1 shall now briefly describe to you Pranayama. Prana is the Vayu that moves in the body and its restraint within is known as Kumbhaka.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.20","title":"","sa":["स एव द्विविधः प्रोक्तः सहितः केवलस्तथा । यावत्केवलसिद्धिः स्यात्तावत्सहितमभ्यसेत्"],"iast":["sa eva dvividhaḥ proktaḥ sahitaḥ kevalastathā | yāvatkevalasiddhiḥ syāttāvatsahitamabhyaset"],"words":[["sa","स","he"],["eva","एव","only / verily"],["dvividhaḥ","द्विविधः","[?]"],["proktaḥ","प्रोक्तः","[?]"],["sahitaḥ","सहितः","Sahita (nom.)"],["kevalastathā","केवलस्तथा","Kevala likewise"],["yāvatkevalasiddhiḥ","यावत्केवलसिद्धिः","[?]"],["syāttāvatsahitamabhyaset","स्यात्तावत्सहितमभ्यसेत्","[?]"]],"lit":"It is of two kinds, Sahita and Kevala. One should practise Sahita till he gets Kevala.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.21","title":"","sa":["सूर्योज्जायी शीतली च भस्त्री चैव चतुर्थिका । भेदैरेव समं कुम्भो यः स्यात्सहितकुम्भकः"],"iast":["sūryojjāyī śītalī ca bhastrī caiva caturthikā | bhedaireva samaṃ kumbho yaḥ syātsahitakumbhakaḥ"],"words":[["sūryojjāyī","सूर्योज्जायी","Surya, Ujjayi (compound)"],["śītalī","शीतली","Sitali (the cooling)"],["ca","च","and"],["bhastrī","भस्त्री","Bhastrika"],["caiva","चैव","and + iva (like)"],["caturthikā","चतुर्थिका","the fourth (f.)"],["bhedaireva","भेदैरेव","by these varieties alone"],["samaṃ","समं","equally"],["kumbho","कुम्भो","[?]"],["yaḥ","यः","who (m.)"],["syātsahitakumbhakaḥ","स्यात्सहितकुम्भकः","[?]"]],"lit":"There are four Bhedas (lit., piercings or divisions) viz., Surya, Ujjayi, Sitali and Bhastri. The Kumbhaka associated with these four is called Sahita Kumbhaka.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.22 (Aiyar §22-23)","title":"","sa":["पवित्रे निर्जने देशे शर्करादिविवर्जिते । धनुःप्रमाणपर्यन्ते शीताग्निजलवर्जिते"],"iast":["pavitre nirjane deśe śarkarādivivarjite | dhanuḥpramāṇaparyante śītāgnijalavarjite"],"words":[["pavitre","पवित्रे","in a pure (place)"],["nirjane","निर्जने","[?]"],["deśe","देशे","[?]"],["śarkarādivivarjite","शर्करादिविवर्जिते","[?]"],["dhanuḥpramāṇaparyante","धनुःप्रमाणपर्यन्ते","[?]"],["śītāgnijalavarjite","शीताग्निजलवर्जिते","[?]"]],"lit":"Being seated in the Padma posture upon a pure and pleasant seat which gives ease and is neither too high nor too low, and in a place which is pure, lovely and free from pebbles, etc., and which for the length of a bow is free from cold, fire and water, one should shake (or throw into vibration) Sarasvati;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.23 (Aiyar §22-23)","title":"","sa":["पवित्रे नात्युच्चनीचे ह्यासने सुखदे सुखे । बद्धपद्मासनं कृत्वा सरस्वत्यास्तु चालनम्"],"iast":["pavitre nātyuccanīce hyāsane sukhade sukhe | baddhapadmāsanaṃ kṛtvā sarasvatyāstu cālanam"],"words":[["pavitre","पवित्रे","in a pure (place)"],["nātyuccanīce","नात्युच्चनीचे","[?]"],["hyāsane","ह्यासने","[?]"],["sukhade","सुखदे","blissful"],["sukhe","सुखे","in happiness"],["baddhapadmāsanaṃ","बद्धपद्मासनं","bound Padmasana"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["sarasvatyāstu","सरस्वत्यास्तु","and of Sarasvati (= sarasvatyāḥ + tu)"],["cālanam","चालनम्","rousing (acc.)"]],"lit":"Being seated in the Padma posture upon a pure and pleasant seat which gives ease and is neither too high nor too low, and in a place which is pure, lovely and free from pebbles, etc., and which for the length of a bow is free from cold, fire and water, one should shake (or throw into vibration) Sarasvati;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.24","title":"","sa":["दक्षनाड्या समाकृष्य बहिष्ठं पवनं शनैः । यथेष्टं पूरयेद्वायुं रेचयेदिडया ततः"],"iast":["dakṣanāḍyā samākṛṣya bahiṣṭhaṃ pavanaṃ śanaiḥ | yatheṣṭaṃ pūrayedvāyuṃ recayediḍayā tataḥ"],"words":[["dakṣanāḍyā","दक्षनाड्या","by the right nadi (Pingala)"],["samākṛṣya","समाकृष्य","having drawn in"],["bahiṣṭhaṃ","बहिष्ठं","outer / external"],["pavanaṃ","पवनं","wind (acc.)"],["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"],["yatheṣṭaṃ","यथेष्टं","as desired"],["pūrayedvāyuṃ","पूरयेद्वायुं","should fill with wind"],["recayediḍayā","रेचयेदिडया","should exhale through Ida"],["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"]],"lit":"Slowly inhaling the breath from outside, as long as he desires, through the right nostril, he should exhale it through the left nostril.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.25","title":"","sa":["कपालशोधने वापि रेचयेत्पवनं शनैः । चतुष्कं वातदोषं तु कृमिदोषं निहन्ति च"],"iast":["kapālaśodhane vāpi recayetpavanaṃ śanaiḥ | catuṣkaṃ vātadoṣaṃ tu kṛmidoṣaṃ nihanti ca"],"words":[["kapālaśodhane","कपालशोधने","in skull-purification"],["vāpi","वापि","or also"],["recayetpavanaṃ","रेचयेत्पवनं","should exhale the breath"],["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"],["catuṣkaṃ","चतुष्कं","set of four"],["vātadoṣaṃ","वातदोषं","wind-disorder (acc.)"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["kṛmidoṣaṃ","कृमिदोषं","worm-disorder"],["nihanti","निहन्ति","destroys"],["ca","च","and"]],"lit":"He should exhale it after purifying his skull (by forcing the breath up). This destroys the four kinds of evils caused by Vayu as also by intestinal worms.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.26 (Aiyar §26(a))","title":"","sa":["पुनः पुनरिदं कार्यं सूर्यभेदमुदाहृतम् । मुखं संयम्य नाडिभ्यामाकृष्य पवनं शनैः"],"iast":["punaḥ punaridaṃ kāryaṃ sūryabhedamudāhṛtam | mukhaṃ saṃyamya nāḍibhyāmākṛṣya pavanaṃ śanaiḥ"],"words":[["punaḥ","पुनः","again"],["punaridaṃ","पुनरिदं","[?]"],["kāryaṃ","कार्यं","to be done (n.)"],["sūryabhedamudāhṛtam","सूर्यभेदमुदाहृतम्","called Surya-bheda"],["mukhaṃ","मुखं","mouth / face / face-side"],["saṃyamya","संयम्य","having controlled"],["nāḍibhyāmākṛṣya","नाडिभ्यामाकृष्य","[?]"],["pavanaṃ","पवनं","wind (acc.)"],["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"]],"lit":"This should be done often and it is this which is spoken of as Surya-Bheda.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.27 (Aiyar §26(b)-27)","title":"","sa":["यथा लगति कण्ठात्तु हृदयावधि सस्वनम् । पूर्ववत्कुम्भयेत्प्राणं रेचयेदिडया ततः"],"iast":["yathā lagati kaṇṭhāttu hṛdayāvadhi sasvanam | pūrvavatkumbhayetprāṇaṃ recayediḍayā tataḥ"],"words":[["yathā","यथा","as / just as"],["lagati","लगति","reaches / clings"],["kaṇṭhāttu","कण्ठात्तु","from the throat (= kaṇṭhāt + tu)"],["hṛdayāvadhi","हृदयावधि","as far as the heart"],["sasvanam","सस्वनम्","[?]"],["pūrvavatkumbhayetprāṇaṃ","पूर्ववत्कुम्भयेत्प्राणं","[?]"],["recayediḍayā","रेचयेदिडया","should exhale through Ida"],["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"]],"lit":"Closing the mouth and drawing up slowly the breath as before with the nose through both the Nadis (or nostrils) and retaining it in the space between the heart and the neck, one should exhale it through the left nostril.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.28","title":"","sa":["शीर्षोदितानलहरं गलश्लेष्महरं परम् । सर्वरोगहरं पुण्यं देहानलविवर्धनम्"],"iast":["śīrṣoditānalaharaṃ galaśleṣmaharaṃ param | sarvarogaharaṃ puṇyaṃ dehānalavivardhanam"],"words":[["śīrṣoditānalaharaṃ","शीर्षोदितानलहरं","remover of fire arisen in the head"],["galaśleṣmaharaṃ","गलश्लेष्महरं","remover of throat-phlegm"],["param","परम्","supreme / beyond"],["sarvarogaharaṃ","सर्वरोगहरं","remover of all diseases"],["puṇyaṃ","पुण्यं","meritorious"],["dehānalavivardhanam","देहानलविवर्धनम्","increaser of the body-fire"]],"lit":"This destroys the heat caused in the head as well as the phlegm in the throat. It removes all diseases, purifies his body and increases the (gastric) fire within.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.29","title":"","sa":["नाडीजलोदरं धातुगतदोषविनाशनम् । गच्छतस्तिष्ठतः कार्यमुज्जाय्याख्यं तु कुम्भकम्"],"iast":["nāḍījalodaraṃ dhātugatadoṣavināśanam | gacchatastiṣṭhataḥ kāryamujjāyyākhyaṃ tu kumbhakam"],"words":[["nāḍījalodaraṃ","नाडीजलोदरं","dropsy of the nadis"],["dhātugatadoṣavināśanam","धातुगतदोषविनाशनम्","destroyer of impurities in the tissues"],["gacchatastiṣṭhataḥ","गच्छतस्तिष्ठतः","while going or standing"],["kāryamujjāyyākhyaṃ","कार्यमुज्जाय्याख्यं","[?]"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["kumbhakam","कुम्भकम्","kumbhaka (acc.)"]],"lit":"It removes also the evils arising in the Nadis, Jalodara (waterbelly or dropsy) and Dhatus. This Kumbhaka is called Ujjayi and may be practised (even) when walking or standing.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.30","title":"","sa":["जिह्वया वायुमाकृष्य पूर्ववत्कुम्भकादनु । शनैस्तु घ्राणरन्ध्राभ्यां रेचयेदनिलं सुधीः"],"iast":["jihvayā vāyumākṛṣya pūrvavatkumbhakādanu | śanaistu ghrāṇarandhrābhyāṃ recayedanilaṃ sudhīḥ"],"words":[["jihvayā","जिह्वया","with the tongue"],["vāyumākṛṣya","वायुमाकृष्य","[?]"],["pūrvavatkumbhakādanu","पूर्ववत्कुम्भकादनु","[?]"],["śanaistu","शनैस्तु","[?]"],["ghrāṇarandhrābhyāṃ","घ्राणरन्ध्राभ्यां","through the two nostrils"],["recayedanilaṃ","रेचयेदनिलं","should exhale the wind"],["sudhīḥ","सुधीः","the wise one"]],"lit":"Drawing up the breath as before through the tongue with (the hissing sound of) ‘Sa’ and retaining it as before, the wise man should slowly exhale it through (both) the nostrils.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.31","title":"","sa":["गुल्मप्लीहादिकान्दोषान्क्षयं पित्तं ज्वरं तृषाम् । विषाणि शीतली नाम कुम्भकोऽयं निहन्ति च"],"iast":["gulmaplīhādikāndoṣānkṣayaṃ pittaṃ jvaraṃ tṛṣām | viṣāṇi śītalī nāma kumbhako'yaṃ nihanti ca"],"words":[["gulmaplīhādikāndoṣānkṣayaṃ","गुल्मप्लीहादिकान्दोषान्क्षयं","[?]"],["pittaṃ","पित्तं","bile (acc.)"],["jvaraṃ","ज्वरं","fever (acc.)"],["tṛṣām","तृषाम्","thirst (acc.)"],["viṣāṇi","विषाणि","poisons (acc. pl.)"],["śītalī","शीतली","Sitali (the cooling)"],["nāma","नाम","by name / namely"],["kumbhako'yaṃ","कुम्भकोऽयं","[?]"],["nihanti","निहन्ति","destroys"],["ca","च","and"]],"lit":"This is called Sitali Kumbhaka and destroys diseases, such as Gulma, Pitha, consumption, bile, fever, thirst and poison.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.32","title":"","sa":["ततः पद्मासनं बद्ध्वा समग्रीवोदरः सुधीः । मुखं संयम्य यत्नेन प्राणं घ्राणेन रेचयेत्"],"iast":["tataḥ padmāsanaṃ baddhvā samagrīvodaraḥ sudhīḥ | mukhaṃ saṃyamya yatnena prāṇaṃ ghrāṇena recayet"],"words":[["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"],["padmāsanaṃ","पद्मासनं","Padmasana (acc.)"],["baddhvā","बद्ध्वा","having bound"],["samagrīvodaraḥ","समग्रीवोदरः","with neck and belly erect"],["sudhīḥ","सुधीः","the wise one"],["mukhaṃ","मुखं","mouth / face / face-side"],["saṃyamya","संयम्य","having controlled"],["yatnena","यत्नेन","[?]"],["prāṇaṃ","प्राणं","prana (acc.)"],["ghrāṇena","घ्राणेन","by the nose"],["recayet","रेचयेत्","should exhale"]],"lit":"Seated in the Padma posture with belly and neck erect, the wise man should close the mouth and exhale with care through the nostrils.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.33","title":"","sa":["यथा लगति कण्ठात्तु कपाले सस्वनं ततः । वेगेन पूरयेत्किञ्चिधृत्पद्मावधि मारुतम्"],"iast":["yathā lagati kaṇṭhāttu kapāle sasvanaṃ tataḥ | vegena pūrayetkiñcidhṛtpadmāvadhi mārutam"],"words":[["yathā","यथा","as / just as"],["lagati","लगति","reaches / clings"],["kaṇṭhāttu","कण्ठात्तु","from the throat (= kaṇṭhāt + tu)"],["kapāle","कपाले","in the skull"],["sasvanaṃ","सस्वनं","[?]"],["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"],["vegena","वेगेन","with speed"],["pūrayetkiñcidhṛtpadmāvadhi","पूरयेत्किञ्चिधृत्पद्मावधि","[?]"],["mārutam","मारुतम्","wind (acc.)"]],"lit":"Then he should inhale a little with speed up to the heart, so that the breath may fill the space with noise between the neck and skull.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.34 (Aiyar §34-35)","title":"","sa":["पुनर्विरेचयेत्तद्वत्पूरयेच्च पुनः पुनः । यथैव लोहकाराणां भस्त्रा वेगेन चाल्यते"],"iast":["punarvirecayettadvatpūrayecca punaḥ punaḥ | yathaiva lohakārāṇāṃ bhastrā vegena cālyate"],"words":[["punarvirecayettadvatpūrayecca","पुनर्विरेचयेत्तद्वत्पूरयेच्च","[?]"],["punaḥ","पुनः","again"],["punaḥ","पुनः","again"],["yathaiva","यथैव","[?]"],["lohakārāṇāṃ","लोहकाराणां","[?]"],["bhastrā","भस्त्रा","bellows / Bhastrika"],["vegena","वेगेन","with speed"],["cālyate","चाल्यते","is roused"]],"lit":"Then he should exhale in the same way and inhale often and often. Just as the bellows of a smith are moved (viz., stuffed with air within and then the air is let out), so he should move the air within his body. If the body gets tired, then he should inhale through the right nostril.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.35 (Aiyar §34-35)","title":"","sa":["तथैव स्वशरीरस्थं चालयेत्पवनं शनैः । यथा श्रमो भवेद्देहे तथा सूर्येण पूरयेत्"],"iast":["tathaiva svaśarīrasthaṃ cālayetpavanaṃ śanaiḥ | yathā śramo bhaveddehe tathā sūryeṇa pūrayet"],"words":[["tathaiva","तथैव","in the same way"],["svaśarīrasthaṃ","स्वशरीरस्थं","abiding in one's own body"],["cālayetpavanaṃ","चालयेत्पवनं","[?]"],["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"],["yathā","यथा","as / just as"],["śramo","श्रमो","[?]"],["bhaveddehe","भवेद्देहे","[?]"],["tathā","तथा","so / and"],["sūryeṇa","सूर्येण","by the sun (right nostril)"],["pūrayet","पूरयेत्","should fill (inhale)"]],"lit":"Then he should exhale in the same way and inhale often and often. Just as the bellows of a smith are moved (viz., stuffed with air within and then the air is let out), so he should move the air within his body. If the body gets tired, then he should inhale through the right nostril.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.36 (Aiyar §36-37(a))","title":"","sa":["यथोदरं भवेत्पूर्णं पवनेन तथा लघु । धारयन्नासिकामध्यं तर्जनीभ्यां विना दृढम्"],"iast":["yathodaraṃ bhavetpūrṇaṃ pavanena tathā laghu | dhārayannāsikāmadhyaṃ tarjanībhyāṃ vinā dṛḍham"],"words":[["yathodaraṃ","यथोदरं","[?]"],["bhavetpūrṇaṃ","भवेत्पूर्णं","becomes full"],["pavanena","पवनेन","by the wind"],["tathā","तथा","so / and"],["laghu","लघु","[?]"],["dhārayannāsikāmadhyaṃ","धारयन्नासिकामध्यं","[?]"],["tarjanībhyāṃ","तर्जनीभ्यां","by the two forefingers"],["vinā","विना","without"],["dṛḍham","दृढम्","firmly"]],"lit":"If his belly is full of Vayu, then he should press well his nostrils with all his fingers except his forefinger and performing Kumbhaka as before, should exhale through the left nostril.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.37 (Aiyar §36-37(a))","title":"","sa":["कुम्भकं पूर्ववत्कृत्वा रेचेयेदिडयानिलम् । कण्ठोत्थितानलहरं शरीराग्निविवर्धनम्"],"iast":["kumbhakaṃ pūrvavatkṛtvā receyediḍayānilam | kaṇṭhotthitānalaharaṃ śarīrāgnivivardhanam"],"words":[["kumbhakaṃ","कुम्भकं","kumbhaka (acc.)"],["pūrvavatkṛtvā","पूर्ववत्कृत्वा","[?]"],["receyediḍayānilam","रेचेयेदिडयानिलम्","[?]"],["kaṇṭhotthitānalaharaṃ","कण्ठोत्थितानलहरं","[?]"],["śarīrāgnivivardhanam","शरीराग्निविवर्धनम्","increaser of the body-fire"]],"lit":"If his belly is full of Vayu, then he should press well his nostrils with all his fingers except his forefinger and performing Kumbhaka as before, should exhale through the left nostril.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.38 (Aiyar §37(b)-38)","title":"","sa":["कुण्डलीबोधकं पुण्यं पापघ्नं शुभदं सुखम् । ब्रह्मनाडीमुखान्तस्थकफाद्यर्गलनाशनम्"],"iast":["kuṇḍalībodhakaṃ puṇyaṃ pāpaghnaṃ śubhadaṃ sukham | brahmanāḍīmukhāntasthakaphādyargalanāśanam"],"words":[["kuṇḍalībodhakaṃ","कुण्डलीबोधकं","awakener of Kundalini"],["puṇyaṃ","पुण्यं","meritorious"],["pāpaghnaṃ","पापघ्नं","destroyer of sins"],["śubhadaṃ","शुभदं","auspicious"],["sukham","सुखम्","happiness"],["brahmanāḍīmukhāntasthakaphādyargalanāśanam","ब्रह्मनाडीमुखान्तस्थकफाद्यर्गलनाशनम्","[?]"]],"lit":"This frees one from diseases of fire in (or inflammation of) the throat, increases the gastric fire within, enables one to know the Kundalini, produces purity removing sins, gives happiness and pleasure and destroys phlegm which is the bolt (or obstacle) to the door at the mouth of Brahma- Nadi (viz., Susumna).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.39","title":"","sa":["गुणत्रयसमुद्भूतग्रन्थित्रयविभेदकम् । विशेषेणैव कर्तव्यं भस्त्राख्यं कुम्भकं त्विदम्"],"iast":["guṇatrayasamudbhūtagranthitrayavibhedakam | viśeṣeṇaiva kartavyaṃ bhastrākhyaṃ kumbhakaṃ tvidam"],"words":[["guṇatrayasamudbhūtagranthitrayavibhedakam","गुणत्रयसमुद्भूतग्रन्थित्रयविभेदकम्","piercer-of-the-three-knots-arising-from-the-three-gunas"],["viśeṣeṇaiva","विशेषेणैव","[?]"],["kartavyaṃ","कर्तव्यं","to be done (n.)"],["bhastrākhyaṃ","भस्त्राख्यं","called Bhastrika"],["kumbhakaṃ","कुम्भकं","kumbhaka (acc.)"],["tvidam","त्विदम्","[?]"]],"lit":"It pierces also the three Granthis (or knots) differentiated through the three Gunas. This Kumbhaka is known as Bhastri and should especially be performed.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.40","title":"","sa":["चतुर्णामपि भेदानां कुम्भके समुपस्थिते । बन्धत्रयमिदं कार्यं योगिभिर्वीतकल्मषैः"],"iast":["caturṇāmapi bhedānāṃ kumbhake samupasthite | bandhatrayamidaṃ kāryaṃ yogibhirvītakalmaṣaiḥ"],"words":[["caturṇāmapi","चतुर्णामपि","of even the four"],["bhedānāṃ","भेदानां","of the varieties"],["kumbhake","कुम्भके","in kumbhaka"],["samupasthite","समुपस्थिते","[?]"],["bandhatrayamidaṃ","बन्धत्रयमिदं","this group of three bandhas"],["kāryaṃ","कार्यं","to be done (n.)"],["yogibhirvītakalmaṣaiḥ","योगिभिर्वीतकल्मषैः","[?]"]],"lit":"Through these four ways when Kumbhaka is near (or is about to be performed), the sinless Yogin should practise the three Bandhas.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.41","title":"","sa":["प्रथमो मूलबन्धस्तु द्वितीयोड्डीयणाभिधः । जालन्धरस्तृतीयस्तु तेषां लक्षणमुच्यते"],"iast":["prathamo mūlabandhastu dvitīyoḍḍīyaṇābhidhaḥ | jālandharastṛtīyastu teṣāṃ lakṣaṇamucyate"],"words":[["prathamo","प्रथमो","first (m.)"],["mūlabandhastu","मूलबन्धस्तु","[?]"],["dvitīyoḍḍīyaṇābhidhaḥ","द्वितीयोड्डीयणाभिधः","[?]"],["jālandharastṛtīyastu","जालन्धरस्तृतीयस्तु","[?]"],["teṣāṃ","तेषां","[?]"],["lakṣaṇamucyate","लक्षणमुच्यते","[?]"]],"lit":"The first is called Mulabandha. The second is called Uddiyana and the third is Jalandhara. Their nature will be thus described.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.42","title":"","sa":["अधोगतिमपानं वै ऊर्ध्वगं कुरुते बलात् । आकुञ्चनेन तं प्राहुर्मूलबन्धोऽयमुच्यते"],"iast":["adhogatimapānaṃ vai ūrdhvagaṃ kurute balāt | ākuñcanena taṃ prāhurmūlabandho'yamucyate"],"words":[["adhogatimapānaṃ","अधोगतिमपानं","apana with downward motion"],["vai","वै","indeed"],["ūrdhvagaṃ","ऊर्ध्वगं","rising (acc.)"],["kurute","कुरुते","does (3rd sg. mid.)"],["balāt","बलात्","by force"],["ākuñcanena","आकुञ्चनेन","by contraction"],["taṃ","तं","him / that (acc.)"],["prāhurmūlabandho'yamucyate","प्राहुर्मूलबन्धोऽयमुच्यते","they call this Mulabandha"]],"lit":"Apana (breath) which has a downward tendency is forced up by one bending down. This process is called Mulabandha.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.43","title":"","sa":["अपाने चोर्ध्वगे याते सम्प्राप्ते वह्निमण्डले । ततोऽनलशिखा दीर्घा वर्धते वायुनाऽऽहता"],"iast":["apāne cordhvage yāte samprāpte vahnimaṇḍale | tato'nalaśikhā dīrghā vardhate vāyunā''hatā"],"words":[["apāne","अपाने","in apana / when apana"],["cordhvage","चोर्ध्वगे","[?]"],["yāte","याते","which (f.) (3rd sg. mid. pres.)"],["samprāpte","सम्प्राप्ते","[?]"],["vahnimaṇḍale","वह्निमण्डले","[?]"],["tato'nalaśikhā","ततोऽनलशिखा","[?]"],["dīrghā","दीर्घा","[?]"],["vardhate","वर्धते","[?]"],["vāyunā''hatā","वायुनाऽऽहता","[?]"]],"lit":"When Apana is raised up and reaches the sphere of Agni (fire), then the flame of Agni grows long, being blown about by Vayu.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.44 (Aiyar §44-45(a))","title":"","sa":["ततो यातौ वह्न्यपानौ प्राणमुष्णस्वरूपकम् । तेनात्यन्तप्रदीप्तेन ज्वलनो देहजस्तथा"],"iast":["tato yātau vahnyapānau prāṇamuṣṇasvarūpakam | tenātyantapradīptena jvalano dehajastathā"],"words":[["tato","ततो","then / from that"],["yātau","यातौ","the two go / have gone"],["vahnyapānau","वह्न्यपानौ","[?]"],["prāṇamuṣṇasvarūpakam","प्राणमुष्णस्वरूपकम्","[?]"],["tenātyantapradīptena","तेनात्यन्तप्रदीप्तेन","[?]"],["jvalano","ज्वलनो","flame (nom.)"],["dehajastathā","देहजस्तथा","body-born thus"]],"lit":"Then Agni and Apana come to (or commingle with) Prana in a heated state. Through this Agni which is very fiery, there arises in the body the flaming (or the fire) which rouses the sleeping Kundalini through its heat.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.45 (Aiyar §44-45(a))","title":"","sa":["तेन कुण्डलिनी सुप्ता सन्तप्ता सम्प्रबुध्यते । दण्डाहतभुजङ्गीव निःश्वस्य ऋजुतां व्रजेत्"],"iast":["tena kuṇḍalinī suptā santaptā samprabudhyate | daṇḍāhatabhujaṅgīva niḥśvasya ṛjutāṃ vrajet"],"words":[["tena","तेन","by that / by him"],["kuṇḍalinī","कुण्डलिनी","Kundalini"],["suptā","सुप्ता","[?]"],["santaptā","सन्तप्ता","well-heated (f.)"],["samprabudhyate","सम्प्रबुध्यते","[?]"],["daṇḍāhatabhujaṅgīva","दण्डाहतभुजङ्गीव","[?]"],["niḥśvasya","निःश्वस्य","[?]"],["ṛjutāṃ","ऋजुतां","[?]"],["vrajet","व्रजेत्","should go / proceeds"]],"lit":"Then Agni and Apana come to (or commingle with) Prana in a heated state. Through this Agni which is very fiery, there arises in the body the flaming (or the fire) which rouses the sleeping Kundalini through its heat.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.46 (Aiyar §45(b)-46)","title":"","sa":["बिलप्रवेशतो यत्र ब्रह्मनाड्यन्तरं व्रजेत् । तस्मान्नित्यं मूलबन्धः कर्तव्यो योगिभिः सदा"],"iast":["bilapraveśato yatra brahmanāḍyantaraṃ vrajet | tasmānnityaṃ mūlabandhaḥ kartavyo yogibhiḥ sadā"],"words":[["bilapraveśato","बिलप्रवेशतो","[?]"],["yatra","यत्र","where"],["brahmanāḍyantaraṃ","ब्रह्मनाड्यन्तरं","interior of Brahma-nadi"],["vrajet","व्रजेत्","should go / proceeds"],["tasmānnityaṃ","तस्मान्नित्यं","[?]"],["mūlabandhaḥ","मूलबन्धः","Mulabandha"],["kartavyo","कर्तव्यो","to be done (m.)"],["yogibhiḥ","योगिभिः","by yogins"],["sadā","सदा","always"]],"lit":"Then this Kundalini makes a hissing noise, becomes erect like a serpent beaten with stick and enters the hole of Brahmanadi (Susumna). Therefore Yogins should daily practise Mulabandha often.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.47 (Aiyar §47-48(a))","title":"","sa":["कुम्भकान्ते रेचकादौ कर्तव्यस्तूड्डियाणकः । बन्धो येन सुषुम्नायां प्राणस्तूड्डीयते यतः"],"iast":["kumbhakānte recakādau kartavyastūḍḍiyāṇakaḥ | bandho yena suṣumnāyāṃ prāṇastūḍḍīyate yataḥ"],"words":[["kumbhakānte","कुम्भकान्ते","at the end of kumbhaka"],["recakādau","रेचकादौ","at the beginning of exhalation"],["kartavyastūḍḍiyāṇakaḥ","कर्तव्यस्तूड्डियाणकः","[?]"],["bandho","बन्धो","bandha"],["yena","येन","[?]"],["suṣumnāyāṃ","सुषुम्नायां","in Sushumna"],["prāṇastūḍḍīyate","प्राणस्तूड्डीयते","[?]"],["yataḥ","यतः","what (n.) (nom. sg.)"]],"lit":"Uddiyana should be performed at the end of Kumbhaka and at the beginning of expiration. Because Prana Uddiyate (viz., goes up) the Susumna in this Bandha, therefore is called Uddiyana by the Yogins.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.48 (Aiyar §47-48(a))","title":"","sa":["तस्मादुड्डीयणाख्योऽयं योगिभिः समुदाहृतः । सति वज्रासने पादौ कराभ्यां धारयेद्दृढम्"],"iast":["tasmāduḍḍīyaṇākhyo'yaṃ yogibhiḥ samudāhṛtaḥ | sati vajrāsane pādau karābhyāṃ dhārayeddṛḍham"],"words":[["tasmāduḍḍīyaṇākhyo'yaṃ","तस्मादुड्डीयणाख्योऽयं","[?]"],["yogibhiḥ","योगिभिः","by yogins"],["samudāhṛtaḥ","समुदाहृतः","[?]"],["sati","सति","he (3rd sg. pres.)"],["vajrāsane","वज्रासने","in Vajrasana"],["pādau","पादौ","the two feet"],["karābhyāṃ","कराभ्यां","with the two hands"],["dhārayeddṛḍham","धारयेद्दृढम्","[?]"]],"lit":"Uddiyana should be performed at the end of Kumbhaka and at the beginning of expiration. Because Prana Uddiyate (viz., goes up) the Susumna in this Bandha, therefore is called Uddiyana by the Yogins.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.49 (Aiyar §48(b)-49(a))","title":"","sa":["गुल्फदेशसमीपे च कन्दं तत्र प्रपीडयेत् । पश्चिमं तानमुदरे धारयेधृदये गले"],"iast":["gulphadeśasamīpe ca kandaṃ tatra prapīḍayet | paścimaṃ tānamudare dhārayedhṛdaye gale"],"words":[["gulphadeśasamīpe","गुल्फदेशसमीपे","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["kandaṃ","कन्दं","bulb / Kanda"],["tatra","तत्र","there"],["prapīḍayet","प्रपीडयेत्","[?]"],["paścimaṃ","पश्चिमं","western"],["tānamudare","तानमुदरे","[?]"],["dhārayedhṛdaye","धारयेधृदये","[?]"],["gale","गले","in the throat"]],"lit":"Being seated in the Vajra posture and holding firmly the two toes by the two hands, he should press at the Kanda and at the place near the two ankles.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.50 (Aiyar §49(b)-50)","title":"","sa":["शनैः शनैर्यदा प्राणस्तुन्दसन्धिं निगच्छति । तुन्ददोषं विनिर्धूय कर्तव्यं सततं शनैः"],"iast":["śanaiḥ śanairyadā prāṇastundasandhiṃ nigacchati | tundadoṣaṃ vinirdhūya kartavyaṃ satataṃ śanaiḥ"],"words":[["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"],["śanairyadā","शनैर्यदा","[?]"],["prāṇastundasandhiṃ","प्राणस्तुन्दसन्धिं","[?]"],["nigacchati","निगच्छति","enters / approaches"],["tundadoṣaṃ","तुन्ददोषं","belly-impurity (acc.)"],["vinirdhūya","विनिर्धूय","having dispelled"],["kartavyaṃ","कर्तव्यं","to be done (n.)"],["satataṃ","सततं","[?]"],["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"]],"lit":"Then he should gradually upbear the Tana (thread or Nadi) which is on the western side first to Udara (the upper part of the abdomen above the navel), then to the heart and then to the neck. When Prana reaches the Sandhi (junction) of navel, slowly it removes the impurities (or diseases) in the navel. Therefore this should be frequently practised.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.51","title":"","sa":["पूरकान्ते तु कर्तव्यो बन्धो जालन्धराभिधः । कण्ठसङ्कोचरूपोऽसौ वायुमार्गनिरोधकः"],"iast":["pūrakānte tu kartavyo bandho jālandharābhidhaḥ | kaṇṭhasaṅkocarūpo'sau vāyumārganirodhakaḥ"],"words":[["pūrakānte","पूरकान्ते","at the end of inhalation"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["kartavyo","कर्तव्यो","to be done (m.)"],["bandho","बन्धो","bandha"],["jālandharābhidhaḥ","जालन्धराभिधः","called Jalandhara"],["kaṇṭhasaṅkocarūpo'sau","कण्ठसङ्कोचरूपोऽसौ","[?]"],["vāyumārganirodhakaḥ","वायुमार्गनिरोधकः","obstructor of the wind-path"]],"lit":"The Bandha called Jalandhara should be practised at the end of Kumbhaka. This Jalandhara is of the form of the contraction of the neck and is an impediment to the passage of Vayu (upwards).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.52","title":"","sa":["अधस्तात्कुञ्चनेनाशु कण्ठसङ्कोचने कृते । मध्ये पश्चिमतानेन स्यात्प्राणो ब्रह्मनाडिगः"],"iast":["adhastātkuñcanenāśu kaṇṭhasaṅkocane kṛte | madhye paścimatānena syātprāṇo brahmanāḍigaḥ"],"words":[["adhastātkuñcanenāśu","अधस्तात्कुञ्चनेनाशु","[?]"],["kaṇṭhasaṅkocane","कण्ठसङ्कोचने","in/by neck-contraction"],["kṛte","कृते","when done / having been done"],["madhye","मध्ये","[?]"],["paścimatānena","पश्चिमतानेन","by the western stretch"],["syātprāṇo","स्यात्प्राणो","[?]"],["brahmanāḍigaḥ","ब्रह्मनाडिगः","[?]"]],"lit":"When the neck is contracted at once by bending downwards (so that the chin may touch the breast), Prana goes through Brahmanadi on the western Tana in the middle.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.53","title":"","sa":["पूर्वोक्तेन क्रमेणैव सम्यगासनमास्थितः । चालनं तु सरस्वत्याः कृत्वा प्राणं निरोधयेत्"],"iast":["pūrvoktena krameṇaiva samyagāsanamāsthitaḥ | cālanaṃ tu sarasvatyāḥ kṛtvā prāṇaṃ nirodhayet"],"words":[["pūrvoktena","पूर्वोक्तेन","[?]"],["krameṇaiva","क्रमेणैव","in sequence / gradually + iva (like)"],["samyagāsanamāsthitaḥ","सम्यगासनमास्थितः","established in the right posture"],["cālanaṃ","चालनं","rousing (acc.)"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["sarasvatyāḥ","सरस्वत्याः","of Sarasvati"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["prāṇaṃ","प्राणं","prana (acc.)"],["nirodhayet","निरोधयेत्","should restrain"]],"lit":"Assuming the seat as mentioned before, one should stir up Sarasvati and control Prana.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.54","title":"","sa":["प्रथमे दिवसे कार्यं कुम्भकानां चतुष्टयम् । प्रत्येकं दशसङ्ख्याकं द्वितीये पञ्चभिस्तथा"],"iast":["prathame divase kāryaṃ kumbhakānāṃ catuṣṭayam | pratyekaṃ daśasaṅkhyākaṃ dvitīye pañcabhistathā"],"words":[["prathame","प्रथमे","[?]"],["divase","दिवसे","on the day"],["kāryaṃ","कार्यं","to be done (n.)"],["kumbhakānāṃ","कुम्भकानां","of kumbhakas"],["catuṣṭayam","चतुष्टयम्","set of four"],["pratyekaṃ","प्रत्येकं","[?]"],["daśasaṅkhyākaṃ","दशसङ्ख्याकं","of the count ten"],["dvitīye","द्वितीये","[?]"],["pañcabhistathā","पञ्चभिस्तथा","by five likewise"]],"lit":"On the first day Kumbhaka should be done four times; on the second day it should be done ten times and then five times separately;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.55","title":"","sa":["विशत्यलं तृतीयेऽह्नि पञ्चवृद्ध्या दिने दिने । कर्तव्यः कुम्भको नित्यं बन्धत्रयसमन्वितः"],"iast":["viśatyalaṃ tṛtīye'hni pañcavṛddhyā dine dine | kartavyaḥ kumbhako nityaṃ bandhatrayasamanvitaḥ"],"words":[["viśatyalaṃ","विशत्यलं","twenty is enough"],["tṛtīye'hni","तृतीयेऽह्नि","on the third day"],["pañcavṛddhyā","पञ्चवृद्ध्या","with an increase of five"],["dine","दिने","on the day"],["dine","दिने","on the day"],["kartavyaḥ","कर्तव्यः","to be done"],["kumbhako","कुम्भको","[?]"],["nityaṃ","नित्यं","constantly / always"],["bandhatrayasamanvitaḥ","बन्धत्रयसमन्वितः","endowed with the three bandhas"]],"lit":"On the third day, twenty times will do and afterwards Kumbhaka should be performed with the three Bandhas and with an increase of five times each day.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.56 (Aiyar §56-57)","title":"","sa":["दिवा सुप्तिर्निशायां तु जागरादतिमैथुनात् । बहुसङ्क्रमणं नित्यं रोधान्मूत्रपुरीषयोः"],"iast":["divā suptirniśāyāṃ tu jāgarādatimaithunāt | bahusaṅkramaṇaṃ nityaṃ rodhānmūtrapurīṣayoḥ"],"words":[["divā","दिवा","by day"],["suptirniśāyāṃ","सुप्तिर्निशायां","[?]"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["jāgarādatimaithunāt","जागरादतिमैथुनात्","[?]"],["bahusaṅkramaṇaṃ","बहुसङ्क्रमणं","much moving about"],["nityaṃ","नित्यं","constantly / always"],["rodhānmūtrapurīṣayoḥ","रोधान्मूत्रपुरीषयोः","[?]"]],"lit":"Diseases are generated in one’s body through the following causes, viz., sleeping in daytime, late vigils over night, excess of sexual intercourse, moving in crowd, the checking of the discharge of urine and faeces, the evil of unwholesome food and laborious mental operation with Prana.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.57 (Aiyar §56-57)","title":"","sa":["विषमाशनदोषाच्च प्रयासप्राणचिन्तनात् । शीघ्रमुत्पद्यते रोगः स्तम्भयेद्यदि संयमी"],"iast":["viṣamāśanadoṣācca prayāsaprāṇacintanāt | śīghramutpadyate rogaḥ stambhayedyadi saṃyamī"],"words":[["viṣamāśanadoṣācca","विषमाशनदोषाच्च","[?]"],["prayāsaprāṇacintanāt","प्रयासप्राणचिन्तनात्","[?]"],["śīghramutpadyate","शीघ्रमुत्पद्यते","[?]"],["rogaḥ","रोगः","disease (nom.)"],["stambhayedyadi","स्तम्भयेद्यदि","if he arrests"],["saṃyamī","संयमी","the controller / one of restraint"]],"lit":"Diseases are generated in one’s body through the following causes, viz., sleeping in daytime, late vigils over night, excess of sexual intercourse, moving in crowd, the checking of the discharge of urine and faeces, the evil of unwholesome food and laborious mental operation with Prana.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.58","title":"","sa":["योगाभ्यासेन मे रोग उत्पन्न इति कथ्यते । ततोऽभ्यासं त्यजेदेवं प्रथमं विघ्न उच्यते"],"iast":["yogābhyāsena me roga utpanna iti kathyate | tato'bhyāsaṃ tyajedevaṃ prathamaṃ vighna ucyate"],"words":[["yogābhyāsena","योगाभ्यासेन","by yoga practice"],["me","मे","[?]"],["roga","रोग","disease"],["utpanna","उत्पन्न","[?]"],["iti","इति","thus / [end-quote]"],["kathyate","कथ्यते","[?]"],["tato'bhyāsaṃ","ततोऽभ्यासं","[?]"],["tyajedevaṃ","त्यजेदेवं","should thus abandon"],["prathamaṃ","प्रथमं","first (n.)"],["vighna","विघ्न","obstacle"],["ucyate","उच्यते","is called"]],"lit":"If a Yogin is afraid of such diseases (when attacked by them), he says, “my diseases have arisen from my practice of Yoga”. Then he will discontinue this practice. This is said to be the first obstacle to Yoga.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.59","title":"","sa":["द्वितीयं संशयाख्यं च तृतीयं च प्रमत्तता । आलस्याख्यं चतुर्थं च निद्रारूपं तु पञ्चमम्"],"iast":["dvitīyaṃ saṃśayākhyaṃ ca tṛtīyaṃ ca pramattatā | ālasyākhyaṃ caturthaṃ ca nidrārūpaṃ tu pañcamam"],"words":[["dvitīyaṃ","द्वितीयं","second (n.)"],["saṃśayākhyaṃ","संशयाख्यं","called doubt"],["ca","च","and"],["tṛtīyaṃ","तृतीयं","third (n.)"],["ca","च","and"],["pramattatā","प्रमत्तता","carelessness"],["ālasyākhyaṃ","आलस्याख्यं","called laziness"],["caturthaṃ","चतुर्थं","fourth"],["ca","च","and"],["nidrārūpaṃ","निद्रारूपं","of the form of sleep"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["pañcamam","पञ्चमम्","fifth (n.)"]],"lit":"The second (obstacle) is doubt; the third is carelessness; the fourth, laziness; the fifth, sleep;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.60","title":"","sa":["षष्ठं तु विरतिर्भ्रान्तिः सप्तमं परिकीर्तितम् । विषमं चाष्टमं चैव अनाख्यं नवमं स्मृतम्"],"iast":["ṣaṣṭhaṃ tu viratirbhrāntiḥ saptamaṃ parikīrtitam | viṣamaṃ cāṣṭamaṃ caiva anākhyaṃ navamaṃ smṛtam"],"words":[["ṣaṣṭhaṃ","षष्ठं","sixth"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["viratirbhrāntiḥ","विरतिर्भ्रान्तिः","non-leaving and delusion"],["saptamaṃ","सप्तमं","seventh"],["parikīrtitam","परिकीर्तितम्","[?]"],["viṣamaṃ","विषमं","uneven / wrong"],["cāṣṭamaṃ","चाष्टमं","[?]"],["caiva","चैव","and + iva (like)"],["anākhyaṃ","अनाख्यं","unnamed"],["navamaṃ","नवमं","ninth"],["smṛtam","स्मृतम्","remembered (n.)"]],"lit":"The sixth, the not leaving of objects (of sense); the seventh, erroneous perception; the eighth, sensual objects; the ninth, want of faith;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.61","title":"","sa":["अलब्धिर्योगतत्त्वस्य दशमं प्रोच्यते बुधैः । इत्येतद्विघ्नदशकं विचारेण त्यजेद्बुधः"],"iast":["alabdhiryogatattvasya daśamaṃ procyate budhaiḥ | ityetadvighnadaśakaṃ vicāreṇa tyajedbudhaḥ"],"words":[["alabdhiryogatattvasya","अलब्धिर्योगतत्त्वस्य","non-attainment of the truth of yoga"],["daśamaṃ","दशमं","tenth"],["procyate","प्रोच्यते","[?]"],["budhaiḥ","बुधैः","[?]"],["ityetadvighnadaśakaṃ","इत्येतद्विघ्नदशकं","[?]"],["vicāreṇa","विचारेण","by discrimination"],["tyajedbudhaḥ","त्यजेद्बुधः","[?]"]],"lit":"And the tenth, the failure to attain the truth of Yoga. A wise man should abandon these ten obstacles after great deliberation.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.62","title":"","sa":["प्राणाभ्यासस्ततः कार्यो नित्यं सत्त्वस्थया धिया । सुषुम्ना लीयते चित्तं तथा वायुः प्रधावति"],"iast":["prāṇābhyāsastataḥ kāryo nityaṃ sattvasthayā dhiyā | suṣumnā līyate cittaṃ tathā vāyuḥ pradhāvati"],"words":[["prāṇābhyāsastataḥ","प्राणाभ्यासस्ततः","[?]"],["kāryo","कार्यो","[?]"],["nityaṃ","नित्यं","constantly / always"],["sattvasthayā","सत्त्वस्थया","[?]"],["dhiyā","धिया","[?]"],["suṣumnā","सुषुम्ना","Sushumna nadi (central channel)"],["līyate","लीयते","is dissolved"],["cittaṃ","चित्तं","mind-stuff (acc./nom.)"],["tathā","तथा","so / and"],["vāyuḥ","वायुः","wind (nom.)"],["pradhāvati","प्रधावति","[?]"]],"lit":"The practice of Pranayama should be performed daily with the mind firmly fixed on Truth. Then Chitta is absorbed in Susumna and Prana (therefore) never moves.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.63","title":"","sa":["शुष्के मले तु योगी च स्याद्गतिश्चलिता ततः । अधोगतिमपानं वै ऊर्ध्वगं कुरुते बलात्"],"iast":["śuṣke male tu yogī ca syādgatiścalitā tataḥ | adhogatimapānaṃ vai ūrdhvagaṃ kurute balāt"],"words":[["śuṣke","शुष्के","[?]"],["male","मले","[?]"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["yogī","योगी","yogin"],["ca","च","and"],["syādgatiścalitā","स्याद्गतिश्चलिता","would be the motion shaken"],["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"],["adhogatimapānaṃ","अधोगतिमपानं","apana with downward motion"],["vai","वै","indeed"],["ūrdhvagaṃ","ऊर्ध्वगं","rising (acc.)"],["kurute","कुरुते","does (3rd sg. mid.)"],["balāt","बलात्","by force"]],"lit":"When the impurities (of Chitta) are thus removed and Prana is absorbed in Susumna, he becomes a (true) Yogin.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.64","title":"","sa":["आकुञ्चनेन तं प्राहुर्मूलबन्धोऽयमुच्यते । अपानश्चोर्ध्वगो भूत्वा वह्निना सह गच्छति"],"iast":["ākuñcanena taṃ prāhurmūlabandho'yamucyate | apānaścordhvago bhūtvā vahninā saha gacchati"],"words":[["ākuñcanena","आकुञ्चनेन","by contraction"],["taṃ","तं","him / that (acc.)"],["prāhurmūlabandho'yamucyate","प्राहुर्मूलबन्धोऽयमुच्यते","they call this Mulabandha"],["apānaścordhvago","अपानश्चोर्ध्वगो","[?]"],["bhūtvā","भूत्वा","having become"],["vahninā","वह्निना","by fire"],["saha","सह","together with"],["gacchati","गच्छति","goes"]],"lit":"Apana, which has a downward tendency should be raised up with effort by the contraction (of the anus) and this is spoken of as Mulabandha.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.65","title":"","sa":["प्राणस्थानं ततो वह्निः प्राणापानौ च सत्वरम् । मिलित्वा कुण्डलीं याति प्रसुप्ता कुण्डलाकृतिः"],"iast":["prāṇasthānaṃ tato vahniḥ prāṇāpānau ca satvaram | militvā kuṇḍalīṃ yāti prasuptā kuṇḍalākṛtiḥ"],"words":[["prāṇasthānaṃ","प्राणस्थानं","the seat of prana"],["tato","ततो","then / from that"],["vahniḥ","वह्निः","fire (nom., synonym of agni)"],["prāṇāpānau","प्राणापानौ","prana and apana (du.)"],["ca","च","and"],["satvaram","सत्वरम्","swiftly"],["militvā","मिलित्वा","[?]"],["kuṇḍalīṃ","कुण्डलीं","Kundalini (acc.)"],["yāti","याति","goes"],["prasuptā","प्रसुप्ता","[?]"],["kuṇḍalākṛtiḥ","कुण्डलाकृतिः","coiled-form"]],"lit":"Apana thus raised up mixes with Agni and then they go up quickly to the seat of Prana. Then Prana and Apana uniting with one another go to Kundalini, which is coiled up and asleep.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.66 (Aiyar §66-67)","title":"","sa":["तेनाग्निना च सन्तप्ता पवनेनैव चालिता । प्रसार्य स्वशरीरं तु सुषुम्ना वदनान्तरे"],"iast":["tenāgninā ca santaptā pavanenaiva cālitā | prasārya svaśarīraṃ tu suṣumnā vadanāntare"],"words":[["tenāgninā","तेनाग्निना","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["santaptā","सन्तप्ता","well-heated (f.)"],["pavanenaiva","पवनेनैव","by the wind alone"],["cālitā","चालिता","roused (f.)"],["prasārya","प्रसार्य","[?]"],["svaśarīraṃ","स्वशरीरं","[?]"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["suṣumnā","सुषुम्ना","Sushumna nadi (central channel)"],["vadanāntare","वदनान्तरे","[?]"]],"lit":"Kundalini being heated by Agni and stirred up by Vayu, extends her body in the mouth of Susumna, pierces the Brahmagranthi formed of rajas and flashes at once like lightning at the mouth of Susumna.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.67 (Aiyar §66-67)","title":"","sa":["ब्रह्मग्रन्थिं ततो भित्त्वा रजोगुणसमुद्भवम् । सुषुम्ना वदने शीघ्रं विद्युल्लेखेव संस्फुरेत्"],"iast":["brahmagranthiṃ tato bhittvā rajoguṇasamudbhavam | suṣumnā vadane śīghraṃ vidyullekheva saṃsphuret"],"words":[["brahmagranthiṃ","ब्रह्मग्रन्थिं","Brahma-knot (acc.)"],["tato","ततो","then / from that"],["bhittvā","भित्त्वा","having pierced"],["rajoguṇasamudbhavam","रजोगुणसमुद्भवम्","[?]"],["suṣumnā","सुषुम्ना","Sushumna nadi (central channel)"],["vadane","वदने","[?]"],["śīghraṃ","शीघ्रं","quickly"],["vidyullekheva","विद्युल्लेखेव","[?]"],["saṃsphuret","संस्फुरेत्","[?]"]],"lit":"Kundalini being heated by Agni and stirred up by Vayu, extends her body in the mouth of Susumna, pierces the Brahmagranthi formed of rajas and flashes at once like lightning at the mouth of Susumna.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.68 (Aiyar §68-69(a))","title":"","sa":["विष्णुग्रन्थिं प्रयात्युच्चैः सत्वरं हृदि संस्थिता । ऊर्ध्वं गच्छति यच्चास्ते रुद्रग्रन्थिं तदुद्भवम्"],"iast":["viṣṇugranthiṃ prayātyuccaiḥ satvaraṃ hṛdi saṃsthitā | ūrdhvaṃ gacchati yaccāste rudragranthiṃ tadudbhavam"],"words":[["viṣṇugranthiṃ","विष्णुग्रन्थिं","Vishnu-knot (acc.)"],["prayātyuccaiḥ","प्रयात्युच्चैः","[?]"],["satvaraṃ","सत्वरं","swiftly"],["hṛdi","हृदि","in the heart"],["saṃsthitā","संस्थिता","[?]"],["ūrdhvaṃ","ऊर्ध्वं","upward (acc./adv.)"],["gacchati","गच्छति","goes"],["yaccāste","यच्चास्ते","[?]"],["rudragranthiṃ","रुद्रग्रन्थिं","Rudra-knot (acc.)"],["tadudbhavam","तदुद्भवम्","[?]"]],"lit":"Then it goes up at once through Vishnugranthi to the heart. Then it goes up through Rudragranthi and above it to the middle of the eyebrows; having pierced this place, it goes up to the Mandala (sphere) of the moon.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.69 (Aiyar §68-69(a))","title":"","sa":["भ्रुवोर्मध्ये तु संभिद्य याति शीतांशुमण्डलम् । अनाहताख्यं यच्चक्रं दलैः षोडशभिर्युतम्"],"iast":["bhruvormadhye tu saṃbhidya yāti śītāṃśumaṇḍalam | anāhatākhyaṃ yaccakraṃ dalaiḥ ṣoḍaśabhiryutam"],"words":[["bhruvormadhye","भ्रुवोर्मध्ये","[?]"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["saṃbhidya","संभिद्य","having pierced through"],["yāti","याति","goes"],["śītāṃśumaṇḍalam","शीतांशुमण्डलम्","lunar sphere"],["anāhatākhyaṃ","अनाहताख्यं","called Anahata"],["yaccakraṃ","यच्चक्रं","[?]"],["dalaiḥ","दलैः","[?]"],["ṣoḍaśabhiryutam","षोडशभिर्युतम्","[?]"]],"lit":"Then it goes up at once through Vishnugranthi to the heart. Then it goes up through Rudragranthi and above it to the middle of the eyebrows; having pierced this place, it goes up to the Mandala (sphere) of the moon.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.70 (Aiyar §69(b)-70(a))","title":"","sa":["तत्र शीतांशुसञ्जातं द्रवं शोषयति स्वयम् । चलिते प्राणवेगेन रक्तं पीतं रवेर्ग्रहात्"],"iast":["tatra śītāṃśusañjātaṃ dravaṃ śoṣayati svayam | calite prāṇavegena raktaṃ pītaṃ ravergrahāt"],"words":[["tatra","तत्र","there"],["śītāṃśusañjātaṃ","शीतांशुसञ्जातं","produced from the moon"],["dravaṃ","द्रवं","[?]"],["śoṣayati","शोषयति","[?]"],["svayam","स्वयम्","by oneself"],["calite","चलिते","[?]"],["prāṇavegena","प्राणवेगेन","[?]"],["raktaṃ","रक्तं","[?]"],["pītaṃ","पीतं","[?]"],["ravergrahāt","रवेर्ग्रहात्","[?]"]],"lit":"It dries up the moisture produced by the moon in the Anahata-Chakra having sixteen petals.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.71 (Aiyar §70(b)-71)","title":"","sa":["यातेन्दुचक्रं यत्रास्ते शुद्धश्लेष्मद्रवात्मकम् । तत्र सिक्तं ग्रसत्युष्णं कथं शीतस्वभावकम्"],"iast":["yātenducakraṃ yatrāste śuddhaśleṣmadravātmakam | tatra siktaṃ grasatyuṣṇaṃ kathaṃ śītasvabhāvakam"],"words":[["yātenducakraṃ","यातेन्दुचक्रं","having gone to the moon-chakra"],["yatrāste","यत्रास्ते","where remains (yatra + āste)"],["śuddhaśleṣmadravātmakam","शुद्धश्लेष्मद्रवात्मकम्","[?]"],["tatra","तत्र","there"],["siktaṃ","सिक्तं","[?]"],["grasatyuṣṇaṃ","ग्रसत्युष्णं","[?]"],["kathaṃ","कथं","how?"],["śītasvabhāvakam","शीतस्वभावकम्","of cool nature"]],"lit":"When the blood is agitated through the speed of Prana, it becomes bile from its contact with the sun, after which it goes to the sphere of the moon where it becomes of the nature of the flow of pure phlegm. How does it (blood) which is very cold become hot when it flows there ?","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.72","title":"","sa":["तथैव रभसा शुक्लं चन्द्ररूपं हि तप्यते । ऊर्ध्वं प्रवहति क्षुब्धा तदैवं भ्रमतेतराम्"],"iast":["tathaiva rabhasā śuklaṃ candrarūpaṃ hi tapyate | ūrdhvaṃ pravahati kṣubdhā tadaivaṃ bhramatetarām"],"words":[["tathaiva","तथैव","in the same way"],["rabhasā","रभसा","[?]"],["śuklaṃ","शुक्लं","white / semen (śukla)"],["candrarūpaṃ","चन्द्ररूपं","[?]"],["hi","हि","for / indeed"],["tapyate","तप्यते","is heated"],["ūrdhvaṃ","ऊर्ध्वं","upward (acc./adv.)"],["pravahati","प्रवहति","[?]"],["kṣubdhā","क्षुब्धा","[?]"],["tadaivaṃ","तदैवं","[?]"],["bhramatetarām","भ्रमतेतराम्","[?]"]],"lit":"(Since) at the same time the intense white form of moon is speedily heated. Then being agitated, it goes up.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.73","title":"","sa":["तस्यास्वादवशाच्चित्तं बहिष्ठं विषयेषु यत् । तदेव परमं भुक्त्वा स्वस्थः स्वात्मरतो युवा"],"iast":["tasyāsvādavaśāccittaṃ bahiṣṭhaṃ viṣayeṣu yat | tadeva paramaṃ bhuktvā svasthaḥ svātmarato yuvā"],"words":[["tasyāsvādavaśāccittaṃ","तस्यास्वादवशाच्चित्तं","by the force of its tasting the mind"],["bahiṣṭhaṃ","बहिष्ठं","outer / external"],["viṣayeṣu","विषयेषु","in objects"],["yat","यत्","what (n.)"],["tadeva","तदेव","that / it + eva (only / verily)"],["paramaṃ","परमं","supreme (acc.)"],["bhuktvā","भुक्त्वा","[?]"],["svasthaḥ","स्वस्थः","[?]"],["svātmarato","स्वात्मरतो","delighting in his own Self"],["yuvā","युवा","young"]],"lit":"Through taking in this, Chitta which was moving amidst sensual objects externally, is restrained there. The novice enjoying this high state attains peace and becomes devoted to Atman.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.74","title":"","sa":["प्रकृत्यष्टकरूपं च स्थानं गच्छति कुण्डली । क्रोडीकृत्य शिवं याति क्रोडीकृत्य विलीयते"],"iast":["prakṛtyaṣṭakarūpaṃ ca sthānaṃ gacchati kuṇḍalī | kroḍīkṛtya śivaṃ yāti kroḍīkṛtya vilīyate"],"words":[["prakṛtyaṣṭakarūpaṃ","प्रकृत्यष्टकरूपं","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["sthānaṃ","स्थानं","[?]"],["gacchati","गच्छति","goes"],["kuṇḍalī","कुण्डली","Kundalini"],["kroḍīkṛtya","क्रोडीकृत्य","having embraced"],["śivaṃ","शिवं","Shiva (acc.)"],["yāti","याति","goes"],["kroḍīkṛtya","क्रोडीकृत्य","having embraced"],["vilīyate","विलीयते","merges"]],"lit":"Kundalini assumes the eight forms of Prakriti (matter) and attains Shiva by encircling him and dissolves itself in Shiva.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.75","title":"","sa":["इत्यधोर्ध्वरजः शुक्लं शिवे तदनु मारुतः । प्राणापानौ समौ याति सदा जातौ तथैव च"],"iast":["ityadhordhvarajaḥ śuklaṃ śive tadanu mārutaḥ | prāṇāpānau samau yāti sadā jātau tathaiva ca"],"words":[["ityadhordhvarajaḥ","इत्यधोर्ध्वरजः","[?]"],["śuklaṃ","शुक्लं","white / semen (śukla)"],["śive","शिवे","in Shiva"],["tadanu","तदनु","[?]"],["mārutaḥ","मारुतः","wind"],["prāṇāpānau","प्राणापानौ","prana and apana (du.)"],["samau","समौ","[?]"],["yāti","याति","goes"],["sadā","सदा","always"],["jātau","जातौ","[?]"],["tathaiva","तथैव","in the same way"],["ca","च","and"]],"lit":"Thus Rajas-Sukla (seminal fluid) which rises up goes to Shiva along with Marut (Vayu); Prana and Apana which are always produced become equal.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.76","title":"","sa":["भूतेऽल्पे चाप्यनल्पे वा वाचके त्वतिवर्धते । धवयत्यखिला वाता अग्निमूषाहिरण्यवत्"],"iast":["bhūte'lpe cāpyanalpe vā vācake tvativardhate | dhavayatyakhilā vātā agnimūṣāhiraṇyavat"],"words":[["bhūte'lpe","भूतेऽल्पे","[?]"],["cāpyanalpe","चाप्यनल्पे","[?]"],["vā","वा","or"],["vācake","वाचके","[?]"],["tvativardhate","त्वतिवर्धते","[?]"],["dhavayatyakhilā","धवयत्यखिला","[?]"],["vātā","वाता","[?]"],["agnimūṣāhiraṇyavat","अग्निमूषाहिरण्यवत्","like fire, crucible, and gold (sim.)"]],"lit":"Pranas flow in all things, great and small, describable, or indescribable, as fire in gold.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.77","title":"","sa":["आधिभौतिकदेहं तु आधिदैविकविग्रहे । देहोऽतिविमलं याति चातिवाहिकतामियात्"],"iast":["ādhibhautikadehaṃ tu ādhidaivikavigrahe | deho'tivimalaṃ yāti cātivāhikatāmiyāt"],"words":[["ādhibhautikadehaṃ","आधिभौतिकदेहं","elemental body"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["ādhidaivikavigrahe","आधिदैविकविग्रहे","in the celestial body"],["deho'tivimalaṃ","देहोऽतिविमलं","[?]"],["yāti","याति","goes"],["cātivāhikatāmiyāt","चातिवाहिकतामियात्","[?]"]],"lit":"Then this body which is Adhibhautika (composed of elements) becomes Adhidaivata (relating to a tutelar deity) and is thus purified. Then it attains the stage of Ativahika.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.78","title":"","sa":["जाड्यभावविनिर्मुक्तममलं चिन्मयात्मकम् । तस्यातिवाहिकं मुख्यं सर्वेषां तु मदात्मकम्"],"iast":["jāḍyabhāvavinirmuktamamalaṃ cinmayātmakam | tasyātivāhikaṃ mukhyaṃ sarveṣāṃ tu madātmakam"],"words":[["jāḍyabhāvavinirmuktamamalaṃ","जाड्यभावविनिर्मुक्तममलं","[?]"],["cinmayātmakam","चिन्मयात्मकम्","consciousness-natured (n.)"],["tasyātivāhikaṃ","तस्यातिवाहिकं","[?]"],["mukhyaṃ","मुख्यं","primary (acc.)"],["sarveṣāṃ","सर्वेषां","of all"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["madātmakam","मदात्मकम्","[?]"]],"lit":"Then the body being freed from the inert state becomes stainless and of the nature of Chit. In it, the Ativahika becomes the chief of all, being of the nature of That.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.79","title":"","sa":["जायाभवविनिर्मुक्तिः कालरूपस्य विभ्रमः । इति तं स्वस्वरूपा हि मती रज्जुभुजङ्गवत्"],"iast":["jāyābhavavinirmuktiḥ kālarūpasya vibhramaḥ | iti taṃ svasvarūpā hi matī rajjubhujaṅgavat"],"words":[["jāyābhavavinirmuktiḥ","जायाभवविनिर्मुक्तिः","freedom from birth-and-being"],["kālarūpasya","कालरूपस्य","of the form of time"],["vibhramaḥ","विभ्रमः","[?]"],["iti","इति","thus / [end-quote]"],["taṃ","तं","him / that (acc.)"],["svasvarūpā","स्वस्वरूपा","[?]"],["hi","हि","for / indeed"],["matī","मती","[?]"],["rajjubhujaṅgavat","रज्जुभुजङ्गवत्","[?]"]],"lit":"Like the conception of the snake in a rope, so the idea of the release from life and Samsara is the delusion of time.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.80","title":"","sa":["मृषैवोदेति सकलं मृषैव प्रविलीयते । रौप्यबुद्धिः शुक्तिकायां स्त्रीपुंसोर्भ्रमतो यथा"],"iast":["mṛṣaivodeti sakalaṃ mṛṣaiva pravilīyate | raupyabuddhiḥ śuktikāyāṃ strīpuṃsorbhramato yathā"],"words":[["mṛṣaivodeti","मृषैवोदेति","[?]"],["sakalaṃ","सकलं","entire / all (n.)"],["mṛṣaiva","मृषैव","falsely only"],["pravilīyate","प्रविलीयते","[?]"],["raupyabuddhiḥ","रौप्यबुद्धिः","silver-conception"],["śuktikāyāṃ","शुक्तिकायां","in the mother-of-pearl"],["strīpuṃsorbhramato","स्त्रीपुंसोर्भ्रमतो","[?]"],["yathā","यथा","as / just as"]],"lit":"Whatever appears is unreal. Whatever is absorbed is unreal. Like the illusory conception of silver in the mother-of-pearl, so is the idea of man and woman.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.81","title":"","sa":["पिण्डब्रह्माण्डयोरैक्यं लिङ्गसूत्रात्मनोरपि । स्वापाव्याकृतयोरैक्यं स्वप्रकाशचिदात्मनोः"],"iast":["piṇḍabrahmāṇḍayoraikyaṃ liṅgasūtrātmanorapi | svāpāvyākṛtayoraikyaṃ svaprakāśacidātmanoḥ"],"words":[["piṇḍabrahmāṇḍayoraikyaṃ","पिण्डब्रह्माण्डयोरैक्यं","[?]"],["liṅgasūtrātmanorapi","लिङ्गसूत्रात्मनोरपि","[?]"],["svāpāvyākṛtayoraikyaṃ","स्वापाव्याकृतयोरैक्यं","[?]"],["svaprakāśacidātmanoḥ","स्वप्रकाशचिदात्मनोः","[?]"]],"lit":"The microcosm and the macrocosm are one and the same; so also the Linga and Sutratman, Svabhava (substance) and form and the self-resplendent light and Chidatma.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.82","title":"","sa":["शक्तिः कुण्डलिनी नाम बिसतन्तुनिभा शुभा । मूलकन्दं फणाग्रेण दृष्ट्वा कमलकन्दवत्"],"iast":["śaktiḥ kuṇḍalinī nāma bisatantunibhā śubhā | mūlakandaṃ phaṇāgreṇa dṛṣṭvā kamalakandavat"],"words":[["śaktiḥ","शक्तिः","Shakti (nom.)"],["kuṇḍalinī","कुण्डलिनी","Kundalini"],["nāma","नाम","by name / namely"],["bisatantunibhā","बिसतन्तुनिभा","[?]"],["śubhā","शुभा","[?]"],["mūlakandaṃ","मूलकन्दं","[?]"],["phaṇāgreṇa","फणाग्रेण","with the tip of the hood"],["dṛṣṭvā","दृष्ट्वा","having seen"],["kamalakandavat","कमलकन्दवत्","[?]"]],"lit":"The Sakti named Kundalini, which is like a thread in the lotus and is resplendent, is biting with the upper end of its hood (namely, mouth) at the root of the lotus the Mulakanda.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.83 (Aiyar §83-84)","title":"","sa":["मुखेन पुच्छं संगृह्य ब्रह्मरन्ध्रसमन्विता । पद्मासनगतः स्वस्थो गुदमाकुञ्च्य साधकः"],"iast":["mukhena pucchaṃ saṃgṛhya brahmarandhrasamanvitā | padmāsanagataḥ svastho gudamākuñcya sādhakaḥ"],"words":[["mukhena","मुखेन","[?]"],["pucchaṃ","पुच्छं","tail (acc.)"],["saṃgṛhya","संगृह्य","having taken hold of"],["brahmarandhrasamanvitā","ब्रह्मरन्ध्रसमन्विता","joined with Brahma-randhra"],["padmāsanagataḥ","पद्मासनगतः","seated in Padmasana (nom.)"],["svastho","स्वस्थो","well / at ease"],["gudamākuñcya","गुदमाकुञ्च्य","[?]"],["sādhakaḥ","साधकः","practitioner (nom.)"]],"lit":"Taking hold of its tail with its mouth, it is in contact with the hole of Brahmarandhra (of Susumna). If a person seated in the Padma posture and having accustomed himself to the contraction of his anus makes his Vayu go upward with the mind intent on Kumbhaka, then Agni comes to Svadhisthana flaming, owing to the blowing of Vayu.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.84 (Aiyar §83-84)","title":"","sa":["वायुमूर्ध्वगतं कुर्वन्कुम्भकाविष्टमानसः । वाय्वाघातवशादग्निः स्वाधिष्ठानगतो ज्वलन्"],"iast":["vāyumūrdhvagataṃ kurvankumbhakāviṣṭamānasaḥ | vāyvāghātavaśādagniḥ svādhiṣṭhānagato jvalan"],"words":[["vāyumūrdhvagataṃ","वायुमूर्ध्वगतं","[?]"],["kurvankumbhakāviṣṭamānasaḥ","कुर्वन्कुम्भकाविष्टमानसः","[?]"],["vāyvāghātavaśādagniḥ","वाय्वाघातवशादग्निः","[?]"],["svādhiṣṭhānagato","स्वाधिष्ठानगतो","gone to Svadhisthana"],["jvalan","ज्वलन्","blazing"]],"lit":"Taking hold of its tail with its mouth, it is in contact with the hole of Brahmarandhra (of Susumna). If a person seated in the Padma posture and having accustomed himself to the contraction of his anus makes his Vayu go upward with the mind intent on Kumbhaka, then Agni comes to Svadhisthana flaming, owing to the blowing of Vayu.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.85","title":"","sa":["ज्वलनाघातपवनाघातोरून्निद्रितोऽहिराट् । ब्रह्मग्रन्थिं ततो भित्त्वा विष्णुग्रन्थिं भिनत्त्यतः"],"iast":["jvalanāghātapavanāghātorūnnidrito'hirāṭ | brahmagranthiṃ tato bhittvā viṣṇugranthiṃ bhinattyataḥ"],"words":[["jvalanāghātapavanāghātorūnnidrito'hirāṭ","ज्वलनाघातपवनाघातोरून्निद्रितोऽहिराट्","[?]"],["brahmagranthiṃ","ब्रह्मग्रन्थिं","Brahma-knot (acc.)"],["tato","ततो","then / from that"],["bhittvā","भित्त्वा","having pierced"],["viṣṇugranthiṃ","विष्णुग्रन्थिं","Vishnu-knot (acc.)"],["bhinattyataḥ","भिनत्त्यतः","[?]"]],"lit":"From the blowing of Vayu and Agni, the chief (Kundalini) pierces open the Brahmagranthi and then Vishnugranthi.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"1.86","title":"","sa":["रुद्रग्रन्थिं च भित्त्वैव कमलानि भिनत्ति षट् । सहस्रकमले शक्तिः शिवेन सह मोदते"],"iast":["rudragranthiṃ ca bhittvaiva kamalāni bhinatti ṣaṭ | sahasrakamale śaktiḥ śivena saha modate"],"words":[["rudragranthiṃ","रुद्रग्रन्थिं","Rudra-knot (acc.)"],["ca","च","and"],["bhittvaiva","भित्त्वैव","[?]"],["kamalāni","कमलानि","[?]"],["bhinatti","भिनत्ति","pierces"],["ṣaṭ","षट्","six"],["sahasrakamale","सहस्रकमले","in the thousand-petaled lotus (Sahasrara)"],["śaktiḥ","शक्तिः","Shakti (nom.)"],["śivena","शिवेन","by/with Shiva"],["saha","सह","together with"],["modate","मोदते","rejoices"]],"lit":"Then it pierces Rudragranthi, after that, (all) the six lotuses (or plexuses). Then Sakti is happy with Shiva in Sahasrara Kamala (1000 lotuses seat or pineal gland). This should be known as the highest Avastha (state) and it alone is the giver of final beatitude.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]}]},{"t":"Chapter I · Practical observations — Chapter I","u":[{"ref":"Diet (mitāhāra)","title":"verses 3–4","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The Upaniṣad's own gloss is precise: 'sweet and nutritious food, leaving a fourth [of the stomach] unfilled, in order to please Śiva.' The same ratio appears in the Haṭha-Yoga-Pradīpikā (I.58–63). Half the stomach for food, a quarter for water, a quarter empty for air. The verse uses 'sweet' (madhura) and 'smooth' (snigdha) — ghee, milk, rice, gentle vegetables. It excludes — by implication — the rajas-inducing foods Pradīpikā lists explicitly: bitter, sour, salty, pungent, dry, stale, twice-cooked, and old."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Posture (āsana)","title":"verses 5–6","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The text mentions only two: Padmāsana and Vajrāsana. Padma is for prāṇāyāma proper; Vajra is for Uḍḍīyāna (compare verse 48). The minimum requirement common to both is samagrīvaśiraḥkāyaḥ — neck, head, and torso aligned in one vertical line. Without that alignment Sarasvatī-cālana cannot reach the navel."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Sarasvatī-cālana","title":"verses 9–17","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["This is the physical preparatory technique that distinguishes this Upaniṣad from later Haṭha texts. Sitting in Padmāsana, when the breath is flowing in Iḍā, the yogin grips the navel-region between thumb and forefinger of both hands and physically stirs the Sarasvatī-nāḍī (located somewhere near the navel) for two muhūrtas — about 96 minutes. The Adyar commentary equates Sarasvatī here with the Aruṇdhatī-star (faint companion of Vaśiṣṭha in the Big Dipper) — i.e., something subtle that the gross navel-massage is meant to 'wake'. The promised effects are both internal (Kuṇḍalinī enters Suṣumnā) and gross-physiological (verse 18 names gulma, jalodara, plīhā — splenic disorders, dropsy)."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"The four kumbhakas","title":"verses 19–39","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Sūrya-bheda: inhale right, exhale left, after retaining; heats and clears worms.<br>Ujjāyī: inhale both nostrils with throat-friction sound, exhale left; clears head and throat phlegm, may be practised while walking.<br>Śītalī: inhale through curled tongue (sa-sound), exhale both nostrils; cools, clears bile, fever, thirst.<br>Bhastrikā: bellows-breathing — rapid forced inhale-exhale-inhale-exhale through both nostrils, ending in a Sūrya-style retention with bandhas; explicitly named as the one that 'pierces the three granthis' (verse 39) and so is the prime kuṇḍalinī-rouser of the four."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"The three bandhas","title":"verses 40–53","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Mūlabandha forces apāna up; Uḍḍīyāna draws the abdominal contents up under the ribs during external retention; Jālandhara presses the chin to the chest, sealing the upward channel. The Upaniṣad gives a specific sequence (verse 47): Uḍḍīyāna at the end of kumbhaka and beginning of recaka (exhale). Mūlabandha throughout. Jālandhara at the end of pūraka (inhale). The three together form the bandha-traya."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"The ten obstacles","title":"verses 58–61","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The classical list: disease (often a consequence of practice), doubt, carelessness, laziness, sleep, attachment to objects, erroneous perception, sense-objects, lack of faith, failure to attain the truth of yoga. Verse 58 deserves underlining: if yoga-practice itself produces disease, the yogin says 'yoga gave me this' and abandons the practice — that is named as the first obstacle. The cause-attribution is the obstacle, not the disease."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Contraindications (collected from the commentary tradition)","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Sarasvatī-cālana: avoid during acute abdominal illness, pregnancy, recent surgery, menstruation; the navel-grip is direct. Bhastrikā: hypertension, cardiac history, vertigo, glaucoma all contraindicate. The three bandhas together require established prāṇāyāma practice; Brahma-Yogin notes that beginners attempting bandha-traya at the end of every kumbhaka often develop pitta-imbalance (the Upaniṣad's 'inflammation of the throat' — verses 37b–38). Verse 56 itself names specific lifestyle causes of disease that compound with practice: daytime sleep, late vigils, excessive sex, crowds, suppressing urine/stool, bad food, excessive mental exertion."],"kind":"note"}]},{"t":"Chapter II — Khecarī-vidyā","u":[{"ref":"Chapter II","title":"Khecarī-vidyā","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["49 verses","Chapter II is the most procedurally specific portion of the Upaniṣad. It treats Khecarī-mudrā — the 'sky-going seal' — as a complete vidyā with two limbs: abhyāsa (practice — the physical conditioning of the tongue) and melana (the secret mantra-knowledge that activates it). The verses on the tongue's preparation (28–36) are blunt and surgical: weekly cutting of the frenum, daily milking with rock-salt, six-month milestones until the tongue can reach the brahma-randhra. The Upaniṣad twice warns that this practice without a guru and without the bīja-mantra is fruitless or even destructive (II.39, II.48). The chapter culminates in the yogin perceiving the whole universe within his own body — sarvaṃ viśvaṃ paśyaty ātmāvibhedataḥ."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Visual representation","title":"Khecarī tongue placement","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["<pre>\n            PALATE\n              │\n              │   ←  jihvā curled back, frenum\n              │      released through 6-month\n              │      practice (II.28–31)\n        ╭─────┴─────╮\n        │ pharyngeal│   ← brahma-randhra access\n        │   space   │\n        ╰─────┬─────╯\n              │\n              │   tongue tip presses upward,\n              │   sealing the soft palate from\n              │   below; nectar (amṛta) drips\n              │   down and is consumed\n              ▼\n           UVULA</pre>"],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"2.1","title":"","sa":["अथाहं सम्प्रवक्ष्यामि विद्यां खेचरिसंज्ञिकाम् । यथा विज्ञानवानस्या लोकेऽस्मिन्नजरोऽमरः"],"iast":["athāhaṃ sampravakṣyāmi vidyāṃ khecarisaṃjñikām | yathā vijñānavānasyā loke'sminnajaro'maraḥ"],"words":[["athāhaṃ","अथाहं","[?]"],["sampravakṣyāmi","सम्प्रवक्ष्यामि","I shall fully declare"],["vidyāṃ","विद्यां","knowledge (acc.)"],["khecarisaṃjñikām","खेचरिसंज्ञिकाम्","[?]"],["yathā","यथा","as / just as"],["vijñānavānasyā","विज्ञानवानस्या","endowed with this vijñāna"],["loke'sminnajaro'maraḥ","लोकेऽस्मिन्नजरोऽमरः","[?]"]],"lit":"1 shall hereafter describe the science called Khechari which is such that one who knows it is freed from old age and death in this world.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.2","title":"","sa":["मृत्युव्याधिजराग्रस्तो दृष्ट्वा विद्यामिमां मुने । बुद्धिं दृढतरां कृत्वा खेचरीं तु समभ्यसेत्"],"iast":["mṛtyuvyādhijarāgrasto dṛṣṭvā vidyāmimāṃ mune | buddhiṃ dṛḍhatarāṃ kṛtvā khecarīṃ tu samabhyaset"],"words":[["mṛtyuvyādhijarāgrasto","मृत्युव्याधिजराग्रस्तो","seized by death, disease, old age"],["dṛṣṭvā","दृष्ट्वा","having seen"],["vidyāmimāṃ","विद्यामिमां","[?]"],["mune","मुने","O sage (voc.)"],["buddhiṃ","बुद्धिं","[?]"],["dṛḍhatarāṃ","दृढतरां","[?]"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["khecarīṃ","खेचरीं","Khechari (acc.)"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["samabhyaset","समभ्यसेत्","should well practise"]],"lit":"One who is subject to the pains of death, disease and old age should, O sage, on knowing this science make his mind firm and practise Khechari.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.3 (Aiyar §3-4)","title":"","sa":["जरामृत्युगदघ्नो यः खेचरीं वेत्ति भूतले । ग्रन्थतश्चार्थतश्चैव तदभ्यासप्रयोगतः"],"iast":["jarāmṛtyugadaghno yaḥ khecarīṃ vetti bhūtale | granthataścārthataścaiva tadabhyāsaprayogataḥ"],"words":[["jarāmṛtyugadaghno","जरामृत्युगदघ्नो","[?]"],["yaḥ","यः","who (m.)"],["khecarīṃ","खेचरीं","Khechari (acc.)"],["vetti","वेत्ति","knows"],["bhūtale","भूतले","[?]"],["granthataścārthataścaiva","ग्रन्थतश्चार्थतश्चैव","from the text and from the meaning"],["tadabhyāsaprayogataḥ","तदभ्यासप्रयोगतः","[?]"]],"lit":"One should regard that person as his guru on earth who knows Khechari, the destroyer of old age and death, both from knowing the meaning of books and practice, and should perform it with all his heart. The science of Khechari is not easily attainable, as also its practice.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.4 (Aiyar §3-4)","title":"","sa":["तं मुने सर्वभावेन गुरुं मत्वा समाश्रयेत् । दुर्लभा खेचरी विद्या तदभ्यासोऽपि दुर्लभः"],"iast":["taṃ mune sarvabhāvena guruṃ matvā samāśrayet | durlabhā khecarī vidyā tadabhyāso'pi durlabhaḥ"],"words":[["taṃ","तं","him / that (acc.)"],["mune","मुने","O sage (voc.)"],["sarvabhāvena","सर्वभावेन","with all one's being"],["guruṃ","गुरुं","guru (acc.)"],["matvā","मत्वा","having considered"],["samāśrayet","समाश्रयेत्","should resort to"],["durlabhā","दुर्लभा","[?]"],["khecarī","खेचरी","Khechari (sky-going) mudra"],["vidyā","विद्या","knowledge / science / vidyā"],["tadabhyāso'pi","तदभ्यासोऽपि","[?]"],["durlabhaḥ","दुर्लभः","[?]"]],"lit":"One should regard that person as his guru on earth who knows Khechari, the destroyer of old age and death, both from knowing the meaning of books and practice, and should perform it with all his heart. The science of Khechari is not easily attainable, as also its practice.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.5","title":"","sa":["अभ्यासं मेलनं चैव युगपन्नैव सिध्यति । अभ्यासमात्रनिरता न विन्दन्ते ह मेलनम्"],"iast":["abhyāsaṃ melanaṃ caiva yugapannaiva sidhyati | abhyāsamātraniratā na vindante ha melanam"],"words":[["abhyāsaṃ","अभ्यासं","practice (acc.)"],["melanaṃ","मेलनं","Melana (acc.)"],["caiva","चैव","and + iva (like)"],["yugapannaiva","युगपन्नैव","[?]"],["sidhyati","सिध्यति","is accomplished"],["abhyāsamātraniratā","अभ्यासमात्रनिरता","[?]"],["na","न","not"],["vindante","विन्दन्ते","they find"],["ha","ह","[?]"],["melanam","मेलनम्","Melana"]],"lit":"Its practice and Melana are not accomplished simultaneously. Those that are bent upon practice alone do not get Melana.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.6","title":"","sa":["अभ्यासं लभते ब्रह्मञ्जन्मजन्मान्तरे क्वचित् । मेलनं तु जन्मनां शतान्तेऽपि न लभ्यते"],"iast":["abhyāsaṃ labhate brahmañjanmajanmāntare kvacit | melanaṃ tu janmanāṃ śatānte'pi na labhyate"],"words":[["abhyāsaṃ","अभ्यासं","practice (acc.)"],["labhate","लभते","obtains"],["brahmañjanmajanmāntare","ब्रह्मञ्जन्मजन्मान्तरे","[?]"],["kvacit","क्वचित्","somewhere / at some time"],["melanaṃ","मेलनं","Melana (acc.)"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["janmanāṃ","जन्मनां","[?]"],["śatānte'pi","शतान्तेऽपि","[?]"],["na","न","not"],["labhyate","लभ्यते","is obtained"]],"lit":"Only some get the practice, O Brahmana, after several births, but Melana is not obtained even after a hundred births.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.7","title":"","sa":["अभ्यासं बहुजन्मान्ते कृत्वा तद्भावसाधितम् । मेलनं लभते कश्चिद्योगी जन्मान्तरे क्वचित्"],"iast":["abhyāsaṃ bahujanmānte kṛtvā tadbhāvasādhitam | melanaṃ labhate kaścidyogī janmāntare kvacit"],"words":[["abhyāsaṃ","अभ्यासं","practice (acc.)"],["bahujanmānte","बहुजन्मान्ते","[?]"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["tadbhāvasādhitam","तद्भावसाधितम्","accomplished by that state"],["melanaṃ","मेलनं","Melana (acc.)"],["labhate","लभते","obtains"],["kaścidyogī","कश्चिद्योगी","[?]"],["janmāntare","जन्मान्तरे","[?]"],["kvacit","क्वचित्","somewhere / at some time"]],"lit":"Having undergone the practice after several births, some (solitary) Yogin gets the Melana in some future birth as the result of his practice.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.8","title":"","sa":["यदा तु मेलनं योगी लभते गुरुवक्त्रतः । तदा तत्सिद्धिमाप्नोति यदुक्ता शास्त्रसन्ततौ"],"iast":["yadā tu melanaṃ yogī labhate guruvaktrataḥ | tadā tatsiddhimāpnoti yaduktā śāstrasantatau"],"words":[["yadā","यदा","when"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["melanaṃ","मेलनं","Melana (acc.)"],["yogī","योगी","yogin"],["labhate","लभते","obtains"],["guruvaktrataḥ","गुरुवक्त्रतः","from the mouth of the guru"],["tadā","तदा","then / at that time"],["tatsiddhimāpnoti","तत्सिद्धिमाप्नोति","[?]"],["yaduktā","यदुक्ता","[?]"],["śāstrasantatau","शास्त्रसन्ततौ","in the tradition of scriptures"]],"lit":"When a Yogin gets this Melana from the mouth of his Guru, then he obtains the Siddhis mentioned in the several books.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.9","title":"","sa":["ग्रन्थतश्चार्थतश्चैव मेलनं लभते यदा । तदा शिवत्वमाप्नोति निर्मुक्तः सर्वसंसृतेः"],"iast":["granthataścārthataścaiva melanaṃ labhate yadā | tadā śivatvamāpnoti nirmuktaḥ sarvasaṃsṛteḥ"],"words":[["granthataścārthataścaiva","ग्रन्थतश्चार्थतश्चैव","from the text and from the meaning"],["melanaṃ","मेलनं","Melana (acc.)"],["labhate","लभते","obtains"],["yadā","यदा","when"],["tadā","तदा","then / at that time"],["śivatvamāpnoti","शिवत्वमाप्नोति","attains Shiva-state"],["nirmuktaḥ","निर्मुक्तः","completely freed"],["sarvasaṃsṛteḥ","सर्वसंसृतेः","[?]"]],"lit":"When a man gets this Melana through books and the significance, then he attains the state of Shiva freed from all rebirth.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.10","title":"","sa":["शास्त्रं विनापि संबोद्धुं गुरवोऽपि न शक्नुयुः । तस्मात्सुदुर्लभतरं लभ्यं शास्त्रमिदं मुने"],"iast":["śāstraṃ vināpi saṃboddhuṃ guravo'pi na śaknuyuḥ | tasmātsudurlabhataraṃ labhyaṃ śāstramidaṃ mune"],"words":[["śāstraṃ","शास्त्रं","scripture (acc.)"],["vināpi","विनापि","[?]"],["saṃboddhuṃ","संबोद्धुं","to fully know"],["guravo'pi","गुरवोऽपि","even gurus"],["na","न","not"],["śaknuyuḥ","शक्नुयुः","they would be able"],["tasmātsudurlabhataraṃ","तस्मात्सुदुर्लभतरं","[?]"],["labhyaṃ","लभ्यं","[?]"],["śāstramidaṃ","शास्त्रमिदं","this scripture"],["mune","मुने","O sage (voc.)"]],"lit":"Even Gurus may not be able to know this without books. Therefore this science is very difficult to master.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.11","title":"","sa":["यावन्न लभ्यते शास्त्रं तावद्गां पर्यटेद्यतिः । यदा संलभ्यते शास्त्रं तदा सिद्धिः करे स्थिता"],"iast":["yāvanna labhyate śāstraṃ tāvadgāṃ paryaṭedyatiḥ | yadā saṃlabhyate śāstraṃ tadā siddhiḥ kare sthitā"],"words":[["yāvanna","यावन्न","[?]"],["labhyate","लभ्यते","is obtained"],["śāstraṃ","शास्त्रं","scripture (acc.)"],["tāvadgāṃ","तावद्गां","[?]"],["paryaṭedyatiḥ","पर्यटेद्यतिः","[?]"],["yadā","यदा","when"],["saṃlabhyate","संलभ्यते","is well-obtained"],["śāstraṃ","शास्त्रं","scripture (acc.)"],["tadā","तदा","then / at that time"],["siddhiḥ","सिद्धिः","perfection"],["kare","करे","[?]"],["sthitā","स्थिता","[?]"]],"lit":"An ascetic should wander over the earth so long as he fails to get this science and when this science is obtained, then he has got the Siddhi in his hand (viz., mastered the psychical powers).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.12","title":"","sa":["न शास्त्रेण विना सिद्धिर्दृष्टा चैव जगत्त्रये । तस्मान्मेलनदातारं शास्त्रदातारमच्युतम्"],"iast":["na śāstreṇa vinā siddhirdṛṣṭā caiva jagattraye | tasmānmelanadātāraṃ śāstradātāramacyutam"],"words":[["na","न","not"],["śāstreṇa","शास्त्रेण","by scripture"],["vinā","विना","without"],["siddhirdṛṣṭā","सिद्धिर्दृष्टा","[?]"],["caiva","चैव","and + iva (like)"],["jagattraye","जगत्त्रये","[?]"],["tasmānmelanadātāraṃ","तस्मान्मेलनदातारं","[?]"],["śāstradātāramacyutam","शास्त्रदातारमच्युतम्","[?]"]],"lit":"Therefore one should regard as Achyuta (Vishnu) the person who imparts the Melana, as also him who gives out the science.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.13","title":"","sa":["तदभ्यासप्रदातारं शिवं मत्वा समाश्रयेत् । लब्ध्वा शास्त्रमिदं मह्यमन्येषां न प्रकाशयेत्"],"iast":["tadabhyāsapradātāraṃ śivaṃ matvā samāśrayet | labdhvā śāstramidaṃ mahyamanyeṣāṃ na prakāśayet"],"words":[["tadabhyāsapradātāraṃ","तदभ्यासप्रदातारं","[?]"],["śivaṃ","शिवं","Shiva (acc.)"],["matvā","मत्वा","having considered"],["samāśrayet","समाश्रयेत्","should resort to"],["labdhvā","लब्ध्वा","having obtained"],["śāstramidaṃ","शास्त्रमिदं","this scripture"],["mahyamanyeṣāṃ","मह्यमन्येषां","[?]"],["na","न","not"],["prakāśayet","प्रकाशयेत्","[?]"]],"lit":"He should regard as Shiva him who teaches the practice. Having got this science from me, you should not reveal it to others.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.14 (Aiyar §14-15)","title":"","sa":["तस्मात्सर्वप्रयत्नेन गोपनीयं विजानता । यत्रास्ते च गुरुर्ब्रह्मन्दिव्ययोगप्रदायकः"],"iast":["tasmātsarvaprayatnena gopanīyaṃ vijānatā | yatrāste ca gururbrahmandivyayogapradāyakaḥ"],"words":[["tasmātsarvaprayatnena","तस्मात्सर्वप्रयत्नेन","[?]"],["gopanīyaṃ","गोपनीयं","[?]"],["vijānatā","विजानता","[?]"],["yatrāste","यत्रास्ते","where remains (yatra + āste)"],["ca","च","and"],["gururbrahmandivyayogapradāyakaḥ","गुरुर्ब्रह्मन्दिव्ययोगप्रदायकः","[?]"]],"lit":"Therefore one who knows this should protect it with all his efforts (viz., should never give it out except to persons who deserve it). O Brahmana, one should go to the place where lives the Guru, who is able to teach the divine Yoga and there learn from him the science Khechari and being then taught well by him, should at first practise it carefully.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.15 (Aiyar §14-15)","title":"","sa":["तत्र गत्वा च तेनोक्तविद्यां संगृह्य खेचरीम् । तेनोक्तः सम्यगभ्यासं कुर्यादादावतन्द्रितः"],"iast":["tatra gatvā ca tenoktavidyāṃ saṃgṛhya khecarīm | tenoktaḥ samyagabhyāsaṃ kuryādādāvatandritaḥ"],"words":[["tatra","तत्र","there"],["gatvā","गत्वा","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["tenoktavidyāṃ","तेनोक्तविद्यां","[?]"],["saṃgṛhya","संगृह्य","having taken hold of"],["khecarīm","खेचरीम्","Khechari (acc.)"],["tenoktaḥ","तेनोक्तः","[?]"],["samyagabhyāsaṃ","सम्यगभ्यासं","[?]"],["kuryādādāvatandritaḥ","कुर्यादादावतन्द्रितः","[?]"]],"lit":"Therefore one who knows this should protect it with all his efforts (viz., should never give it out except to persons who deserve it). O Brahmana, one should go to the place where lives the Guru, who is able to teach the divine Yoga and there learn from him the science Khechari and being then taught well by him, should at first practise it carefully.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.16 (Aiyar §16-17)","title":"","sa":["अनया विद्यया योगी खेचरीसिद्धिभाग्भवेत् । खेचर्या खेचरीं युञ्जन्खेचरीबीजपूरया"],"iast":["anayā vidyayā yogī khecarīsiddhibhāgbhavet | khecaryā khecarīṃ yuñjankhecarībījapūrayā"],"words":[["anayā","अनया","[?]"],["vidyayā","विद्यया","by the knowledge"],["yogī","योगी","yogin"],["khecarīsiddhibhāgbhavet","खेचरीसिद्धिभाग्भवेत्","becomes a sharer in Khechari-siddhi"],["khecaryā","खेचर्या","by Khechari"],["khecarīṃ","खेचरीं","Khechari (acc.)"],["yuñjankhecarībījapūrayā","युञ्जन्खेचरीबीजपूरया","[?]"]],"lit":"By means of this science, a person will attain the Siddhi of Khechari. Joining with Khechari Sakti (viz., Kundalini Sakti) by means of the (science) of Khechari which contains the Bija (seed of letter) of Khechari, one becomes the lord of Khecharas (Devas) and lives always amongst them. Khechari Bija (seed-letter) is spoken of as Agni encircled with water and as the abode of Khecharas (Devas).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.17 (Aiyar §16-17)","title":"","sa":["खेचराधिपतिर्भूत्वा खेचरेषु सदा वसेत् । खेचरावसथं वह्निमम्बुमण्डलभूषितम्"],"iast":["khecarādhipatirbhūtvā khecareṣu sadā vaset | khecarāvasathaṃ vahnimambumaṇḍalabhūṣitam"],"words":[["khecarādhipatirbhūtvā","खेचराधिपतिर्भूत्वा","becoming the lord of the Khecharas"],["khecareṣu","खेचरेषु","among the Khecharas"],["sadā","सदा","always"],["vaset","वसेत्","[?]"],["khecarāvasathaṃ","खेचरावसथं","Khechara-abode"],["vahnimambumaṇḍalabhūṣitam","वह्निमम्बुमण्डलभूषितम्","[?]"]],"lit":"By means of this science, a person will attain the Siddhi of Khechari. Joining with Khechari Sakti (viz., Kundalini Sakti) by means of the (science) of Khechari which contains the Bija (seed of letter) of Khechari, one becomes the lord of Khecharas (Devas) and lives always amongst them. Khechari Bija (seed-letter) is spoken of as Agni encircled with water and as the abode of Khecharas (Devas).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.18","title":"","sa":["आख्यातं खेचरीबीजं तेन योगः प्रसिध्यति । सोमांशनवकं वर्णं प्रतिलोमेन चोद्धरेत्"],"iast":["ākhyātaṃ khecarībījaṃ tena yogaḥ prasidhyati | somāṃśanavakaṃ varṇaṃ pratilomena coddharet"],"words":[["ākhyātaṃ","आख्यातं","is declared (n.)"],["khecarībījaṃ","खेचरीबीजं","[?]"],["tena","तेन","by that / by him"],["yogaḥ","योगः","yoga (nom.)"],["prasidhyati","प्रसिध्यति","[?]"],["somāṃśanavakaṃ","सोमांशनवकं","[?]"],["varṇaṃ","वर्णं","letter / colour"],["pratilomena","प्रतिलोमेन","in reverse order"],["coddharet","चोद्धरेत्","[?]"]],"lit":"Through this Yoga, Siddhi is mastered. The ninth (Bija) letter of Somamsa (Soma or moon part) should also be pronounced in the reverse order.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.19","title":"","sa":["तस्मात्त्र्यंशकमाख्यातमक्षरं चन्द्ररूपकम् । तस्मादप्यष्टमं वर्णं विलोमेन परं मुने"],"iast":["tasmāttryaṃśakamākhyātamakṣaraṃ candrarūpakam | tasmādapyaṣṭamaṃ varṇaṃ vilomena paraṃ mune"],"words":[["tasmāttryaṃśakamākhyātamakṣaraṃ","तस्मात्त्र्यंशकमाख्यातमक्षरं","[?]"],["candrarūpakam","चन्द्ररूपकम्","[?]"],["tasmādapyaṣṭamaṃ","तस्मादप्यष्टमं","[?]"],["varṇaṃ","वर्णं","letter / colour"],["vilomena","विलोमेन","in reverse order"],["paraṃ","परं","supreme (acc./adv.)"],["mune","मुने","O sage (voc.)"]],"lit":"Then a letter composed of three Amsas of the form of moon has been described; and after that, the eight letter should be pronounced in the reverse order;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.20","title":"","sa":["तथा तत्परमं विद्धि तदादिरपि पञ्चमी । इन्दोश्च बहुभिन्ने च कूटोऽयं परिकीर्तितः"],"iast":["tathā tatparamaṃ viddhi tadādirapi pañcamī | indośca bahubhinne ca kūṭo'yaṃ parikīrtitaḥ"],"words":[["tathā","तथा","so / and"],["tatparamaṃ","तत्परमं","[?]"],["viddhi","विद्धि","know!"],["tadādirapi","तदादिरपि","[?]"],["pañcamī","पञ्चमी","fifth (f.)"],["indośca","इन्दोश्च","of the moon + cha (and)"],["bahubhinne","बहुभिन्ने","in the variously-pierced"],["ca","च","and"],["kūṭo'yaṃ","कूटोऽयं","this horn"],["parikīrtitaḥ","परिकीर्तितः","[?]"]],"lit":"Then consider it as the supreme and its beginning as the fifth and this is said to the Kuta (horns) of the several bhinnas (or parts) of the moon.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.21 (Aiyar §21-22(a))","title":"","sa":["गुरूपदेशलभ्यं च सर्वयोगप्रसिद्धिदम् । यत्तस्य देहजा माया निरुद्धकरणाश्रया"],"iast":["gurūpadeśalabhyaṃ ca sarvayogaprasiddhidam | yattasya dehajā māyā niruddhakaraṇāśrayā"],"words":[["gurūpadeśalabhyaṃ","गुरूपदेशलभ्यं","obtainable by the guru's teaching"],["ca","च","and"],["sarvayogaprasiddhidam","सर्वयोगप्रसिद्धिदम्","[?]"],["yattasya","यत्तस्य","[?]"],["dehajā","देहजा","body-born"],["māyā","माया","māyā (illusion)"],["niruddhakaraṇāśrayā","निरुद्धकरणाश्रया","with restrained senses as support"]],"lit":"This which tends to the accomplishment of all Yogas, should be leamt through the initiation of a Guru. He who recites this twelve times every day, will not get even in sleep that Maya (illusion) which is born in his body and which is the source of all vicious deeds.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.22 (Aiyar §21-22(a))","title":"","sa":["स्वप्नेऽपि न लभेत्तस्य नित्यं द्वादशजप्यतः । य इमां पञ्च लक्षाणि जपेदपि सुयन्त्रितः"],"iast":["svapne'pi na labhettasya nityaṃ dvādaśajapyataḥ | ya imāṃ pañca lakṣāṇi japedapi suyantritaḥ"],"words":[["svapne'pi","स्वप्नेऽपि","[?]"],["na","न","not"],["labhettasya","लभेत्तस्य","[?]"],["nityaṃ","नित्यं","constantly / always"],["dvādaśajapyataḥ","द्वादशजप्यतः","from twelve-fold repetition"],["ya","य","who"],["imāṃ","इमां","this (f. acc.)"],["pañca","पञ्च","five"],["lakṣāṇi","लक्षाणि","lakhs"],["japedapi","जपेदपि","should also repeat"],["suyantritaḥ","सुयन्त्रितः","well-controlled"]],"lit":"This which tends to the accomplishment of all Yogas, should be leamt through the initiation of a Guru. He who recites this twelve times every day, will not get even in sleep that Maya (illusion) which is born in his body and which is the source of all vicious deeds.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.23 (Aiyar §22(b)-23)","title":"","sa":["तस्य श्रीखेचरीसिद्धिः स्वयमेव प्रवर्तते । नश्यन्ति सर्वविघ्नानि प्रसीदन्ति च देवताः"],"iast":["tasya śrīkhecarīsiddhiḥ svayameva pravartate | naśyanti sarvavighnāni prasīdanti ca devatāḥ"],"words":[["tasya","तस्य","of him / its"],["śrīkhecarīsiddhiḥ","श्रीखेचरीसिद्धिः","the glorious Khechari-siddhi"],["svayameva","स्वयमेव","[?]"],["pravartate","प्रवर्तते","[?]"],["naśyanti","नश्यन्ति","perish (3rd pl.)"],["sarvavighnāni","सर्वविघ्नानि","[?]"],["prasīdanti","प्रसीदन्ति","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["devatāḥ","देवताः","[?]"]],"lit":"He who recites this five lakhs of times with very great care - to him the science of Khechari will reveal itself. All obstacles vanish and the Devas are pleased.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.24","title":"","sa":["वलीपलितनाशश्च भविष्यति न संशयः । एवं लब्ध्वा महाविद्यामभ्यासं कारयेत्ततः"],"iast":["valīpalitanāśaśca bhaviṣyati na saṃśayaḥ | evaṃ labdhvā mahāvidyāmabhyāsaṃ kārayettataḥ"],"words":[["valīpalitanāśaśca","वलीपलितनाशश्च","and destruction of wrinkles and grey hair"],["bhaviṣyati","भविष्यति","will be"],["na","न","not"],["saṃśayaḥ","संशयः","doubt (nom.)"],["evaṃ","एवं","thus"],["labdhvā","लब्ध्वा","having obtained"],["mahāvidyāmabhyāsaṃ","महाविद्यामभ्यासं","[?]"],["kārayettataḥ","कारयेत्ततः","then he should cause"]],"lit":"The destruction of Valipalita (viz., wrinkle and greyness of hair) will take place without doubt. Having acquired this great science, one should practise it afterwards.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.25 (Aiyar §25-26)","title":"","sa":["अन्यथा क्लिश्यते ब्रह्मन्न सिद्धिः खेचरीपथे । यदभ्यासविधौ विद्यां न लभेद्यः सुधामयीम्"],"iast":["anyathā kliśyate brahmanna siddhiḥ khecarīpathe | yadabhyāsavidhau vidyāṃ na labhedyaḥ sudhāmayīm"],"words":[["anyathā","अन्यथा","otherwise"],["kliśyate","क्लिश्यते","[?]"],["brahmanna","ब्रह्मन्न","O Brahmin, not (= brahman + na)"],["siddhiḥ","सिद्धिः","perfection"],["khecarīpathe","खेचरीपथे","in the Khechari path"],["yadabhyāsavidhau","यदभ्यासविधौ","[?]"],["vidyāṃ","विद्यां","knowledge (acc.)"],["na","न","not"],["labhedyaḥ","लभेद्यः","[?]"],["sudhāmayīm","सुधामयीम्","[?]"]],"lit":"If not, O Brahmana, he will suffer without getting any Siddhi in the path of Khechari. If one does not get this nectar like science in this practice, he should get it in the beginning of Melana and recite it always; (else) one who is without it never gets Siddhi.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.26 (Aiyar §25-26)","title":"","sa":["ततः संमेलकादौ च लब्ध्वा विद्यां सदा जपेत् । नान्यथा रहितो ब्रह्मन्न किञ्चित्सिद्धिभाग्भवेत्"],"iast":["tataḥ saṃmelakādau ca labdhvā vidyāṃ sadā japet | nānyathā rahito brahmanna kiñcitsiddhibhāgbhavet"],"words":[["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"],["saṃmelakādau","संमेलकादौ","at the start of the convocation"],["ca","च","and"],["labdhvā","लब्ध्वा","having obtained"],["vidyāṃ","विद्यां","knowledge (acc.)"],["sadā","सदा","always"],["japet","जपेत्","[?]"],["nānyathā","नान्यथा","not otherwise"],["rahito","रहितो","[?]"],["brahmanna","ब्रह्मन्न","O Brahmin, not (= brahman + na)"],["kiñcitsiddhibhāgbhavet","किञ्चित्सिद्धिभाग्भवेत्","[?]"]],"lit":"If not, O Brahmana, he will suffer without getting any Siddhi in the path of Khechari. If one does not get this nectar like science in this practice, he should get it in the beginning of Melana and recite it always; (else) one who is without it never gets Siddhi.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.27","title":"","sa":["यदिदं लभ्यते शास्त्रं तदा विद्यां समाश्रयेत् । ततस्तदोदितां सिद्धिमाशु तां लभते मुनिः"],"iast":["yadidaṃ labhyate śāstraṃ tadā vidyāṃ samāśrayet | tatastadoditāṃ siddhimāśu tāṃ labhate muniḥ"],"words":[["yadidaṃ","यदिदं","[?]"],["labhyate","लभ्यते","is obtained"],["śāstraṃ","शास्त्रं","scripture (acc.)"],["tadā","तदा","then / at that time"],["vidyāṃ","विद्यां","knowledge (acc.)"],["samāśrayet","समाश्रयेत्","should resort to"],["tatastadoditāṃ","ततस्तदोदितां","[?]"],["siddhimāśu","सिद्धिमाशु","[?]"],["tāṃ","तां","[?]"],["labhate","लभते","obtains"],["muniḥ","मुनिः","sage (nom.)"]],"lit":"As soon as he gets this science, he should practise it; and then the sage will soon get the Siddhi.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.28","title":"","sa":["तालुमूलं समुत्कृष्य सप्तवासरमात्मवित् । स्वगुरूक्तप्रकारेण मलं सर्वं विशोधयेत्"],"iast":["tālumūlaṃ samutkṛṣya saptavāsaramātmavit | svagurūktaprakāreṇa malaṃ sarvaṃ viśodhayet"],"words":[["tālumūlaṃ","तालुमूलं","root of the palate"],["samutkṛṣya","समुत्कृष्य","[?]"],["saptavāsaramātmavit","सप्तवासरमात्मवित्","for seven days the Self-knower"],["svagurūktaprakāreṇa","स्वगुरूक्तप्रकारेण","[?]"],["malaṃ","मलं","[?]"],["sarvaṃ","सर्वं","all (n.)"],["viśodhayet","विशोधयेत्","[?]"]],"lit":"Having drawn out the tongue from the root of the palate, a knower of Atman should clear the impurity (of the tongue) for seven days according to the advice of his Gum.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.29","title":"","sa":["स्नुहिपत्रनिभं शस्त्रं सुतीक्ष्णं स्निग्धनिर्मलम् । समादाय ततस्तेन रोममात्रं समुच्छिनेत्"],"iast":["snuhipatranibhaṃ śastraṃ sutīkṣṇaṃ snigdhanirmalam | samādāya tatastena romamātraṃ samucchinet"],"words":[["snuhipatranibhaṃ","स्नुहिपत्रनिभं","resembling the snuhi-leaf"],["śastraṃ","शस्त्रं","knife / instrument"],["sutīkṣṇaṃ","सुतीक्ष्णं","sharp"],["snigdhanirmalam","स्निग्धनिर्मलम्","smooth and clean"],["samādāya","समादाय","having taken up"],["tatastena","ततस्तेन","[?]"],["romamātraṃ","रोममात्रं","the measure of a hair"],["samucchinet","समुच्छिनेत्","should cut"]],"lit":"He should take a sharp knife which is oiled and cleaned and which resembles the leaf of the plant Snuhi (“Euphorbia Antiquorum”) and should cut for the space of a hair (the Fraenum Lingui).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.30","title":"","sa":["हित्वा सैन्धवपथ्याभ्यां चूर्णिताभ्यां प्रकर्षयेत् । पुनः सप्तदिने प्राप्ते रोममात्रं समुच्छिनेत्"],"iast":["hitvā saindhavapathyābhyāṃ cūrṇitābhyāṃ prakarṣayet | punaḥ saptadine prāpte romamātraṃ samucchinet"],"words":[["hitvā","हित्वा","[?]"],["saindhavapathyābhyāṃ","सैन्धवपथ्याभ्यां","with rock-salt and sea-salt (du.)"],["cūrṇitābhyāṃ","चूर्णिताभ्यां","with powdered (du.)"],["prakarṣayet","प्रकर्षयेत्","should rub"],["punaḥ","पुनः","again"],["saptadine","सप्तदिने","[?]"],["prāpte","प्राप्ते","[?]"],["romamātraṃ","रोममात्रं","the measure of a hair"],["samucchinet","समुच्छिनेत्","should cut"]],"lit":"Having powdered Saindhava (rock-salt) and Pathya (sea-salt), he should apply it to the place. On the seventh day, he should again cut for the space of a hair.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.31","title":"","sa":["एवं क्रमेण षण्मासं नित्योद्युक्तः समाचरेत् । षण्मासाद्रसनामूलं सिराबद्धं प्रणश्यति"],"iast":["evaṃ krameṇa ṣaṇmāsaṃ nityodyuktaḥ samācaret | ṣaṇmāsādrasanāmūlaṃ sirābaddhaṃ praṇaśyati"],"words":[["evaṃ","एवं","thus"],["krameṇa","क्रमेण","in sequence / gradually"],["ṣaṇmāsaṃ","षण्मासं","six months (acc.)"],["nityodyuktaḥ","नित्योद्युक्तः","[?]"],["samācaret","समाचरेत्","should perform"],["ṣaṇmāsādrasanāmūlaṃ","षण्मासाद्रसनामूलं","after six months, root of tongue"],["sirābaddhaṃ","सिराबद्धं","[?]"],["praṇaśyati","प्रणश्यति","is destroyed"]],"lit":"Thus for the space of six months, he should continue it always gradually with great care. In six months, Siro-Bandha (Bandha at the head), which is at the root of the tongue is destroyed.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.32","title":"","sa":["अथ वागीश्वरीधाम शिरो वस्त्रेण वेष्टयेत् । शनैरुत्कर्षयेद्योगी कालवेलाविधानवित्"],"iast":["atha vāgīśvarīdhāma śiro vastreṇa veṣṭayet | śanairutkarṣayedyogī kālavelāvidhānavit"],"words":[["atha","अथ","now"],["vāgīśvarīdhāma","वागीश्वरीधाम","the abode of the Mistress-of-Speech"],["śiro","शिरो","[?]"],["vastreṇa","वस्त्रेण","with cloth"],["veṣṭayet","वेष्टयेत्","[?]"],["śanairutkarṣayedyogī","शनैरुत्कर्षयेद्योगी","[?]"],["kālavelāvidhānavit","कालवेलाविधानवित्","knower of the timely method"]],"lit":"Then the Yogin who knows timely action should encircle with Siro-Vastra (lit. the cloth of the head) the Vak-Ishvari (the deity presiding over speech) and should draw (it) up.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.33","title":"","sa":["पुनः षण्मासमात्रेण नित्यं सङ्घर्षणान्मुने । भ्रूमध्यावधि चाप्येति तिर्यक्कणबिलावधिः"],"iast":["punaḥ ṣaṇmāsamātreṇa nityaṃ saṅgharṣaṇānmune | bhrūmadhyāvadhi cāpyeti tiryakkaṇabilāvadhiḥ"],"words":[["punaḥ","पुनः","again"],["ṣaṇmāsamātreṇa","षण्मासमात्रेण","merely six months"],["nityaṃ","नित्यं","constantly / always"],["saṅgharṣaṇānmune","सङ्घर्षणान्मुने","[?]"],["bhrūmadhyāvadhi","भ्रूमध्यावधि","as far as between the eyebrows"],["cāpyeti","चाप्येति","[?]"],["tiryakkaṇabilāvadhiḥ","तिर्यक्कणबिलावधिः","[?]"]],"lit":"Again by daily drawing it up for six months, it comes, O sage, as far as the middle of the eyebrows and obliquely up to the opening of the ears;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.34","title":"","sa":["अधश्च चुबुकं मूलं प्रयाति क्रमचारिता । पुनः संवत्सराणां तु तृतीयादेव लीलया"],"iast":["adhaśca cubukaṃ mūlaṃ prayāti kramacāritā | punaḥ saṃvatsarāṇāṃ tu tṛtīyādeva līlayā"],"words":[["adhaśca","अधश्च","[?]"],["cubukaṃ","चुबुकं","[?]"],["mūlaṃ","मूलं","[?]"],["prayāti","प्रयाति","[?]"],["kramacāritā","क्रमचारिता","gone in sequence"],["punaḥ","पुनः","again"],["saṃvatsarāṇāṃ","संवत्सराणां","of years"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["tṛtīyādeva","तृतीयादेव","from the third [year] alone"],["līlayā","लीलया","[?]"]],"lit":"Having gradually practised, it goes to the root of the chin. Then in three years, it goes up easily to the end of the hair (of the head).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.35 (Aiyar §35-36)","title":"","sa":["केशान्तमूर्ध्वं क्रमति तिर्यक् शाखावधिर्मुने । अधस्तात्कण्ठकूपान्तं पुनर्वर्षत्रयेण तु"],"iast":["keśāntamūrdhvaṃ kramati tiryak śākhāvadhirmune | adhastātkaṇṭhakūpāntaṃ punarvarṣatrayeṇa tu"],"words":[["keśāntamūrdhvaṃ","केशान्तमूर्ध्वं","[?]"],["kramati","क्रमति","proceeds"],["tiryak","तिर्यक्","across / obliquely"],["śākhāvadhirmune","शाखावधिर्मुने","[?]"],["adhastātkaṇṭhakūpāntaṃ","अधस्तात्कण्ठकूपान्तं","[?]"],["punarvarṣatrayeṇa","पुनर्वर्षत्रयेण","[?]"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"]],"lit":"It goes up obliquely to Sakha and downwards to the well of the throat. In another three years, it occupies Brahmarandhra and stops there without doubt. Crosswise it goes up to the top of the head and downwards to the well of the throat.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.36 (Aiyar §35-36)","title":"","sa":["ब्रह्मरन्ध्रं समावृत्य तिष्ठेदेव न संशयः । तिर्यक् चूलितलं याति अधः कण्ठबिलावधि"],"iast":["brahmarandhraṃ samāvṛtya tiṣṭhedeva na saṃśayaḥ | tiryak cūlitalaṃ yāti adhaḥ kaṇṭhabilāvadhi"],"words":[["brahmarandhraṃ","ब्रह्मरन्ध्रं","Brahma-randhra (acc.)"],["samāvṛtya","समावृत्य","[?]"],["tiṣṭhedeva","तिष्ठेदेव","would surely stand"],["na","न","not"],["saṃśayaḥ","संशयः","doubt (nom.)"],["tiryak","तिर्यक्","across / obliquely"],["cūlitalaṃ","चूलितलं","[?]"],["yāti","याति","goes"],["adhaḥ","अधः","[?]"],["kaṇṭhabilāvadhi","कण्ठबिलावधि","as far as the well of the throat"]],"lit":"It goes up obliquely to Sakha and downwards to the well of the throat. In another three years, it occupies Brahmarandhra and stops there without doubt. Crosswise it goes up to the top of the head and downwards to the well of the throat.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.37","title":"","sa":["शनैः शनैर्मस्तकाच्च महावज्रकपाटभित् । पूर्वं बीजयुता विद्या ह्याख्याता यतिदुर्लभा"],"iast":["śanaiḥ śanairmastakācca mahāvajrakapāṭabhit | pūrvaṃ bījayutā vidyā hyākhyātā yatidurlabhā"],"words":[["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"],["śanairmastakācca","शनैर्मस्तकाच्च","[?]"],["mahāvajrakapāṭabhit","महावज्रकपाटभित्","opener of the great adamantine door"],["pūrvaṃ","पूर्वं","previously / formerly"],["bījayutā","बीजयुता","[?]"],["vidyā","विद्या","knowledge / science / vidyā"],["hyākhyātā","ह्याख्याता","[?]"],["yatidurlabhā","यतिदुर्लभा","[?]"]],"lit":"Gradually it opens the great adamantine door in the head. The rare science (of Khechari) Bija has been explained before.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.38","title":"","sa":["तस्याः षडङ्गं कुर्वीत तया षट्स्वरभिन्नया । कुर्यादेवं करन्यासं सर्वसिद्ध्यादिहेतवे"],"iast":["tasyāḥ ṣaḍaṅgaṃ kurvīta tayā ṣaṭsvarabhinnayā | kuryādevaṃ karanyāsaṃ sarvasiddhyādihetave"],"words":[["tasyāḥ","तस्याः","of her"],["ṣaḍaṅgaṃ","षडङ्गं","[?]"],["kurvīta","कुर्वीत","[?]"],["tayā","तया","[?]"],["ṣaṭsvarabhinnayā","षट्स्वरभिन्नया","differentiated by six tones"],["kuryādevaṃ","कुर्यादेवं","[?]"],["karanyāsaṃ","करन्यासं","[?]"],["sarvasiddhyādihetave","सर्वसिद्ध्यादिहेतवे","[?]"]],"lit":"One should perform the six Angas (parts) of this Mantra by pronouncing it in six different intonations. One should do this in order to attain all the Siddhis;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.39","title":"","sa":["शनैरेवं प्रकर्तव्यमभ्यासं युगपन्नहि । युगपद्वर्तते यस्य शरीरं विलयं व्रजेत्"],"iast":["śanairevaṃ prakartavyamabhyāsaṃ yugapannahi | yugapadvartate yasya śarīraṃ vilayaṃ vrajet"],"words":[["śanairevaṃ","शनैरेवं","[?]"],["prakartavyamabhyāsaṃ","प्रकर्तव्यमभ्यासं","[?]"],["yugapannahi","युगपन्नहि","[?]"],["yugapadvartate","युगपद्वर्तते","[?]"],["yasya","यस्य","[?]"],["śarīraṃ","शरीरं","body (acc.)"],["vilayaṃ","विलयं","[?]"],["vrajet","व्रजेत्","should go / proceeds"]],"lit":"And this Karanyasam should be done gradually and not all at a time, since the body of one who does it all at once will soon decay.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.40 (Aiyar §40-41(a))","title":"","sa":["तस्माच्छनैः शनैः कार्यमभ्यासं मुनिपुङ्गव । यदा च बाह्यमार्गेण जिह्वा ब्रह्मबिलं व्रजेत्"],"iast":["tasmācchanaiḥ śanaiḥ kāryamabhyāsaṃ munipuṅgava | yadā ca bāhyamārgeṇa jihvā brahmabilaṃ vrajet"],"words":[["tasmācchanaiḥ","तस्माच्छनैः","[?]"],["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"],["kāryamabhyāsaṃ","कार्यमभ्यासं","should-be-done practice"],["munipuṅgava","मुनिपुङ्गव","O bull among sages"],["yadā","यदा","when"],["ca","च","and"],["bāhyamārgeṇa","बाह्यमार्गेण","[?]"],["jihvā","जिह्वा","tongue"],["brahmabilaṃ","ब्रह्मबिलं","[?]"],["vrajet","व्रजेत्","should go / proceeds"]],"lit":"Therefore it should be practised, O best of sages, little by little. When the tongue goes to the Brahmarandhra through the outer path, then one should place the tongue after moving the bolt of Brahma which cannot be mastered by the Devas.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.41 (Aiyar §40-41(a))","title":"","sa":["तदा ब्रह्मार्गलं ब्रह्मन्दुर्भेद्यं त्रिदशैरपि । अङ्गुल्यग्रेण संघृष्य जिह्वामात्रं निवेशयेत्"],"iast":["tadā brahmārgalaṃ brahmandurbhedyaṃ tridaśairapi | aṅgulyagreṇa saṃghṛṣya jihvāmātraṃ niveśayet"],"words":[["tadā","तदा","then / at that time"],["brahmārgalaṃ","ब्रह्मार्गलं","Brahma-bolt"],["brahmandurbhedyaṃ","ब्रह्मन्दुर्भेद्यं","[?]"],["tridaśairapi","त्रिदशैरपि","even by the gods (Tridashas)"],["aṅgulyagreṇa","अङ्गुल्यग्रेण","with the tip of the finger"],["saṃghṛṣya","संघृष्य","[?]"],["jihvāmātraṃ","जिह्वामात्रं","merely the tongue"],["niveśayet","निवेशयेत्","should place inside"]],"lit":"Therefore it should be practised, O best of sages, little by little. When the tongue goes to the Brahmarandhra through the outer path, then one should place the tongue after moving the bolt of Brahma which cannot be mastered by the Devas.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.42 (Aiyar §41(b)-42)","title":"","sa":["एवं वर्षत्रयं कृत्वा ब्रह्मद्वारं प्रविश्यति । ब्रह्मद्वारे प्रविष्टे तु सम्यङ्मथनमाचरेत्"],"iast":["evaṃ varṣatrayaṃ kṛtvā brahmadvāraṃ praviśyati | brahmadvāre praviṣṭe tu samyaṅmathanamācaret"],"words":[["evaṃ","एवं","thus"],["varṣatrayaṃ","वर्षत्रयं","three years"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["brahmadvāraṃ","ब्रह्मद्वारं","Brahma-door"],["praviśyati","प्रविश्यति","enters"],["brahmadvāre","ब्रह्मद्वारे","at the Brahma-door"],["praviṣṭe","प्रविष्टे","having entered"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["samyaṅmathanamācaret","सम्यङ्मथनमाचरेत्","should well perform churning"]],"lit":"On doing this for three years with the point of linger, he should make the tongue enter within; then it enters Brahmadvara (or hole). On entering the Brahmadvara, one should practise Mathana (churning) well.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.43","title":"","sa":["मथनेन विना केचित्साधयन्ति विपश्चितः । खेचरीमन्त्रसिद्धस्य सिध्यते मथनं विना"],"iast":["mathanena vinā kecitsādhayanti vipaścitaḥ | khecarīmantrasiddhasya sidhyate mathanaṃ vinā"],"words":[["mathanena","मथनेन","by churning"],["vinā","विना","without"],["kecitsādhayanti","केचित्साधयन्ति","[?]"],["vipaścitaḥ","विपश्चितः","the discerning"],["khecarīmantrasiddhasya","खेचरीमन्त्रसिद्धस्य","of one perfected in the Khechari-mantra"],["sidhyate","सिध्यते","is being accomplished"],["mathanaṃ","मथनं","churning (acc./nom.)"],["vinā","विना","without"]],"lit":"Some intelligent men attain Siddhi even without Mathana. One who is versed in Khechari Mantra accomplishes it without Mathana.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.44 (Aiyar §44-46(a))","title":"","sa":["जपं च मथनं चैव कृत्वा शीघ्रं फलं लभेत् । स्वर्णजां रौप्यजां वापि लोहजां वा शलाकिकाम्"],"iast":["japaṃ ca mathanaṃ caiva kṛtvā śīghraṃ phalaṃ labhet | svarṇajāṃ raupyajāṃ vāpi lohajāṃ vā śalākikām"],"words":[["japaṃ","जपं","repetition (acc.)"],["ca","च","and"],["mathanaṃ","मथनं","churning (acc./nom.)"],["caiva","चैव","and + iva (like)"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["śīghraṃ","शीघ्रं","quickly"],["phalaṃ","फलं","[?]"],["labhet","लभेत्","should obtain"],["svarṇajāṃ","स्वर्णजां","golden (f. acc.)"],["raupyajāṃ","रौप्यजां","silvery (f. acc.)"],["vāpi","वापि","or also"],["lohajāṃ","लोहजां","iron (f. acc.)"],["vā","वा","or"],["śalākikām","शलाकिकाम्","a small rod (acc.)"]],"lit":"By doing the Japa and Mathana, one reaps the fruits soon. By connecting a wire made of gold, silver or iron with the nostrils by means of a thread soaked in milk, one should restrain his breath in his heart and seated in a convenient posture with his eyes concentrated between his eyebrows, he should perform Mathana slowly.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.45 (Aiyar §44-46(a))","title":"","sa":["नियोज्य नासिकारन्ध्रं दुग्धसिक्तेन तन्तुना । प्राणान्निरुध्य हृदये सुखमासनमात्मनः"],"iast":["niyojya nāsikārandhraṃ dugdhasiktena tantunā | prāṇānnirudhya hṛdaye sukhamāsanamātmanaḥ"],"words":[["niyojya","नियोज्य","[?]"],["nāsikārandhraṃ","नासिकारन्ध्रं","nostril (acc.)"],["dugdhasiktena","दुग्धसिक्तेन","drenched in milk"],["tantunā","तन्तुना","by a thread"],["prāṇānnirudhya","प्राणान्निरुध्य","[?]"],["hṛdaye","हृदये","[?]"],["sukhamāsanamātmanaḥ","सुखमासनमात्मनः","[?]"]],"lit":"By doing the Japa and Mathana, one reaps the fruits soon. By connecting a wire made of gold, silver or iron with the nostrils by means of a thread soaked in milk, one should restrain his breath in his heart and seated in a convenient posture with his eyes concentrated between his eyebrows, he should perform Mathana slowly.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.46 (Aiyar §44-46(a))","title":"","sa":["शनैः सुमथनं कुर्याद्भ्रूमध्ये न्यस्य चक्षुषी । षण्मासं मथनावस्था भावेनैव प्रजायते"],"iast":["śanaiḥ sumathanaṃ kuryādbhrūmadhye nyasya cakṣuṣī | ṣaṇmāsaṃ mathanāvasthā bhāvenaiva prajāyate"],"words":[["śanaiḥ","शनैः","slowly"],["sumathanaṃ","सुमथनं","[?]"],["kuryādbhrūmadhye","कुर्याद्भ्रूमध्ये","[?]"],["nyasya","न्यस्य","[?]"],["cakṣuṣī","चक्षुषी","[?]"],["ṣaṇmāsaṃ","षण्मासं","six months (acc.)"],["mathanāvasthā","मथनावस्था","the state of churning"],["bhāvenaiva","भावेनैव","by the state alone"],["prajāyate","प्रजायते","[?]"]],"lit":"By doing the Japa and Mathana, one reaps the fruits soon. By connecting a wire made of gold, silver or iron with the nostrils by means of a thread soaked in milk, one should restrain his breath in his heart and seated in a convenient posture with his eyes concentrated between his eyebrows, he should perform Mathana slowly.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.47 (Aiyar §46(b)-47)","title":"","sa":["यथा सुषुप्तिर्बालानां यथा भावस्तथा भवेत् । न सदा मथनं शस्तं मासे मासे समाचरेत्"],"iast":["yathā suṣuptirbālānāṃ yathā bhāvastathā bhavet | na sadā mathanaṃ śastaṃ māse māse samācaret"],"words":[["yathā","यथा","as / just as"],["suṣuptirbālānāṃ","सुषुप्तिर्बालानां","[?]"],["yathā","यथा","as / just as"],["bhāvastathā","भावस्तथा","[?]"],["bhavet","भवेत्","becomes / would be"],["na","न","not"],["sadā","सदा","always"],["mathanaṃ","मथनं","churning (acc./nom.)"],["śastaṃ","शस्तं","[?]"],["māse","मासे","in a month"],["māse","मासे","in a month"],["samācaret","समाचरेत्","should perform"]],"lit":"In six months, the state of Mathana becomes natural like sleep in Children. And it is not advisable to do Mathana always. It should be done (once) only in every month.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.48","title":"","sa":["सदा रसनया योगी मार्गं न परिसंक्रमेत् । एवं द्वादशवर्षान्ते संसिद्धिर्भवति ध्रुवा"],"iast":["sadā rasanayā yogī mārgaṃ na parisaṃkramet | evaṃ dvādaśavarṣānte saṃsiddhirbhavati dhruvā"],"words":[["sadā","सदा","always"],["rasanayā","रसनया","by the tongue"],["yogī","योगी","yogin"],["mārgaṃ","मार्गं","[?]"],["na","न","not"],["parisaṃkramet","परिसंक्रमेत्","[?]"],["evaṃ","एवं","thus"],["dvādaśavarṣānte","द्वादशवर्षान्ते","after twelve years"],["saṃsiddhirbhavati","संसिद्धिर्भवति","[?]"],["dhruvā","ध्रुवा","[?]"]],"lit":"A Yogin should not revolve his tongue in the path. After doing this for twelve years, Siddhi is surely obtained.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"2.49","title":"","sa":["शरीरे सकलं विश्वं पश्यत्यात्माविभेदतः । ब्रह्माण्डोऽयं महामार्गो राजदन्तोर्ध्वकुण्डली"],"iast":["śarīre sakalaṃ viśvaṃ paśyatyātmāvibhedataḥ | brahmāṇḍo'yaṃ mahāmārgo rājadantordhvakuṇḍalī"],"words":[["śarīre","शरीरे","[?]"],["sakalaṃ","सकलं","entire / all (n.)"],["viśvaṃ","विश्वं","[?]"],["paśyatyātmāvibhedataḥ","पश्यत्यात्माविभेदतः","[?]"],["brahmāṇḍo'yaṃ","ब्रह्माण्डोऽयं","[?]"],["mahāmārgo","महामार्गो","[?]"],["rājadantordhvakuṇḍalī","राजदन्तोर्ध्वकुण्डली","[?]"]],"lit":"Then he sees the whole universe in his body as not being different from Atman. This path of the Urdhva-Kundalini (higher Kundalini), O chief of Kings, conquers the macrocosm.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]}]},{"t":"Chapter II · Practical observations — Chapter II","u":[{"ref":"Khecarī as vidyā, not merely mudrā","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Verse II.5 is the most-quoted in this chapter: 'practice (abhyāsa) and the meeting (melana) are not achieved simultaneously.' The Upaniṣad treats Khecarī as a complete vidyā with two limbs — the physical practice (tongue-lengthening) and the mantra-knowledge (the bīja and its activation). The Bihar School commentary stresses that the physical practice without the bīja yields the outer form without the inner result; verses II.42–43 corroborate this directly."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"The tongue-lengthening procedure","title":"verses 28–36","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The procedure has four explicit milestones:<br>  • Day 1–7: cut the frenum 'the breadth of a hair' weekly under guru instruction.<br>  • Months 1–6: continue weekly cuts; the bandha at the root of the tongue dissolves.<br>  • Months 6–12: daily milking with the head wrapped in cloth; tongue reaches between the eyebrows.<br>  • Years 1–3: tongue reaches the chin-root; then the hairline; then the brahma-randhra.<br>The verses are remarkable for their surgical specificity. The Bihar School and modern teachers almost universally counsel a non-cutting alternative — sustained milking and stretching with the fingers — and report that the soft palate / uvula seal alone is sufficient for most practitioners."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Why warnings cluster here","title":"verses 13, 14, 39, 48","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["'You should not reveal it to others' (II.13); 'this should be protected with all one's efforts' (II.14); 'the body of one who does it all at once will soon decay' (II.39); 'a yogin should not revolve his tongue in the path' (II.48). These four are the densest cluster of dissuasion-language in the Yoga-Upaniṣads. The tradition reads them as a single instruction: gradualism + guru + secrecy + single-pointedness. The Satyananda lineage adds a contemporary gloss — that without these, mathana (the churning of verse II.42) generates heat the body cannot dissipate."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"The phenomenological pay-off","title":"verse 49","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["'Then he sees the entire universe in his body, not different from the Self.' This is the Upaniṣad's own statement of what Khecarī produces — a non-dual perception in which the macrocosm is contained in the microcosm. The Adyar commentary connects this to the broader Yoga-Upaniṣad doctrine that the body (piṇḍa) and the cosmos (brahmāṇḍa) are isomorphic (compare I.81)."],"kind":"note"}]},{"t":"Chapter III — Melana, the Six Cakras, and Liberation","u":[{"ref":"Chapter III","title":"Melana, the Six Cakras, and Liberation","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["35 verses","Chapter III gives the Melana-mantra (HRĪṂ BHAṂ SAṂ PAṂ PHAṂ SAṂ KṢAṂ) and ties the lunar calendar to its installation (1–2). It names the six cakras and their locations (9–11), prescribes drawing prāṇa upward into the Sukha-maṇḍala — the bliss-sphere, Sahasrāra (12–13) — and then moves into the metaphysics of the four levels of speech (Parā, Paśyantī, Madhyamā, Vaikharī — 18–19), the three states of the individual (Viśva, Taijasa, Prājña) and their cosmic counterparts (Virāṭ, Hiraṇyagarbha, Īśvara — 21–23). It closes with the description of the Self as thumb-sized, smokeless flame within (26), the path from waking through deep sleep to the jīvanmukta (27–33), and finally the Videha-mukti state, which is described in the closing verse as the imperishable, soundless, touchless, formless, deathless, beginning- and end-less Reality."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Visual representation","title":"six cakras with mantra associations","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["<pre>\n        SAHASRĀRA  (1000-petal lotus, abode of Śiva)\n              ✦\n              │\n        ─── ĀJÑĀ ───   ← between eyebrows (Rudra-granthi)\n              │\n        ─ VIŚUDDHA ─   ← throat\n              │\n        ─ ANĀHATA ──   ← heart (Viṣṇu-granthi)\n              │\n        ─ MAṆIPŪRA ─   ← navel\n              │\n        SVĀDHIṢṬHĀNA   ← genital region\n              │\n        ─ MŪLĀDHĀRA ─  ← perineum (Brahma-granthi)\n              ◯\n        Kuṇḍalinī coiled 3½ times\n\n   ┌──────┬──────┬──────┐\n   │ IḌĀ  │SUṢUMNĀ│ PIṄGALA │\n   │(L)   │(centre) │ (R)   │\n   │cool  │ fire    │ hot   │\n   │lunar │ Brahma- │ solar │\n   │      │ nāḍī    │       │\n   └──────┴──────┴──────┘</pre>"],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"3.1","title":"","sa":["मेलनमनुः । ह्रीं भं सं पं फं सं क्षम् । पद्मज उवाच । अमावास्या च प्रतिपत्पौर्णमासी च शङ्कर । अस्याः का वर्ण्यते संज्ञा एतदाख्याहि तत्त्वतः"],"iast":["melanamanuḥ | hrīṃ bhaṃ saṃ paṃ phaṃ saṃ kṣam | padmaja uvāca | amāvāsyā ca pratipatpaurṇamāsī ca śaṅkara | asyāḥ kā varṇyate saṃjñā etadākhyāhi tattvataḥ"],"words":[["melanamanuḥ","मेलनमनुः","Melana-mantra"],["hrīṃ","ह्रीं","[?]"],["bhaṃ","भं","[?]"],["saṃ","सं","well / together (prefix)"],["paṃ","पं","[?]"],["phaṃ","फं","[?]"],["saṃ","सं","well / together (prefix)"],["kṣam","क्षम्","[?]"],["padmaja","पद्मज","lotus-born (Brahmā)"],["uvāca","उवाच","said"],["amāvāsyā","अमावास्या","new-moon day"],["ca","च","and"],["pratipatpaurṇamāsī","प्रतिपत्पौर्णमासी","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["śaṅkara","शङ्कर","O Shankara"],["asyāḥ","अस्याः","[?]"],["kā","का","[?]"],["varṇyate","वर्ण्यते","[?]"],["saṃjñā","संज्ञा","[?]"],["etadākhyāhi","एतदाख्याहि","[?]"],["tattvataḥ","तत्त्वतः","in truth"]],"lit":"Melana-Mantra: Hrim, Bham, Sam, Pam, Pham, Sam, Ksham. The lotus-bom (Brahma) said: “O Shankara, (among) new moon (the first day of the lunar fortnight) and full moon, which is spoken of as its (mantra’s) sign ?","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.2","title":"","sa":["प्रतिपद्दिनतोऽकाले अमावास्या तथैव च । पौर्णमास्यां स्थिरीकुर्यात्स च पन्था हि नान्यथा"],"iast":["pratipaddinato'kāle amāvāsyā tathaiva ca | paurṇamāsyāṃ sthirīkuryātsa ca panthā hi nānyathā"],"words":[["pratipaddinato'kāle","प्रतिपद्दिनतोऽकाले","[?]"],["amāvāsyā","अमावास्या","new-moon day"],["tathaiva","तथैव","in the same way"],["ca","च","and"],["paurṇamāsyāṃ","पौर्णमास्यां","on the full moon"],["sthirīkuryātsa","स्थिरीकुर्यात्स","should make him firm"],["ca","च","and"],["panthā","पन्था","path"],["hi","हि","for / indeed"],["nānyathā","नान्यथा","not otherwise"]],"lit":"In the first day of lunar fortnight and during new moon and full moon (days), it should be made firm and there is no other way (or time).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.3","title":"","sa":["कामेन विषयाकाङ्क्षी विषयात्काममोहितः । द्वावेव सन्त्यजेन्नित्यं निरञ्जनमुपाश्रयेत्"],"iast":["kāmena viṣayākāṅkṣī viṣayātkāmamohitaḥ | dvāveva santyajennityaṃ nirañjanamupāśrayet"],"words":[["kāmena","कामेन","by desire"],["viṣayākāṅkṣī","विषयाकाङ्क्षी","object-desiring"],["viṣayātkāmamohitaḥ","विषयात्काममोहितः","[?]"],["dvāveva","द्वावेव","[?]"],["santyajennityaṃ","सन्त्यजेन्नित्यं","should always abandon"],["nirañjanamupāśrayet","निरञ्जनमुपाश्रयेत्","should resort to the Stainless"]],"lit":"A man longs for an object through passion and is infatuated with passion for objects. One should always leave these two and seek the Niranjana (stainless).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.4 (Aiyar §4-5)","title":"","sa":["अपरं सन्त्यजेत्सर्वं यदिच्छेदात्मनो हितम् । शक्तिमध्ये मनः कृत्वा मनः शक्तेश्च मध्यगम्"],"iast":["aparaṃ santyajetsarvaṃ yadicchedātmano hitam | śaktimadhye manaḥ kṛtvā manaḥ śakteśca madhyagam"],"words":[["aparaṃ","अपरं","[?]"],["santyajetsarvaṃ","सन्त्यजेत्सर्वं","[?]"],["yadicchedātmano","यदिच्छेदात्मनो","[?]"],["hitam","हितम्","[?]"],["śaktimadhye","शक्तिमध्ये","in the midst of Shakti"],["manaḥ","मनः","mind (manas, nom./acc.)"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["manaḥ","मनः","mind (manas, nom./acc.)"],["śakteśca","शक्तेश्च","of Shakti + cha (and)"],["madhyagam","मध्यगम्","going through the middle"]],"lit":"He should abandon everything else which he thinks is favourable to himself. Keeping the Manas in the midst of Sakti and Sakti in the midst of Manas, one should look into Manas by means of Manas. Then he leaves even the highest stage. Manas alone is the Bindu, the cause of creation and preservation.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.5 (Aiyar §4-5)","title":"","sa":["मनसा मन आलोक्य तत्त्यजेत्परमं पदम् । मन एव हि बिन्दुश्च उत्पत्तिस्थितिकारणम्"],"iast":["manasā mana ālokya tattyajetparamaṃ padam | mana eva hi binduśca utpattisthitikāraṇam"],"words":[["manasā","मनसा","by the mind"],["mana","मन","mind (= manaH)"],["ālokya","आलोक्य","[?]"],["tattyajetparamaṃ","तत्त्यजेत्परमं","[?]"],["padam","पदम्","[?]"],["mana","मन","mind (= manaH)"],["eva","एव","only / verily"],["hi","हि","for / indeed"],["binduśca","बिन्दुश्च","and bindu"],["utpattisthitikāraṇam","उत्पत्तिस्थितिकारणम्","[?]"]],"lit":"He should abandon everything else which he thinks is favourable to himself. Keeping the Manas in the midst of Sakti and Sakti in the midst of Manas, one should look into Manas by means of Manas. Then he leaves even the highest stage. Manas alone is the Bindu, the cause of creation and preservation.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.6","title":"","sa":["मनसोत्पद्यते बिन्दुर्यथा क्षीरं घृतात्मकम् । न च बन्धनमध्यस्थं तद्वै कारणमानसम्"],"iast":["manasotpadyate binduryathā kṣīraṃ ghṛtātmakam | na ca bandhanamadhyasthaṃ tadvai kāraṇamānasam"],"words":[["manasotpadyate","मनसोत्पद्यते","is produced from the mind"],["binduryathā","बिन्दुर्यथा","[?]"],["kṣīraṃ","क्षीरं","[?]"],["ghṛtātmakam","घृतात्मकम्","[?]"],["na","न","not"],["ca","च","and"],["bandhanamadhyasthaṃ","बन्धनमध्यस्थं","[?]"],["tadvai","तद्वै","that / it + vai (indeed)"],["kāraṇamānasam","कारणमानसम्","the cause is mental"]],"lit":"It is only through Manas that Bindu is produced, like the curd from milk. The organs of Manas is not that which is situated in the middle of Bandhana.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.7 (Aiyar §7-8(a))","title":"","sa":["चन्द्रार्कमध्यमा शक्तिर्यत्रस्था तत्र बन्धनम् । ज्ञात्वा सुषुम्नां तद्भेदं कृत्वा वायुं च मध्यगम्"],"iast":["candrārkamadhyamā śaktiryatrasthā tatra bandhanam | jñātvā suṣumnāṃ tadbhedaṃ kṛtvā vāyuṃ ca madhyagam"],"words":[["candrārkamadhyamā","चन्द्रार्कमध्यमा","[?]"],["śaktiryatrasthā","शक्तिर्यत्रस्था","[?]"],["tatra","तत्र","there"],["bandhanam","बन्धनम्","[?]"],["jñātvā","ज्ञात्वा","having known"],["suṣumnāṃ","सुषुम्नां","Sushumna (acc.)"],["tadbhedaṃ","तद्भेदं","[?]"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["vāyuṃ","वायुं","wind (acc.)"],["ca","च","and"],["madhyagam","मध्यगम्","going through the middle"]],"lit":"Bandhana is there where Sakti is between the sun and moon. Having known Susumna and its Bheda (piercing) and making the Vayu go in the middle, one should stand in the seat of Bindu and close the nostrils.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.8 (Aiyar §7-8(a))","title":"","sa":["स्थित्वासौ बैन्दवस्थाने घ्राणरन्ध्रे निरोधयेत् । वायुं बिन्दुं समाख्यातं सत्त्वं प्रकृतिमेव च"],"iast":["sthitvāsau baindavasthāne ghrāṇarandhre nirodhayet | vāyuṃ binduṃ samākhyātaṃ sattvaṃ prakṛtimeva ca"],"words":[["sthitvāsau","स्थित्वासौ","[?]"],["baindavasthāne","बैन्दवस्थाने","in the place of the bindu"],["ghrāṇarandhre","घ्राणरन्ध्रे","in the nostril"],["nirodhayet","निरोधयेत्","should restrain"],["vāyuṃ","वायुं","wind (acc.)"],["binduṃ","बिन्दुं","bindu (acc.)"],["samākhyātaṃ","समाख्यातं","[?]"],["sattvaṃ","सत्त्वं","[?]"],["prakṛtimeva","प्रकृतिमेव","[?]"],["ca","च","and"]],"lit":"Bandhana is there where Sakti is between the sun and moon. Having known Susumna and its Bheda (piercing) and making the Vayu go in the middle, one should stand in the seat of Bindu and close the nostrils.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.9 (Aiyar §8(b)-9(a))","title":"","sa":["षट् चक्राणि परिज्ञात्वा प्रविशेत्सुखमण्डलम् । मूलाधारं स्वाधिष्ठानं मणिपूरं तृतीयकम्"],"iast":["ṣaṭ cakrāṇi parijñātvā praviśetsukhamaṇḍalam | mūlādhāraṃ svādhiṣṭhānaṃ maṇipūraṃ tṛtīyakam"],"words":[["ṣaṭ","षट्","six"],["cakrāṇi","चक्राणि","chakras (n.pl.)"],["parijñātvā","परिज्ञात्वा","having well known"],["praviśetsukhamaṇḍalam","प्रविशेत्सुखमण्डलम्","should enter the bliss-sphere"],["mūlādhāraṃ","मूलाधारं","Muladhara (acc.)"],["svādhiṣṭhānaṃ","स्वाधिष्ठानं","Svadhisthana (acc.)"],["maṇipūraṃ","मणिपूरं","Manipura (acc.)"],["tṛtīyakam","तृतीयकम्","[?]"]],"lit":"Having known Vayu, the above-mentioned Bindu and the Sattva-Prakriti as well as the six Chakras, one should enter the Sukha-Mandala (viz., the Sahasrara or pineal gland, the sphere of happiness).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.10 (Aiyar §9(b)-11)","title":"","sa":["अनाहतं विशुद्धं च आज्ञाचक्रं च षष्ठकम् । आधारं गुदमित्युक्तं स्वाधिष्ठानं तु लैङ्गिकम्"],"iast":["anāhataṃ viśuddhaṃ ca ājñācakraṃ ca ṣaṣṭhakam | ādhāraṃ gudamityuktaṃ svādhiṣṭhānaṃ tu laiṅgikam"],"words":[["anāhataṃ","अनाहतं","Anahata (acc.)"],["viśuddhaṃ","विशुद्धं","Vishuddha (acc.)"],["ca","च","and"],["ājñācakraṃ","आज्ञाचक्रं","Ajna chakra"],["ca","च","and"],["ṣaṣṭhakam","षष्ठकम्","the sixth"],["ādhāraṃ","आधारं","Adhara (acc.)"],["gudamityuktaṃ","गुदमित्युक्तं","[Adhara] is called the anus"],["svādhiṣṭhānaṃ","स्वाधिष्ठानं","Svadhisthana (acc.)"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["laiṅgikam","लैङ्गिकम्","of the generative organ"]],"lit":"There are six Chakras. Muladhara is in the anus; Svadhisthana is near the genital organ; Manipuraka is in the navel; Anahata is in the heart; Visuddhi is at the root of the neck and Ajna is in the head (between the two eyebrows).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.11 (Aiyar §9(b)-11)","title":"","sa":["मणिपूरं नाभिदेशं हृदयस्थमनाहतम् । विशुद्धिः कण्ठमूले च आज्ञाचक्रं च मस्तकम्"],"iast":["maṇipūraṃ nābhideśaṃ hṛdayasthamanāhatam | viśuddhiḥ kaṇṭhamūle ca ājñācakraṃ ca mastakam"],"words":[["maṇipūraṃ","मणिपूरं","Manipura (acc.)"],["nābhideśaṃ","नाभिदेशं","[?]"],["hṛdayasthamanāhatam","हृदयस्थमनाहतम्","Anahata seated in the heart"],["viśuddhiḥ","विशुद्धिः","Vishuddha (nom.)"],["kaṇṭhamūle","कण्ठमूले","at the root of the neck"],["ca","च","and"],["ājñācakraṃ","आज्ञाचक्रं","Ajna chakra"],["ca","च","and"],["mastakam","मस्तकम्","head (acc.)"]],"lit":"There are six Chakras. Muladhara is in the anus; Svadhisthana is near the genital organ; Manipuraka is in the navel; Anahata is in the heart; Visuddhi is at the root of the neck and Ajna is in the head (between the two eyebrows).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.12","title":"","sa":["षट् चक्राणि परिज्ञात्वा प्रविशेत्सुखमण्डले । प्रविशेद्वायुमाकृष्य तयैवोर्ध्वं नियोजयेत्"],"iast":["ṣaṭ cakrāṇi parijñātvā praviśetsukhamaṇḍale | praviśedvāyumākṛṣya tayaivordhvaṃ niyojayet"],"words":[["ṣaṭ","षट्","six"],["cakrāṇi","चक्राणि","chakras (n.pl.)"],["parijñātvā","परिज्ञात्वा","having well known"],["praviśetsukhamaṇḍale","प्रविशेत्सुखमण्डले","[?]"],["praviśedvāyumākṛṣya","प्रविशेद्वायुमाकृष्य","should enter, drawing in the wind"],["tayaivordhvaṃ","तयैवोर्ध्वं","[?]"],["niyojayet","नियोजयेत्","[?]"]],"lit":"Having known these six Mandalas (spheres), one should enter the Sukha-Mandala (pineal gland), drawing up the Vayu and should send it (Vayu) upwards.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.13","title":"","sa":["एवं समभ्यसेद्वायुं स ब्रह्माण्डमयो भवेत् । वायुं बिन्दुं तथा चक्रं चित्तं चैव समभ्यसेत्"],"iast":["evaṃ samabhyasedvāyuṃ sa brahmāṇḍamayo bhavet | vāyuṃ binduṃ tathā cakraṃ cittaṃ caiva samabhyaset"],"words":[["evaṃ","एवं","thus"],["samabhyasedvāyuṃ","समभ्यसेद्वायुं","[?]"],["sa","स","he"],["brahmāṇḍamayo","ब्रह्माण्डमयो","consisting of the macrocosm"],["bhavet","भवेत्","becomes / would be"],["vāyuṃ","वायुं","wind (acc.)"],["binduṃ","बिन्दुं","bindu (acc.)"],["tathā","तथा","so / and"],["cakraṃ","चक्रं","chakra (acc.)"],["cittaṃ","चित्तं","mind-stuff (acc./nom.)"],["caiva","चैव","and + iva (like)"],["samabhyaset","समभ्यसेत्","should well practise"]],"lit":"He who practises thus (the control of) Vayu becomes one with Brahmanda (the macrocosm). He should practise (or master) Vayu, Bindu, Chitta and Chakra.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.14 (Aiyar §14-15)","title":"","sa":["समाधिमेकेन समममृतं यान्ति योगिनः । यथाग्निर्दारुमध्यस्थो नोत्तिष्ठेन्मथनं विना"],"iast":["samādhimekena samamamṛtaṃ yānti yoginaḥ | yathāgnirdārumadhyastho nottiṣṭhenmathanaṃ vinā"],"words":[["samādhimekena","समाधिमेकेन","[?]"],["samamamṛtaṃ","समममृतं","[?]"],["yānti","यान्ति","[?]"],["yoginaḥ","योगिनः","[?]"],["yathāgnirdārumadhyastho","यथाग्निर्दारुमध्यस्थो","[?]"],["nottiṣṭhenmathanaṃ","नोत्तिष्ठेन्मथनं","[?]"],["vinā","विना","without"]],"lit":"Yogins attain the nectar of equality through Samadhi alone. Just as the fire latent in (Sacrificial) wood does not appear without churning, so the lamp of wisdom does not arise without the Abhyasa Yoga (or practice of Yoga). The fire placed in a vessel does not give light outside.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.15 (Aiyar §14-15)","title":"","sa":["विना चाभ्यासयोगेन ज्ञानदीपस्तथा न हि । घटमध्यगतो दीपो बाह्ये नैव प्रकाशते"],"iast":["vinā cābhyāsayogena jñānadīpastathā na hi | ghaṭamadhyagato dīpo bāhye naiva prakāśate"],"words":[["vinā","विना","without"],["cābhyāsayogena","चाभ्यासयोगेन","[?]"],["jñānadīpastathā","ज्ञानदीपस्तथा","the lamp of knowledge likewise"],["na","न","not"],["hi","हि","for / indeed"],["ghaṭamadhyagato","घटमध्यगतो","[?]"],["dīpo","दीपो","lamp"],["bāhye","बाह्ये","[?]"],["naiva","नैव","not + iva (like)"],["prakāśate","प्रकाशते","shines / illumines"]],"lit":"Yogins attain the nectar of equality through Samadhi alone. Just as the fire latent in (Sacrificial) wood does not appear without churning, so the lamp of wisdom does not arise without the Abhyasa Yoga (or practice of Yoga). The fire placed in a vessel does not give light outside.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.16","title":"","sa":["भिन्ने तस्मिन्घटे चैव दीपज्वाला च भासते । स्वकायं घटमित्युक्तं यथा दीपो हि तत्पदम्"],"iast":["bhinne tasminghaṭe caiva dīpajvālā ca bhāsate | svakāyaṃ ghaṭamityuktaṃ yathā dīpo hi tatpadam"],"words":[["bhinne","भिन्ने","[?]"],["tasminghaṭe","तस्मिन्घटे","[?]"],["caiva","चैव","and + iva (like)"],["dīpajvālā","दीपज्वाला","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["bhāsate","भासते","[?]"],["svakāyaṃ","स्वकायं","[?]"],["ghaṭamityuktaṃ","घटमित्युक्तं","is called the pot"],["yathā","यथा","as / just as"],["dīpo","दीपो","lamp"],["hi","हि","for / indeed"],["tatpadam","तत्पदम्","that state"]],"lit":"When the vessel is broken, its light appears without. One’s body is spoken of as the vessel and the seat of ‘That’ is the fire (or light) within;","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.17 (Aiyar §17-18(a))","title":"","sa":["गुरुवाक्यसमाभिन्ने ब्रह्मज्ञानं स्फुटीभवेत् । कर्णधारं गुरुं प्राप्य कृत्वा सूक्ष्मं तरन्ति च"],"iast":["guruvākyasamābhinne brahmajñānaṃ sphuṭībhavet | karṇadhāraṃ guruṃ prāpya kṛtvā sūkṣmaṃ taranti ca"],"words":[["guruvākyasamābhinne","गुरुवाक्यसमाभिन्ने","when [the body] is split by the guru's word"],["brahmajñānaṃ","ब्रह्मज्ञानं","Brahma-knowledge"],["sphuṭībhavet","स्फुटीभवेत्","would be manifest"],["karṇadhāraṃ","कर्णधारं","[?]"],["guruṃ","गुरुं","guru (acc.)"],["prāpya","प्राप्य","[?]"],["kṛtvā","कृत्वा","having done"],["sūkṣmaṃ","सूक्ष्मं","[?]"],["taranti","तरन्ति","they cross"],["ca","च","and"]],"lit":"And when it (the body) is broken through the words of a Guru, the light of Brahma Jnana becomes resplendent. With the Gum as the helmsman, one crosses the subtle body and the ocean of Samsara through the affinities of practice.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.18 (Aiyar §17-18(a))","title":"","sa":["अभ्यासवासनाशक्त्या तरन्ति भवसागरम् । परायामङ्कुरीभूय पश्यन्तां द्विदलीकृता"],"iast":["abhyāsavāsanāśaktyā taranti bhavasāgaram | parāyāmaṅkurībhūya paśyantāṃ dvidalīkṛtā"],"words":[["abhyāsavāsanāśaktyā","अभ्यासवासनाशक्त्या","by the power of latent-tendencies-of-practice"],["taranti","तरन्ति","they cross"],["bhavasāgaram","भवसागरम्","[?]"],["parāyāmaṅkurībhūya","परायामङ्कुरीभूय","[?]"],["paśyantāṃ","पश्यन्तां","Pashyanti (acc./f.)"],["dvidalīkṛtā","द्विदलीकृता","[?]"]],"lit":"And when it (the body) is broken through the words of a Guru, the light of Brahma Jnana becomes resplendent. With the Gum as the helmsman, one crosses the subtle body and the ocean of Samsara through the affinities of practice.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.19 (Aiyar §18(b)-19)","title":"","sa":["मध्यमायां मुकुलिता वैखर्यां विकसीकृता । पूर्वं यथोदिता या वाग्विलोमेनास्तगा भवेत्"],"iast":["madhyamāyāṃ mukulitā vaikharyāṃ vikasīkṛtā | pūrvaṃ yathoditā yā vāgvilomenāstagā bhavet"],"words":[["madhyamāyāṃ","मध्यमायां","in Madhyama"],["mukulitā","मुकुलिता","[?]"],["vaikharyāṃ","वैखर्यां","in Vaikhari"],["vikasīkṛtā","विकसीकृता","[?]"],["pūrvaṃ","पूर्वं","previously / formerly"],["yathoditā","यथोदिता","[?]"],["yā","या","which (f.)"],["vāgvilomenāstagā","वाग्विलोमेनास्तगा","speech reverse-going-to-rest"],["bhavet","भवेत्","becomes / would be"]],"lit":"That Vak (power of speech) which sprouts in Para, gives forth two leaves in Pashyanti; buds forth in Madhyama and blossoms in Vaikhari - that Vak which has before been described, reaches the stage of the absorption of sound, reversing the above order (viz., beginning with Vaikhari, etc.,).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.20 (Aiyar §20-21(a))","title":"","sa":["तस्या वाचः परो देवः कूटस्थो वाक्प्रबोधकः । सोऽहमस्मीति निश्चित्य यः सदा वर्तते पुमान्"],"iast":["tasyā vācaḥ paro devaḥ kūṭastho vākprabodhakaḥ | so'hamasmīti niścitya yaḥ sadā vartate pumān"],"words":[["tasyā","तस्या","of her"],["vācaḥ","वाचः","of speech"],["paro","परो","supreme (nom.)"],["devaḥ","देवः","[?]"],["kūṭastho","कूटस्थो","[?]"],["vākprabodhakaḥ","वाक्प्रबोधकः","awakener of speech"],["so'hamasmīti","सोऽहमस्मीति","[?]"],["niścitya","निश्चित्य","[?]"],["yaḥ","यः","who (m.)"],["sadā","सदा","always"],["vartate","वर्तते","[?]"],["pumān","पुमान्","[?]"]],"lit":"Whoever thinks that He who is the great lord of that Vak, who is the undifferentiated and who is the illuminator of that Vak is Self; whoever thinks over thus, is never affected by words, high or low (or good or bad).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.21 (Aiyar §20-21(a))","title":"","sa":["शब्दैरुच्चावचैर्नीचैर्भाषितोऽपि न लिप्यते । विश्वश्च तैजसश्चैव प्राज्ञश्चेति च ते त्रयः"],"iast":["śabdairuccāvacairnīcairbhāṣito'pi na lipyate | viśvaśca taijasaścaiva prājñaśceti ca te trayaḥ"],"words":[["śabdairuccāvacairnīcairbhāṣito'pi","शब्दैरुच्चावचैर्नीचैर्भाषितोऽपि","[?]"],["na","न","not"],["lipyate","लिप्यते","becomes stained"],["viśvaśca","विश्वश्च","and Vishva"],["taijasaścaiva","तैजसश्चैव","and Taijasa"],["prājñaśceti","प्राज्ञश्चेति","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["te","ते","they / those"],["trayaḥ","त्रयः","three"]],"lit":"Whoever thinks that He who is the great lord of that Vak, who is the undifferentiated and who is the illuminator of that Vak is Self; whoever thinks over thus, is never affected by words, high or low (or good or bad).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.22 (Aiyar §21(b)-23(a))","title":"","sa":["विराड्ढिरण्यगर्भश्च ईश्वरश्चेति ते त्रयः । ब्रह्माण्डं चैव पिण्डाण्डं लोका भूरादयः क्रमात्"],"iast":["virāḍḍhiraṇyagarbhaśca īśvaraśceti te trayaḥ | brahmāṇḍaṃ caiva piṇḍāṇḍaṃ lokā bhūrādayaḥ kramāt"],"words":[["virāḍḍhiraṇyagarbhaśca","विराड्ढिरण्यगर्भश्च","Virat and Hiranyagarbha"],["īśvaraśceti","ईश्वरश्चेति","and Ishvara"],["te","ते","they / those"],["trayaḥ","त्रयः","three"],["brahmāṇḍaṃ","ब्रह्माण्डं","[?]"],["caiva","चैव","and + iva (like)"],["piṇḍāṇḍaṃ","पिण्डाण्डं","[?]"],["lokā","लोका","[?]"],["bhūrādayaḥ","भूरादयः","[?]"],["kramāt","क्रमात्","[?]"]],"lit":"The three (aspects of consciousness), Vishva, Taijasa and Prajna (in man), the three Virat, Hiranyagarbha and Ishvara in the universe, the egg of the universe, the egg of man and the seven worlds - all these in turn are absorbed in Pratyagatman through the absorption of their respective Upadhis (vehicles).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.23 (Aiyar §21(b)-23(a))","title":"","sa":["स्वस्वोपाधिलयादेव लीयन्ते प्रत्यगात्मनि । अण्डं ज्ञानाग्निना तप्तं लीयते कारणैः सह"],"iast":["svasvopādhilayādeva līyante pratyagātmani | aṇḍaṃ jñānāgninā taptaṃ līyate kāraṇaiḥ saha"],"words":[["svasvopādhilayādeva","स्वस्वोपाधिलयादेव","[?]"],["līyante","लीयन्ते","[?]"],["pratyagātmani","प्रत्यगात्मनि","in the inward Self"],["aṇḍaṃ","अण्डं","[?]"],["jñānāgninā","ज्ञानाग्निना","by the fire of knowledge"],["taptaṃ","तप्तं","[?]"],["līyate","लीयते","is dissolved"],["kāraṇaiḥ","कारणैः","by the causes"],["saha","सह","together with"]],"lit":"The three (aspects of consciousness), Vishva, Taijasa and Prajna (in man), the three Virat, Hiranyagarbha and Ishvara in the universe, the egg of the universe, the egg of man and the seven worlds - all these in turn are absorbed in Pratyagatman through the absorption of their respective Upadhis (vehicles).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.24 (Aiyar §23(b)-24(a))","title":"","sa":["परमात्मनि लीनं तत्परं ब्रह्मैव जायते । ततः स्तिमितगम्भीरं न तेजो न तमस्ततम्"],"iast":["paramātmani līnaṃ tatparaṃ brahmaiva jāyate | tataḥ stimitagambhīraṃ na tejo na tamastatam"],"words":[["paramātmani","परमात्मनि","in the supreme Self"],["līnaṃ","लीनं","dissolved"],["tatparaṃ","तत्परं","[?]"],["brahmaiva","ब्रह्मैव","Brahman alone"],["jāyate","जायते","is born / arises"],["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"],["stimitagambhīraṃ","स्तिमितगम्भीरं","still and deep"],["na","न","not"],["tejo","तेजो","light (compound)"],["na","न","not"],["tamastatam","तमस्ततम्","[?]"]],"lit":"The egg being heated by the fire of Jnana is absorbed with its Karana (cause) into Paramatman (Universal Self). Then it becomes one with Para-Brahman.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.25 (Aiyar §24(b)-25)","title":"","sa":["अनाख्यमनभिव्यक्तं सत्किञ्चिदवशिष्यते । ध्यात्वा मध्यस्थमात्मानं कलशान्तरदीपवत्"],"iast":["anākhyamanabhivyaktaṃ satkiñcidavaśiṣyate | dhyātvā madhyasthamātmānaṃ kalaśāntaradīpavat"],"words":[["anākhyamanabhivyaktaṃ","अनाख्यमनभिव्यक्तं","[?]"],["satkiñcidavaśiṣyate","सत्किञ्चिदवशिष्यते","some Sat alone remains"],["dhyātvā","ध्यात्वा","having meditated"],["madhyasthamātmānaṃ","मध्यस्थमात्मानं","[?]"],["kalaśāntaradīpavat","कलशान्तरदीपवत्","[?]"]],"lit":"It is then neither steadiness nor depth, neither light nor darkness, neither describable nor distinguishable. Sat (Be-ness) alone remains. One should think of Atman as being within the body like a light in a vessel.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.26","title":"","sa":["अङ्गुष्ठमात्रमात्मानमधूमज्योतिरूपकम् । प्रकाशयन्तमन्तस्थं ध्यायेत्कूटस्थमव्ययम्"],"iast":["aṅguṣṭhamātramātmānamadhūmajyotirūpakam | prakāśayantamantasthaṃ dhyāyetkūṭasthamavyayam"],"words":[["aṅguṣṭhamātramātmānamadhūmajyotirūpakam","अङ्गुष्ठमात्रमात्मानमधूमज्योतिरूपकम्","[?]"],["prakāśayantamantasthaṃ","प्रकाशयन्तमन्तस्थं","[?]"],["dhyāyetkūṭasthamavyayam","ध्यायेत्कूटस्थमव्ययम्","should meditate on the unchanging immutable"]],"lit":"Atman is of the dimensions of a thumb, is a light without smoke and without form, is shining within (the body) and is undifferentiated and immutable.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.27 (Aiyar §27-28(a))","title":"","sa":["विज्ञानात्मा तथा देहे जाग्रत्स्वप्नसुषुप्तितः । मायया मोहितः पश्चाद्बहुजन्मान्तरे पुनः"],"iast":["vijñānātmā tathā dehe jāgratsvapnasuṣuptitaḥ | māyayā mohitaḥ paścādbahujanmāntare punaḥ"],"words":[["vijñānātmā","विज्ञानात्मा","vijñāna-self"],["tathā","तथा","so / and"],["dehe","देहे","in the body"],["jāgratsvapnasuṣuptitaḥ","जाग्रत्स्वप्नसुषुप्तितः","[?]"],["māyayā","मायया","by māyā"],["mohitaḥ","मोहितः","deluded"],["paścādbahujanmāntare","पश्चाद्बहुजन्मान्तरे","[?]"],["punaḥ","पुनः","again"]],"lit":"The Vijnana Atman that dwells in this body is deluded by Maya during the states of waking, dreaming and dreamless sleep; but after many births, owing to the effect of good Karma, it wishes to attain its own state.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.28 (Aiyar §27-28(a))","title":"","sa":["सत्कर्मपरिपाकात्तु स्वविकारं चिकीर्षति । कोऽहं कथमयं दोषः संसाराख्य उपागतः"],"iast":["satkarmaparipākāttu svavikāraṃ cikīrṣati | ko'haṃ kathamayaṃ doṣaḥ saṃsārākhya upāgataḥ"],"words":[["satkarmaparipākāttu","सत्कर्मपरिपाकात्तु","from the ripening of good karma + tu (but / indeed)"],["svavikāraṃ","स्वविकारं","[?]"],["cikīrṣati","चिकीर्षति","[?]"],["ko'haṃ","कोऽहं","[?]"],["kathamayaṃ","कथमयं","[?]"],["doṣaḥ","दोषः","humour / impurity"],["saṃsārākhya","संसाराख्य","called samsāra"],["upāgataḥ","उपागतः","[?]"]],"lit":"The Vijnana Atman that dwells in this body is deluded by Maya during the states of waking, dreaming and dreamless sleep; but after many births, owing to the effect of good Karma, it wishes to attain its own state.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.29 (Aiyar §28(b)-29(a))","title":"","sa":["जाग्रत्स्वप्ने व्यवहरन्त्सुषुप्तौ क्व गतिर्मम । इति चिन्तापरो भूत्वा स्वभासा च विशेषतः"],"iast":["jāgratsvapne vyavaharantsuṣuptau kva gatirmama | iti cintāparo bhūtvā svabhāsā ca viśeṣataḥ"],"words":[["jāgratsvapne","जाग्रत्स्वप्ने","[?]"],["vyavaharantsuṣuptau","व्यवहरन्त्सुषुप्तौ","[?]"],["kva","क्व","where?"],["gatirmama","गतिर्मम","[?]"],["iti","इति","thus / [end-quote]"],["cintāparo","चिन्तापरो","absorbed in thought (nom.)"],["bhūtvā","भूत्वा","having become"],["svabhāsā","स्वभासा","[?]"],["ca","च","and"],["viśeṣataḥ","विशेषतः","[?]"]],"lit":"Who am I ? How has this stain of mundane existence accrued to me ? What becomes in the dreamless sleep of me who am engaged in business in the waking and dreaming states ?","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.30 (Aiyar §29(b)-30)","title":"","sa":["अज्ञानात्तु चिदाभासो बहिस्तापेन तापितः । दग्धं भवत्येव तदा तूलपिण्डमिवाग्निना"],"iast":["ajñānāttu cidābhāso bahistāpena tāpitaḥ | dagdhaṃ bhavatyeva tadā tūlapiṇḍamivāgninā"],"words":[["ajñānāttu","अज्ञानात्तु","from ignorance + tu (but / indeed)"],["cidābhāso","चिदाभासो","reflection of consciousness (nom.)"],["bahistāpena","बहिस्तापेन","[?]"],["tāpitaḥ","तापितः","heated"],["dagdhaṃ","दग्धं","[?]"],["bhavatyeva","भवत्येव","[?]"],["tadā","तदा","then / at that time"],["tūlapiṇḍamivāgninā","तूलपिण्डमिवाग्निना","[?]"]],"lit":"Just as a bale of cotton is burnt by fire, so the Chidabhasa which is the result of non- wisdom, is burnt by the (wise) thoughts like the above and by its own supreme illumination. The outer burning (of body as done in the world) is no burning at all.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.31 (Aiyar §31-32)","title":"","sa":["दहरस्थः प्रत्यगात्मा नष्टे ज्ञाने ततः परम् । विततो व्याप्य विज्ञानं दहत्येव क्षणेन तु"],"iast":["daharasthaḥ pratyagātmā naṣṭe jñāne tataḥ param | vitato vyāpya vijñānaṃ dahatyeva kṣaṇena tu"],"words":[["daharasthaḥ","दहरस्थः","[?]"],["pratyagātmā","प्रत्यगात्मा","the inward Self"],["naṣṭe","नष्टे","[?]"],["jñāne","ज्ञाने","[?]"],["tataḥ","ततः","that / it (n.) (nom. sg.)"],["param","परम्","supreme / beyond"],["vitato","विततो","[?]"],["vyāpya","व्याप्य","[?]"],["vijñānaṃ","विज्ञानं","vijñāna (acc.)"],["dahatyeva","दहत्येव","[?]"],["kṣaṇena","क्षणेन","[?]"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"]],"lit":"When the worldly wisdom is destroyed, Pratyagatman that is in the Dahara (Akasa or ether of the heart) obtains Vijnana, diffusing itself everywhere and bums in an instant Jnanamaya and Manomaya (sheaths). After this, He himself shines always within, like a light within a vessel.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.32 (Aiyar §31-32)","title":"","sa":["मनोमयज्ञानमयान्सम्यग्दग्ध्वा क्रमेण तु । घटस्थदीपवच्छश्वदन्तरेव प्रकाशते"],"iast":["manomayajñānamayānsamyagdagdhvā krameṇa tu | ghaṭasthadīpavacchaśvadantareva prakāśate"],"words":[["manomayajñānamayānsamyagdagdhvā","मनोमयज्ञानमयान्सम्यग्दग्ध्वा","[?]"],["krameṇa","क्रमेण","in sequence / gradually"],["tu","तु","but / indeed"],["ghaṭasthadīpavacchaśvadantareva","घटस्थदीपवच्छश्वदन्तरेव","[?]"],["prakāśate","प्रकाशते","shines / illumines"]],"lit":"When the worldly wisdom is destroyed, Pratyagatman that is in the Dahara (Akasa or ether of the heart) obtains Vijnana, diffusing itself everywhere and bums in an instant Jnanamaya and Manomaya (sheaths). After this, He himself shines always within, like a light within a vessel.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.33","title":"","sa":["ध्यायन्नास्ते मुनिश्चैवमासुप्तेरामृतेस्तु यः । जीवन्मुक्तः स विज्ञेयः स धन्यः कृतकृत्यवान्"],"iast":["dhyāyannāste muniścaivamāsupterāmṛtestu yaḥ | jīvanmuktaḥ sa vijñeyaḥ sa dhanyaḥ kṛtakṛtyavān"],"words":[["dhyāyannāste","ध्यायन्नास्ते","remains meditating"],["muniścaivamāsupterāmṛtestu","मुनिश्चैवमासुप्तेरामृतेस्तु","[?]"],["yaḥ","यः","who (m.)"],["jīvanmuktaḥ","जीवन्मुक्तः","liberated-in-life (nom.)"],["sa","स","he"],["vijñeyaḥ","विज्ञेयः","[?]"],["sa","स","he"],["dhanyaḥ","धन्यः","[?]"],["kṛtakṛtyavān","कृतकृत्यवान्","[?]"]],"lit":"That Muni who contemplates thus till sleep and till death is to be known as a Jivanmukta. Having done what ought to be done, he is a fortunate person.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.34","title":"","sa":["जीवन्मुक्तपदं त्यक्त्वा स्वदेहे कालसात्कृते । विशत्यदेहमुक्तत्वं पवनोऽस्पन्दतामिव"],"iast":["jīvanmuktapadaṃ tyaktvā svadehe kālasātkṛte | viśatyadehamuktatvaṃ pavano'spandatāmiva"],"words":[["jīvanmuktapadaṃ","जीवन्मुक्तपदं","the state of jīvanmukta"],["tyaktvā","त्यक्त्वा","having abandoned"],["svadehe","स्वदेहे","in one's own body"],["kālasātkṛte","कालसात्कृते","given over to time"],["viśatyadehamuktatvaṃ","विशत्यदेहमुक्तत्वं","enters the bodiless-liberation"],["pavano'spandatāmiva","पवनोऽस्पन्दतामिव","[?]"]],"lit":"And having given up (even) the state of a Jivanmukta, he attains Videhamukta (emancipation in a disembodied state), after his body wears off. He attains the state, as if of moving in the air.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"3.35","title":"","sa":["अशब्दमस्पर्शमरूपमव्ययं तथारसं नित्यमगन्धवच्च यत् । अनाद्यनन्तं महतः परं ध्रुवं तदेव शिष्यत्यमलं निरामयम्"],"iast":["aśabdamasparśamarūpamavyayaṃ tathārasaṃ nityamagandhavacca yat | anādyanantaṃ mahataḥ paraṃ dhruvaṃ tadeva śiṣyatyamalaṃ nirāmayam"],"words":[["aśabdamasparśamarūpamavyayaṃ","अशब्दमस्पर्शमरूपमव्ययं","[?]"],["tathārasaṃ","तथारसं","and tasteless"],["nityamagandhavacca","नित्यमगन्धवच्च","[?]"],["yat","यत्","what (n.)"],["anādyanantaṃ","अनाद्यनन्तं","without beginning or end"],["mahataḥ","महतः","[?]"],["paraṃ","परं","supreme (acc./adv.)"],["dhruvaṃ","ध्रुवं","permanent"],["tadeva","तदेव","that / it + eva (only / verily)"],["śiṣyatyamalaṃ","शिष्यत्यमलं","[?]"],["nirāmayam","निरामयम्","decayless"]],"lit":"Then That alone remains which is soundless, touchless, formless and deathless, which is the Rasa (essence), eternal, and odourless, which has neither beginning nor end, which is greater than the great and which is permanent, stainless and decayless.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"The Melana-mantra","title":"verse 1","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["HRĪṂ BHAṂ SAṂ PAṂ PHAṂ SAṂ KṢAṂ — seven bīja-akṣaras. The exact decoding is a matter of tantric dīkṣā and is deliberately encrypted in verses II.18–20 (read in reverse, by pieces, with substitutions). The Adyar commentary supplies one reading; the Bihar and Himalayan lineages give others. The Upaniṣad itself states that the mantra can only be transmitted by a qualified guru (II.13–14, III.1–2 by implication)."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Calendar","title":"verse 2","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The mantra is to be installed (sthirīkuryāt) on three specific lunar days: pratipat (first day of the bright half), amāvāsyā (new moon), and pūrṇimā (full moon). The text says 'there is no other way' — na panthā hi nānyathā. Tantric tradition reads this as alignment with the soma-lunar current that modulates the ojas/amṛta cycle in the body."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Six cakras","title":"verses 9–11","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Mūlādhāra at the anus, Svādhiṣṭhāna near the genitals, Maṇipūra at the navel, Anāhata in the heart, Viśuddhi at the root of the neck, Ājñā in the head. Five mantra-bījas correspond to the lower five (LAṂ, VAṂ, RAṂ, YAṂ, HAṂ); the Yoga-Kuṇḍalinī Upaniṣad does not state the bījas itself — they appear in the parallel Yoga-Cūḍāmaṇi Upaniṣad (verse 66, which cross-references back to this text)."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"The four levels of speech","title":"verses 18–19","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Parā (the unmanifest source), Paśyantī (the seeing/intuitive), Madhyamā (the mental/conceptual), Vaikharī (the spoken). All practice begins at Vaikharī and reverses up through Parā — the absorption (laya) is described as 'reversing the above order'. This is the Yoga-Upaniṣad's compact statement of pratyāhāra-as-laya."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Jīvanmukta and Videhamukta","title":"verses 33–35","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Jīvanmukta: the sage who meditates thus 'until sleep, until death' — liberation while embodied. Videhamukta: 'having given up even the state of jīvanmukta', having the body worn away, attains a state 'as of moving in air'. The final verse (35) is the longest in the chapter and gives the apophatic description of the Absolute that remains: aśabdam, asparśam, arūpam, avyayam, arasam, agandhavat, anādyantam — soundless, touchless, formless, imperishable, tasteless, odourless, without beginning or end."],"kind":"note"}]},{"t":"Comparative notes from the five principal commentaries","u":[{"ref":"Comparative notes from the five principal commentaries","title":"Overview","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Below, for each chapter, are the points where the five chosen commentators either substantially agree (consensus) or visibly diverge (contested reading). Where Aiyar's English already mediates Brahma-Yogin's Sanskrit gloss, only the verbatim Aiyar reading is given; where the Adyar / Bihar / Himalayan traditions extend or contest it, those readings are paraphrased with attribution."],"kind":"note"}]},{"t":"Chapter I — disputed and consensus readings","u":[{"ref":"I.7","title":"what is 'Śakti'?","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Consensus across all five: śakti here is Kuṇḍalinī. Brahma-Yogin (via Aiyar) and Ayyaṅgār both gloss the verse as defining Kuṇḍalinī as the śakti to be raised. Satyananda and Tigunait both emphasise that this gloss preempts the later tantric multiplication of śaktis: this Upaniṣad knows one śakti for yogic purposes, and it is Kuṇḍalinī."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"I.9","title":"Sarasvatī = Aruṇdhatī?","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The text says 'Sarasvatī is no other than Aruṇdhatī.' Brahma-Yogin reads this literally — the faint companion star of Vaśiṣṭha in the Big Dipper, used in the Vedic marriage ritual; the Sarasvatī-nāḍī is being identified with something so subtle it can only be 'pointed at' indirectly. Ayyaṅgār preserves this. Satyananda offers a different anatomical correlate — the Sarasvatī-nāḍī as the channel running parallel to Suṣumnā on the left, connecting the throat to the navel — and treats the Aruṇdhatī line as metaphor. Tigunait stays close to Brahma-Yogin."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"I.39","title":"Bhastrikā as granthi-bhedaka","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Aiyar and Ayyaṅgār both translate 'pierces the three granthis differentiated through the three guṇas.' The Bihar School (Satyananda) notes that this is the only kumbhaka of the four explicitly named as granthi-bhedaka, and treats Bhastrikā with its bandhas as the operative kuṇḍalinī-rousing technique of Chapter I — the prior three are preparatory."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"I.66–86","title":"the path of the ascent","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["All five commentators agree on the sequence: Mūlādhāra → piercing of Brahma-granthi (rajas) → Maṇipūra → Viṣṇu-granthi (sattva, at heart) → Anāhata → Rudra-granthi (tamas, between brows) → Sahasrāra (verses 67–69, 86). Aiyar's 'flashes at once like lightning' (vidyullekheva) for the first piercing is verbatim from Brahma-Yogin. The phenomenology in 73–80 (the novice tastes peace; Kuṇḍalinī assumes the eight forms of prakṛti and dissolves in Śiva) is among the densest in any Upaniṣad and Brahma-Yogin's Sanskrit gloss extends to several folios."],"kind":"note"}]},{"t":"Chapter II — disputed and consensus readings","u":[{"ref":"II.28–31","title":"the cutting procedure","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Aiyar and Ayyaṅgār render the procedure literally — snuhi-leaf-shaped knife, rock-salt and sea-salt rub, weekly cut for six months. Satyananda explicitly discourages the cutting in modern practice and offers a milking-only alternative; Tigunait notes that some lineages substitute a butter-and-thread milking technique that achieves the same elongation without surgery. All five agree that the procedure must not be self-administered."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"II.49","title":"'sees the whole universe in his body'","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Brahma-Yogin reads this as a phenomenological description, not a metaphor — the yogin literally has a unitive perception in which the cosmos is experienced as one's own body. Ayyaṅgār preserves this. The Bihar and Himalayan traditions both speak of this in terms of the dissolution of the subject-object distinction at the level of perception itself."],"kind":"note"}]},{"t":"Chapter III — disputed and consensus readings","u":[{"ref":"III.1","title":"decoding the Melana-mantra","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The mantra hrīṃ bhaṃ saṃ paṃ phaṃ saṃ kṣaṃ. Brahma-Yogin glosses each syllable to a deity: HRĪṂ to Kuṇḍalinī-as-Śakti; BHAṂ to bhairava; SAṂ to Sadāśiva; PAṂ to the lord of the cakras; PHAṂ to the seed of phala (fruit/result); KṢAṂ to Kṣetrajña (the field-knower). Ayyaṅgār reproduces this. The Bihar / Himalayan lineages give different decompositions tied to their initiatory traditions; the Upaniṣad's own internal reference (verses II.18–20) yields yet another decoding by reversing parts of the bīja. The text itself insists that any reading without guru-transmission is incomplete."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"III.34","title":"Videha-mukti as 'movement in air'","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["pavano 'spandatām iva — 'as if the wind became still'. Aiyar renders 'as if of moving in the air'; Ayyaṅgār 'like the wind that ceases to stir'. The ambiguity is preserved in Brahma-Yogin's gloss: the body wears away as the wind subsides, and what remains has no locus, neither here nor elsewhere. This is the Upaniṣad's terminal description of liberation (continued and amplified in the final verse)."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Colophon","title":"","sa":["इति योगकुण्डलिन्युपनिषत्समाप्ता ॥","ॐ शान्तिः शान्तिः शान्तिः ॥"],"iast":["iti yogakuṇḍalinyupaniṣat samāptā ||"],"words":[],"lit":"Thus ends the Yoga-Kuṇḍalinī Upaniṣad belonging to the Kṛṣṇa-Yajur-Veda.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]}]}]};
